ub.com/hle-mia-dt","id":114322484,"login":"hle-mia-dt","node_id":"U_kgDOBtBsNA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HuyPhat/orbit-platform/commits/8cf12bccb86578c0cc2ac1555370134985ad4699/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T07:24:27Z","email":"phathuy261089@gmail.com","name":"Lph"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T07:24:27Z","email":"phathuy261089@gmail.com","name":"Lph"},"message":"feat(infra): load harness, k6 scenario, demo traffic and CI\n\nThe load harness needs only Node and Redis so the published numbers can be\nreproduced by anyone who can run the project. It asserts zero oversells and\nzero double-allocation on every run, and CI fails the build if either is\never non-zero.\n\nMeasured: 71,640 hold attempts/sec, p95 8.47ms, zero oversells with 50,000\nbuyers contending for 10,000 seats.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01APG5C4GouwX8BKRBuvLdSL","tree":{"sha":"c4aa66d1c9258e1465c9eb5bee606e6f05781c0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HuyPhat/orbit-platform/git/trees/c4aa66d1c9258e1465c9eb5bee606e6f05781c0f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HuyPhat/orbit-platform/git/commits/8cf12bccb86578c0cc2ac1555370134985ad4699","verification":{"payload":"tree c4aa66d1c9258e1465c9eb5bee606e6f05781c0f\nparent 3379ae4b1eae74e942adcd02c5a083b709ca15eb\nauthor Lph <phathuy261089@gmail.com> 1789716267 +0000\ncommitter Lph <phathuy261089@gmail.com> 1789716267 +0000\n\nfeat(infra): load harness, k6 scenario, demo traffic and CI\n\nThe load harness needs only Node and Redis so the published numbers can be\nreproduced by anyone who can run the project. It asserts zero oversells and\nzero double-allocation on every run, and CI fails the build if either is\never non-zero.\n\nMeasured: 71,640 hold attempts/sec, p95 8.47ms, zero oversells with 50,000\nbuyers contending for 10,000 seats.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01APG5C4GouwX8BKRBuvLdSL\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOYhq7wZ\ndo0PK4Hr8xUCASq9U9+EUTQfUM6MNVfXB9mfR6rgEnqqtEloGw0xKY59W8DJJuO4y5zu0F6Xdz1r\nIwc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/114322484?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hle-mia-dt","id":114322484,"login":"hle-mia-dt","node_id":"U_kgDOBtBsNA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/HuyPhat/orbit-platform/commit/8cf12bccb86578c0cc2ac1555370134985ad4699","node_id":"C_kwDOUf0S_doAKDhjZjEyYmNjYjg2NTc4YzBjYzJhYzE1NTUzNzAxMzQ5ODVhZDQ2OTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/HuyPhat/orbit-platform/commit/3379ae4b1eae74e942adcd02c5a083b709ca15eb","sha":"3379ae4b1eae74e942adcd02c5a083b709ca15eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HuyPhat/orbit-platform/commits/3379ae4b1eae74e942adcd02c5a083b709ca15eb"}],"sha":"8cf12bccb86578c0cc2ac1555370134985ad4699","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HuyPhat/orbit-platform/commits/8cf12bccb86578c0cc2ac1555370134985ad4699"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/114322484?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hle-mia-dt","id":114322484,"login":"hle-mia-dt","node_id":"U_kgDOBtBsNA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HuyPhat/orbit-platform/commits/3379ae4b1eae74e942adcd02c5a083b709ca15eb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T07:24:27Z","email":"phathuy261089@gmail.com","name":"Lph"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T07:24:27Z","email":"phathuy261089@gmail.com","name":"Lph"},"message":"feat(zones): shell, tickets and console as Next.js Multi-Zones\n\nThree Next applications serving one domain, each deploying on its own\nschedule. Rewrites are server-side so it stays one origin: one cookie\ndomain, no cross-origin checkout. Each zone serves its build output under\nits own assetPrefix so two independently-versioned Next apps never collide\non /_next.\n\nRendering strategy is chosen per route by asking how wrong a page is allowed\nto be — SSG for the fixed category set, ISR for the pages that absorb a\nmarketing spike, never-cached for anything showing money. See ADR 0003.\n\nallowedDevOrigins is required in dev: behind the zone proxy the browser''s\norigin is the shell''s, so without it Next blocks its own HMR resources and\nthe page never hydrates — which looks like a React bug and is not one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01APG5C4GouwX8BKRBuvLdSL","tree":{"sha":"d69c0d92504aa34ad800c73d2edaf5f5c058ee56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HuyPhat/orbit-platform/git/trees/d69c0d92504aa34ad800c73d2edaf5f5c058ee56"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HuyPhat/orbit-platform/git/commits/3379ae4b1eae74e942adcd02c5a083b709ca15eb","verification":{"payload":"tree d69c0d92504aa34ad800c73d2edaf5f5c058ee56\nparent 33b0fe994169d7081da65ee5e9053dda50223b50\nauthor Lph <phathuy261089@gmail.com> 1789716267 +0000\ncommitter Lph <phathuy261089@gmail.com> 1789716267 +0000\n\nfeat(zones): shell, tickets and console as Next.js Multi-Zones\n\nThree Next applications serving one domain, each deploying on its own\nschedule. Rewrites are server-side so it stays one origin: one cookie\ndomain, no cross-origin checkout. Each zone serves its build output under\nits own assetPrefix so two independently-versioned Next apps never collide\non /_next.\n\nRendering strategy is chosen per route by asking how wrong a page is allowed\nto be — SSG for the fixed category set, ISR for the pages that absorb a\nmarketing spike, never-cached for anything showing money. See ADR 0003.\n\nallowedDevOrigins is required in dev: behind the zone proxy the browser''s\norigin is the shell''s, so without it Next blocks its own HMR resources and\nthe page never hydrates — which looks like a React bug and is not one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01APG5C4GouwX8BKRBuvLdSL\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQD0QeTZk\noftLGeklMfLJHGPHGsOxrnu38VN9CBdttWp6ISfeaHINcMPzlEuapepDGRKzrRYeui1UNsAu62Xy\ndgw=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/114322484?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hle-mia-dt","id":114322484,"login":"hle-mia-dt","node_id":"U_kgDOBtBsNA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/HuyPhat/orbit-platform/commit/3379ae4b1eae74e942adcd02c5a083b709ca15eb","node_id":"C_kwDOUf0S_doAKDMzNzlhZTRiMWVhZTc0ZTk0MmFkY2QwMmM1YTA4M2I3MDljYTE1ZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/HuyPhat/orbit-platform/commit/33b0fe994169d7081da65ee5e9053dda50223b50","sha":"33b0fe994169d7081da65ee5e9053dda50223b50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HuyPhat/orbit-platform/commits/33b0fe994169d7081da65ee5e9053dda50223b50"}],"sha":"3379ae4b1eae74e942adcd02c5a083b709ca15eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HuyPhat/orbit-platform/commits/3379ae4b1eae74e942adcd02c5a083b709ca15eb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/114322484?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hle-mia-dt","id":114322484,"login":"hle-mia-dt","node_id":"U_kgDOBtBsNA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HuyPhat/orbit-platform/commits/33b0fe994169d7081da65ee5e9053dda50223b50/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T07:24:27Z","email":"phathuy261089@gmail.com","name":"Lph"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T07:24:27Z","email":"phathuy261089@gmail.com","name":"Lph"},"message":"feat(remotes): federated seat map and promo banner\n\nBuilt with Rsbuild, outside Next.js entirely, and consumed through the plain\n@module-federation/runtime API. nextjs-mf is in maintenance mode and its docs\nstate the App Router is unsupported — see ADR 0002.\n\nThe seat map bypasses React for availability updates: React renders the\nseats once and a diff loop mutates only what changed, O(changes) rather than\nO(seats). Level-of-detail switches to section heatmaps when zoomed out.\nOne focus stop with a roving arrow-key cursor, because 2,000 focusable\nseats would make Tab useless for everyone.\n\nThe promo remote is declared optional in the registry and carries a\ndeliberate crash switch, to demonstrate that an optional remote failing\nleaves no trace on the page.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01APG5C4GouwX8BKRBuvLdSL","tree":{"sha":"5ecfc87a9c39978e129014bc6cd49a2b470b3106","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HuyPhat/orbit-platform/git/trees/5ecfc87a9c39978e129014bc6cd49a2b470b3106"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HuyPhat/orbit-platform/git/commits/33b0fe994169d7081da65ee5e9053dda50223b50","verification":{"payload":"tree 5ecfc87a9c39978e129014bc6cd49a2b470b3106\nparent fb31bf87d6a102522bf355cddab1451468ddecae\nauthor Lph <phathuy261089@gmail.com> 1789716267 +0000\ncommitter Lph <phathuy261089@gmail.com> 1789716267 +0000\n\nfeat(remotes): federated seat map and promo banner\n\nBuilt with Rsbuild, outside Next.js entirely, and consumed through the plain\n@module-federation/runtime API. nextjs-mf is in maintenance mode and its docs\nstate the App Router is unsupported — see ADR 0002.\n\nThe seat map bypasses React for availability updates: React renders the\nseats once and a diff loop mutates only what changed, O(changes) rather than\nO(seats). Level-of-detail switches to section heatmaps when zoomed out.\nOne focus stop with a roving arrow-key cursor, because 2,000 focusable\nseats would make Tab useless for everyone.\n\nThe promo remote is declared optional in the registry and carries a\ndeliberate crash switch, to demonstrate that an optional remote failing\nleaves no trace on the page.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01APG5C4GouwX8BKRBuvLdSL\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQN13+/kY\nrAfZbQNvp3FXl5alZ4W+UkxMb1IZiXsu7JqwcdtArUfQzE9+xf1/4BBLqQn4NTPs4SRIm3MPKGf6\nYgc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/114322484?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hle-mia-dt","id":114322484,"login":"hle-mia-dt","node_id":"U_kgDOBtBsNA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/HuyPhat/orbit-platform/commit/33b0fe994169d7081da65ee5e9053dda50223b50","node_id":"C_kwDOUf0S_doAKDMzYjBmZTk5NDE2OWQ3MDgxZGE2NWVlNWU5MDUzZGRhNTAyMjNiNTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/HuyPhat/orbit-platform/commit/fb31bf87d6a102522bf355cddab1451468ddecae","sha":"fb31bf87d6a102522bf355cddab1451468ddecae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HuyPhat/orbit-platform/commits/fb31bf87d6a102522bf355cddab1451468ddecae"}],"sha":"33b0fe994169d7081da65ee5e9053dda50223b50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HuyPhat/orbit-platform/commits/33b0fe994169d7081da65ee5e9053dda50223b50"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/114322484?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hle-mia-dt","id":114322484,"login":"hle-mia-dt","node_id":"U_kgDOBtBsNA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HuyPhat/orbit-platform/commits/fb31bf87d6a102522bf355cddab1451468ddecae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T07:24:27Z","email":"phathuy261089@gmail.com","name":"Lph"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T07:24:27Z","email":"phathuy261089@gmail.com","name":"Lph"},"message":"feat(realtime): socket.io gateway with a reconnect protocol\n\nSeat deltas fan out from the API over Redis pub/sub, so the gateway scales\nwith concurrent viewers while the API scales with purchase rate — numbers\nthat differ by orders of magnitude during a drop.\n\nClients keep a version and are only sent the deltas they missed. A client\ntoo far behind to patch gets a fresh snapshot instead: patching from an\nunknown baseline renders a map that is confidently wrong, which is worse\nthan a moment of loading.\n\n8 tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01APG5C4GouwX8BKRBuvLdSL","tree":{"sha":"9a39aca4aaa7c1bd1fb20da907106be2f372ba03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HuyPhat/orbit-platform/git/trees/9a39aca4aaa7c1bd1fb20da907106be2f372ba03"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HuyPhat/orbit-platform/git/commits/fb31bf87d6a102522bf355cddab1451468ddecae","verification":{"payload":"tree 9a39aca4aaa7c1bd1fb20da907106be2f372ba03\nparent d7255c97e7b37b3787e03dcc355aa8c4de3502bb\nauthor Lph <phathuy261089@gmail.com> 1789716267 +0000\ncommitter Lph <phathuy261089@gmail.com> 1789716267 +0000\n\nfeat(realtime): socket.io gateway with a reconnect protocol\n\nSeat deltas fan out from the API over Redis pub/sub, so the gateway scales\nwith concurrent viewers while the API scales with purchase rate — numbers\nthat differ by orders of magnitude during a drop.\n\nClients keep a version and are only sent the deltas they missed. A client\ntoo far behind to patch gets a fresh snapshot instead: patching from an\nunknown baseline renders a map that is confidently wrong, which is worse\nthan a moment of loading.\n\n8 tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01APG5C4GouwX8BKRBuvLdSL\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCur1Xev\naZX+0FrX0DTCuRdm3YhV6ksV5RroVN4dKlriJwYq0O4hZoPk4cGk+Fh38N44EZ+8o+TtyNJV7cWT\nEQc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/114322484?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hle-mia-dt","id":114322484,"login":"hle-mia-dt","node_id":"U_kgDOBtBsNA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/HuyPhat/orbit-platform/commit/fb31bf87d6a102522bf355cddab1451468ddecae","node_id":"C_kwDOUf0S_doAKGZiMzFiZjg3ZDZhMTAyNTIyYmYzNTVjZGRhYjE0NTE0NjhkZGVjYWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/HuyPhat/orbit-platform/commit/d7255c97e7b37b3787e03dcc355aa8c4de3502bb","sha":"d7255c97e7b37b3787e03dcc355aa8c4de3502bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HuyPhat/orbit-platform/commits/d7255c97e7b37b3787e03dcc355aa8c4de3502bb"}],"sha":"fb31bf87d6a102522bf355cddab1451468ddecae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HuyPhat/orbit-platform/commits/fb31bf87d6a102522bf355cddab1451468ddecae"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/114322484?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hle-mia-dt","id":114322484,"login":"hle-mia-dt","node_id":"U_kgDOBtBsNA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HuyPhat/orbit-platform/commits/d7255c97e7b37b3787e03dcc355aa8c4de3502bb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T07:24:27Z","email":"phathuy261089@gmail.com","name":"Lph"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T07:24:27Z","email":"phathuy261089@gmail.com","name":"Lph"},"message":"feat(api): oversell-proof hold engine and virtual waiting room\n\nThe hold engine is six Redis Lua scripts. Redis executes a script atomically\non one thread, so check-and-claim is indivisible across any number of seats —\ncorrect by construction rather than by optimistic retry, which collapses\nunder exactly the contention that matters.\n\nHolds are expiry TIMESTAMPS, not TTL keys. Redis expiry is lazy, so a TTL\ndesign leaves seats reading as held past their deadline. Here a lapsed hold\nis logically free the instant it lapses; the sweeper only drives broadcasts.\nIf it stopped running, the engine still would not oversell.\n\nThe waiting room converts an unbounded arrival spike into a metered, fair\nstream. Strictly FIFO, and ZADD NX means refreshing cannot improve your\nplace. Wait estimates come from measured throughput and are allowed to be\nabsent — a wrong ETA is worse than none.\n\nAlso: ports-and-adapters persistence (memory + Mongoose), an allowlist HTML\nsanitiser with 16 XSS regression tests, per-route rate limits shared across\nreplicas, and generated poster SVGs so the demo needs no external images.\n\n70 tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01APG5C4GouwX8BKRBuvLdSL","tree":{"sha":"e23cf9d601f840820b009a13680ba2accb3c2b7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HuyPhat/orbit-platform/git/trees/e23cf9d601f840820b009a13680ba2accb3c2b7a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HuyPhat/orbit-platform/git/commits/d7255c97e7b37b3787e03dcc355aa8c4de3502bb","verification":{"payload":"tree e23cf9d601f840820b009a13680ba2accb3c2b7a\nparent e117270d6fc83cf5850e9c564a4d603889ef6a7b\nauthor Lph <phathuy261089@gmail.com> 1789716267 +0000\ncommitter Lph <phathuy261089@gmail.com> 1789716267 +0000\n\nfeat(api): oversell-proof hold engine and virtual waiting room\n\nThe hold engine is six Redis Lua scripts. Redis executes a script atomically\non one thread, so check-and-claim is indivisible across any number of seats —\ncorrect by construction rather than by optimistic retry, which collapses\nunder exactly the contention that matters.\n\nHolds are expiry TIMESTAMPS, not TTL keys. Redis expiry is lazy, so a TTL\ndesign leaves seats reading as held past their deadline. Here a lapsed hold\nis logically free the instant it lapses; the sweeper only drives broadcasts.\nIf it stopped running, the engine still would not oversell.\n\nThe waiting room converts an unbounded arrival spike into a metered, fair\nstream. Strictly FIFO, and ZADD NX means refreshing cannot improve your\nplace. Wait estimates come from measured throughput and are allowed to be\nabsent — a wrong ETA is worse than none.\n\nAlso: ports-and-adapters persistence (memory + Mongoose), an allowlist HTML\nsanitiser with 16 XSS regression tests, per-route rate limits shared across\nreplicas, and generated poster SVGs so the demo needs no external images.\n\n70 tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01APG5C4GouwX8BKRBuvLdSL\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQER5UPLH\nXOljuQHctOhBbvgwAQPuO2T27Ki4O1YIHCmop0t3AZZedvhcpYyHIAmBumX5zKSfe/frs0VVlwDf\nhwM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/114322484?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hle-mia-dt/gists{/gist_i