l":"https://api.github.com/users/dineshmj","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dineshmj/EnterpriseWebPlatform_V3/commits/957557afd8f08dd083f4de71b57c1a81ecb4e6cd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T19:12:57Z","email":"dineshmj@yahoo.com","name":"dineshmj"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T19:12:57Z","email":"dineshmj@yahoo.com","name":"dineshmj"},"message":"Payments (5a): orchestrated saga. Payments API (EwpPaymentsDb) with the PaymentSaga state machine, step runner (payment network over HTTP, reply timeouts, resends), Outbox/Inbox and a timeline per payment; 202 on POST, Idempotency-Key per payment.\nAccounts as participant: balances + funds_holds (reserve/settle/release, one per PaymentRef, replies on accounts.funds.replies), demo opening deposit, Upgrade-5a-Funds.sql. Couriers AccountsCommandSubscriber and PaymentsSagaReplySubscriber; Payment Network Simulator.\nCompensation releases funds; COMPENSATION_FAILED when the release is not confirmed. IDP: payment.initiate/view for CSAs, Emily to SYD001, two M2M clients. Kafka users/topics/ACLs, DB user, solution, launch profile.\nDocs: saga plan §2 (with diagram and comparison), event catalogue §4.5, Payments/Accounts requirements, READMEs, ReadMe.txt.","tree":{"sha":"4db0386fb6186567249839a81e9369c716dfbcda","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dineshmj/EnterpriseWebPlatform_V3/git/trees/4db0386fb6186567249839a81e9369c716dfbcda"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dineshmj/EnterpriseWebPlatform_V3/git/commits/957557afd8f08dd083f4de71b57c1a81ecb4e6cd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1352986?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dineshmj/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dineshmj/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dineshmj/following{/other_user}","gists_ur