","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/8e2648104a2b4ce9d9621752f7ae040c77cfa077/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T07:04:59Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T07:04:59Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Docs: the theme audit, and the fidelity report''s pointer to it\n\ndocs/design/theme-audit.md is the method, the numbers and the before/after\nfor every root cause: what was measured and against what, the twelve places\nthe theme was changing the components rather than restyling them, and the\none deviation that is left — the design''s focus pink does not reach 3:1 on a\nlight surface, and there is no second focus hue in the transcription to\nreach it with.\n\nThe fidelity report gains §0.1 pointing at it, because the two answer\ndifferent questions. §1 down is about fidelity, how close the theme gets to\nthe transcribed design. It has nothing to say about whether the theme leaves\nthe components working, and a theme can carry every colour of a design and\nstill take a component apart.\n\ndocs/design/theme-audit/ carries seven before/after/reference triples, and\nfixtures/theme-audit/evidence.mjs is what produced them.","tree":{"sha":"4bb6603ba60a672a4c46184a631a957114924cfb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/trees/4bb6603ba60a672a4c46184a631a957114924cfb"},"url":"h