 component names. There is no such list\nany more, so it reads the doc objects the pages are printed from: every module\nwith a main doc has a page, every page documents one, and every page''s import\nline names a subpath the package actually exports. It also checks that every\npage is in the grouped sidebar exactly once — a page in none is a page only\nsearch can find, a page in two looks like two things.\n\nThe name check now runs over the exported HTML as well as the MDX, with one\nallowance written down in both places: the `@astryx.` message ids, the\n`data-astryx-*` attributes and the `astryx-*` class names, all of which a\nreader meets verbatim in DevTools or writes in a selector.\n\n`every-page.spec.ts` covers all 217 routes and now also asserts that a\ncomponent page which documents examples rendered at least one frame — a page\nwhose examples all failed to mount used to pass, because it had no frames to\nfind empty.\n\nThe temporary `port-examples.tsconfig.json` and its stand-in root declaration\nare gone: `apps/docs/examples` is inside the app''s own `tsconfig.json`, so\n`pnpm --filter @tecton/docs typecheck` type-checks all 699 example files\nagainst the real package.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JWM57sS5nw57y7RDQZBBhn","tree":{"sha":"94d26b787118e1ae4fad9fd5f80d19e97a80cc6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/trees/94d26b787118e1ae4fad9fd5f80d19e97a80cc6f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/commits/1e46478fd28fb79e6ce482fdebcf61db0830a734","verification":{"payload":"tree 94d26b787118e1ae4fad9fd5f80d19e97a80cc6f\nparent 5731396f0683674764641aa57072903dbf22ea56\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789887173 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789887173 +0000\n\nCheck the site against the doc objects, and drive every page in a browser\n\nThe guard used to read the barrel for component names. There is no such list\nany more, so it reads the doc objects the pages are printed from: every module\nwith a main doc has a page, every page documents one, and every page''s import\nline names a subpath the package actually exports. It also checks that every\npage is in the grouped sidebar exactly once — a page in none is a page only\nsearch can find, a page in two looks like two things.\n\nThe name check now runs over the exported HTML as well as the MDX, with one\nallowance written down in both places: the `@astryx.` message ids, the\n`data-astryx-*` attributes and the `astryx-*` class names, all of which a\nreader meets verbatim in DevTools or writes in a selector.\n\n`every-page.spec.ts` covers all 217 routes and now also asserts that a\ncomponent page which documents examples rendered at least one frame — a page\nwhose examples all failed to mount used to pass, because it had no frames to\nfind empty.\n\nThe temporary `port-examples.tsconfig.json` and its stand-in root declaration\nare gone: `apps/docs/examples` is inside the app''s own `tsconfig.json`, so\n`pnpm --filter @tecton/docs typecheck` type-checks all 699 example files\nagainst the real package.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JWM57sS5nw57y7RDQZBBhn\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOgp1++P\nXkMfRQkk99Z8qfO/f7CWGxoJ8g+bR3M7g0ldEQJV0yNinvFlIaZfoA0vP7DvcAUfWewTrgwOUuWJ\nVQo=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T07:50:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commit/1e46478fd28fb79e6ce482fdebcf61db0830a734","node_id":"C_kwDOUh2LgdoAKDFlNDY0NzhmZDI4ZmI3OWU2Y2U0ODJmZGViY2Y2MWRiMDgzMGE3MzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commit/5731396f0683674764641aa57072903dbf22ea56","sha":"5731396f0683674764641aa57072903dbf22ea56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/5731396f0683674764641aa57072903dbf22ea56"}],"sha":"1e46478fd28fb79e6ce482fdebcf61db0830a734","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/1e46478fd28fb79e6ce482fdebcf61db0830a734"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/5731396f0683674764641aa57072903dbf22ea56/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T06:52:42Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T06:52:42Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Rewrite the guides to the component system''s own API\n\nEvery code sample in them was written against components the package no longer\nhas: `TextField`, `Panel`, `<Icon name=\"add\">`, `Text variant=\"small\"`,\n`Heading outlineLevel`, a `ToggleButtonGroup` taking `items`. A guide that\nshows code a reader cannot run is worse than no guide.\n\nThey now show what a consumer writes — `TextInput`, `Card` with `VStack` and\n`Heading`, glyph components from `@tecton/react/icons` handed to `Icon`,\n`Text type=` with the eight text types Tecton adds through the theme, and\n`accessibilityLevel` for a heading whose size and rank disagree — and say what\nTecton actually is: a theme over a component system, whose API is that system''s.\n\nTwo guides also needed correcting on substance rather than syntax.\n`micro-frontends` now says each copy of the package shows its own toasts in its\nown viewport (the bus that routed payloads between copies is gone with the rest\nof the invented surface), and that every Tecton rule now sits in one cascade\nlayer, which makes a per-component decision a cross-version contract in the way\na token value already was. `upgrading` follows both through.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JWM57sS5nw57y7RDQZBBhn","tree":{"sha":"89c5a0f6479337bef1615bbadd24a1bba25fe177","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/trees/89c5a0f6479337bef1615bbadd24a1bba25fe177"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/commits/5731396f0683674764641aa57072903dbf22ea56","verification":{"payload":"tree 89c5a0f6479337bef1615bbadd24a1bba25fe177\nparent 37073ffd98f493289373613534073f7b452f1676\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789887162 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789887162 +0000\n\nRewrite the guides to the component system''s own API\n\nEvery code sample in them was written against components the package no longer\nhas: `TextField`, `Panel`, `<Icon name=\"add\">`, `Text variant=\"small\"`,\n`Heading outlineLevel`, a `ToggleButtonGroup` taking `items`. A guide that\nshows code a reader cannot run is worse than no guide.\n\nThey now show what a consumer writes — `TextInput`, `Card` with `VStack` and\n`Heading`, glyph components from `@tecton/react/icons` handed to `Icon`,\n`Text type=` with the eight text types Tecton adds through the theme, and\n`accessibilityLevel` for a heading whose size and rank disagree — and say what\nTecton actually is: a theme over a component system, whose API is that system''s.\n\nTwo guides also needed correcting on substance rather than syntax.\n`micro-frontends` now says each copy of the package shows its own toasts in its\nown viewport (the bus that routed payloads between copies is gone with the rest\nof the invented surface), and that every Tecton rule now sits in one cascade\nlayer, which makes a per-component decision a cross-version contract in the way\na token value already was. `upgrading` follows both through.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JWM57sS5nw57y7RDQZBBhn\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQH9TNu0f\nVmZ0JO4hXfoATQvPBHRBuuIdpFy++j/q9Ydxlt2/e3WFGMKQp1L3RNB/S+58fBZG/cQsaWZFEBTk\nwAg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T07:50:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commit/5731396f0683674764641aa57072903dbf22ea56","node_id":"C_kwDOUh2LgdoAKDU3MzEzOTZmMDY4MzY3NDc2NDY0MWFhNTcwNzI5MDNkYmYyMmVhNTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commit/37073ffd98f493289373613534073f7b452f1676","sha":"37073ffd98f493289373613534073f7b452f1676","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/37073ffd98f493289373613534073f7b452f1676"}],"sha":"5731396f0683674764641aa57072903dbf22ea56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/5731396f0683674764641aa57072903dbf22ea56"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/37073ffd98f493289373613534073f7b452f1676/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T06:52:31Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T06:52:31Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Ship the images the ported templates reference\n\n101 files, copied verbatim from the component system''s documentation site and\ncredited with the rest of the corpus in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md. The ported\nexamples reference 80 of them; the other 21 are the @2x variants and alternate\ntheme shots that came with the set.\n\nTwo paths stay missing on purpose. `AvatarFallbackChain` names\n`does-not-exist-primary.jpg` and `does-not-exist-fallback.jpg` to demonstrate\nwhat an avatar does when its image 404s, so giving them a placeholder would\ndocument the opposite of what the example is about.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JWM57sS5nw57y7RDQZBBhn","tree":{"sha":"979c8a62737dfcebdcc8f9ccefa0a0e0b40e99c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/trees/979c8a62737dfcebdcc8f9ccefa0a0e0b40e99c8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/commits/37073ffd98f493289373613534073f7b452f1676","verification":{"payload":"tree 979c8a62737dfcebdcc8f9ccefa0a0e0b40e99c8\nparent 3108fcdd23b88865ef97794ec022fc8783c397ec\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789887151 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789887151 +0000\n\nShip the images the ported templates reference\n\n101 files, copied verbatim from the component system''s documentation site and\ncredited with the rest of the corpus in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md. The ported\nexamples reference 80 of them; the other 21 are the @2x variants and alternate\ntheme shots that came with the set.\n\nTwo paths stay missing on purpose. `AvatarFallbackChain` names\n`does-not-exist-primary.jpg` and `does-not-exist-fallback.jpg` to demonstrate\nwhat an avatar does when its image 404s, so giving them a placeholder would\ndocument the opposite of what the example is about.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JWM57sS5nw57y7RDQZBBhn\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQG4i+i4o\nhNduQ9jg/80KUd81jPomokm0aUQU3ofJLu4cPZOhoroVwH9sK2HjscS/Bt9MlgADbsN2+BBpJPoa\nvAk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T07:50:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscript