aude"},"message":"Port the component page, the gallery and the template gallery from upstream\n\nThe owner called the old sidebar and gallery unusable, and the pages described\ncomponents that no longer exist. Rather than invent a shape again, these are\nports of the component system''s own documentation site — its\n`component-detail/*`, `ShowcaseThumbnail.tsx`, `eagerShowcases.ts`, the\ncomponents gallery and the template gallery — with the file each one came from\nnamed in its header and the licence credited at the repository root.\n\nThree deliberate differences. Previews render under Tecton''s theme in a nested\n`TectonProvider` with a dark/light switch, because what a page is for is what\nTecton''s theme makes of the component; upstream renders under its neutral one.\nThe tabs are flattened into one page, so search and the table of contents see\nthe theming targets and the accessibility table rather than only the overview.\nAnd the showcase leads the page as an example block rather than a bare card, so\nthe code that drew it is one tab away — which is also what keeps \"every example\nis shown as code\" true.\n\nDropped on the way in: the shadcn install tabs, the playground links, the\nanalytics calls, the canary gates, and the inline type-definition popovers, for\nwhich the vendored docs carry no extracted declarations.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JWM57sS5nw57y7RDQZBBhn","tree":{"sha":"fec5a9a01af9b1cb31ae43c45d9412895ae79ef2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/trees/fec5a9a01af9b1cb31ae43c45d9412895ae79ef2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/commits/3108fcdd23b88865ef97794ec022fc8783c397ec","verification":{"payload":"tree fec5a9a01af9b1cb31ae43c45d9412895ae79ef2\nparent e3dd25bb0dc05bd6da706360f697ed2215f1ca47\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789887139 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789887139 +0000\n\nPort the component page, the gallery and the template gallery from upstream\n\nThe owner called the old sidebar and gallery unusable, and the pages described\ncomponents that no longer exist. Rather than invent a shape again, these are\nports of the component system''s own documentation site — its\n`component-detail/*`, `ShowcaseThumbnail.tsx`, `eagerShowcases.ts`, the\ncomponents gallery and the template gallery — with the file each one came from\nnamed in its header and the licence credited at the repository root.\n\nThree deliberate differences. Previews render under Tecton''s theme in a nested\n`TectonProvider` with a dark/light switch, because what a page is for is what\nTecton''s theme makes of the component; upstream renders under its neutral one.\nThe tabs are flattened into one page, so search and the table of contents see\nthe theming targets and the accessibility table rather than only the overview.\nAnd the showcase leads the page as an example block rather than a bare card, so\nthe code that drew it is one tab away — which is also what keeps \"every example\nis shown as code\" true.\n\nDropped on the way in: the shadcn install tabs, the playground links, the\nanalytics calls, the canary gates, and the inline type-definition popovers, for\nwhich the vendored docs carry no extracted declarations.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JWM57sS5nw57y7RDQZBBhn\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHoEuQW5\nCg4LW789s8tt8XQdffmjc699G7AA53MQtZ5lmdAmNSd4gTfag57Jg23oXxV64isKScfvD9WeU0Hd\nBww=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T07:50:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commit/3108fcdd23b88865ef97794ec022fc8783c397ec","node_id":"C_kwDOUh2LgdoAKDMxMDhmY2RkMjNiODg4NjVlZjk3Nzk0ZWMwMjJmYzg3ODNjMzk3ZWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commit/e3dd25bb0dc05bd6da706360f697ed2215f1ca47","sha":"e3dd25bb0dc05bd6da706360f697ed2215f1ca47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/e3dd25bb0dc05bd6da706360f697ed2215f1ca47"}],"sha":"3108fcdd23b88865ef97794ec022fc8783c397ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/3108fcdd23b88865ef97794ec022fc8783c397ec"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/e3dd25bb0dc05bd6da706360f697ed2215f1ca47/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T06:52:05Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T06:52:05Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Print the component pages from the component system''s own doc objects\n\nThe site documented components Tecton had invented. It has none: the package\nre-exports a component system one for one, and that system ships a `.doc.mjs`\nbeside every module — the prose, the props, the anatomy, the best practices,\nthe accessibility requirements, the theming targets. 229 of them, plus\n`groups.doc.mjs`. The generator now reads those instead.\n\nOne page per main doc: 106 components and 38 hooks. A doc with `subComponentOf`\ndocuments part of another component, so its props become a table on that\ncomponent''s page rather than a route of its own — which is what keeps the\nsidebar a list of things a consumer imports.\n\nEvery string is rewritten to say Tecton. Three things survive verbatim, because\na reader meets them exactly as they are and a renamed one would match nothing:\nthe `@astryx.` message ids an override is keyed on, the `data-astryx-*`\nattributes the theme is scoped to, and the `astryx-*` class and layer names the\ncomponents carry and a `defineTheme` target names.\n\nThe sidebar is grouped by the component system''s own rule, and the folders are\nsynthetic: the files stay flat, so a page is still `/docs/components/Button`\nrather than `/docs/components/Button/Button`. 144 rows become 75 with the\ncurrent page''s group open.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JWM57sS5nw57y7RDQZBBhn","tree":{"sha":"fa64fa88036af26ae603ccafeeca6f8e27cc4845","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/trees/fa64fa88036af26ae603ccafeeca6f8e27cc4845"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/commits/e3dd25bb0dc05bd6da706360f697ed2215f1ca47","verification":{"payload":"tree fa64fa88036af26ae603ccafeeca6f8e27cc4845\nparent d5a133a85594281642a19d342d95dc14c6a7362b\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789887125 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789887125 +0000\n\nPrint the component pages from the component system''s own doc objects\n\nThe site documented components Tecton had invented. It has none: the package\nre-exports a component system one for one, and that system ships a `.doc.mjs`\nbeside every module — the prose, the props, the anatomy, the best practices,\nthe accessibility requirements, the theming targets. 229 of them, plus\n`groups.doc.mjs`. The generator now reads those instead.\n\nOne page per main doc: 106 components and 38 hooks. A doc with `subComponentOf`\ndocuments part of another component, so its props become a table on that\ncomponent''s page rather than a route of its own — which is what keeps the\nsidebar a list of things a consumer imports.\n\nEvery string is rewritten to say Tecton. Three things survive verbatim, because\na reader meets them exactly as they are and a renamed one would match nothing:\nthe `@astryx.` message ids an override is keyed on, the `data-astryx-*`\nattributes the theme is scoped to, and the `astryx-*` class and layer names the\ncomponents carry and a `defineTheme` target names.\n\nThe sidebar is grouped by the component system''s own rule, and the folders are\nsynthetic: the files stay flat, so a page is still `/docs/components/Button`\nrather than `/docs/components/Button/Button`. 144 rows become 75 with the\ncurrent page''s group open.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JWM57sS5nw57y7RDQZBBhn\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMQaswe2\nIFemykC2dVPu1sybbHIGHuxm4brPEhPXe1j8FFaewK1xwzsaWE5IUj5JKL73xQtfJVRNCL4kjbMk\ngw8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T07:50:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commit/e3dd25bb0dc05bd6da706360f697ed2215f1ca47","node_id":"C_kwDOUh2LgdoAKGUzZGQyNWJiMGRjMDViZDZkYTcwNjM2MGY2OTdlZDIyMTVmMWNhNDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commit/d5a133a85594281642a19d342d95dc14c6a7362b","sha":"d5a133a85594281642a19d342d95dc14c6a7362b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/d5a133a85594281642a19d342d95dc14c6a7362b"}],"sha":"e3dd25bb0dc05bd6da706360f697ed2215f1ca47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/e3dd25bb0dc05bd6da706360f697ed2215f1ca47"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/d5a133a85594281642a19d342d95dc14c6a7362b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T06:51:54Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T06:51:54Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Compile StyleX on the docs site, so the examples that use it can run\n\nEighteen of the ported examples style themselves with `@stylexjs/stylex`, and\nseven of those read `@tecton/react/theme/tokens.stylex`. They are shown as\nsource and run in the reader''s browser, so the site has to compile StyleX the\nway a consumer''s build would.\n\n`babel.config.json` runs the StyleX plugin with the options the package builds\nwith, so a class the site emits is namespaced like a class the package emits.\nIt is JSON because Next''s Babel loader refuses a `.cjs` or `.mjs` config and\nthis package is `\"type\": \"module\"`, which makes a `.js` one ESM. A Babel config\nmeans webpack rather than Turbopack, so `dev` and `build` pass `--webpack`.\n\n`postcss.config.cjs` extracts the compiled classes into `@stylex;`, which lives\nin a stylesheet of its own rather than in `global.css`: Tailwind v4 rebuilds\nwhatever stylesheet it is handed from its own tree and drops the rules the\nStyleX plugin injected, whichever order the two plugins run in.\n\nThe `browserslist` entry is not cosmetic. Without it Babel down-levels the\nUnicode property escapes in fumadocs'' own dependencies, and the build fails on\nregular expressions nobody in this repository wrote.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JWM57sS5nw57y7RDQZBBhn","tree":{"sha":"e7c12215f52ea582d8dc9875f258fc63a9f6a4e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/trees/e7c12215f52ea582d8dc9875f258fc63a9f6a4e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/commits/d5a133a85594281642a19d342d95dc14c6a7362b","verification":{"payload":"tree e7c12215f52ea582d8dc9875f258fc63a9f6a4e0\nparent eae140a5221cee73d759b9cc00e55e0f1b24b8b2\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789887114 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789887114 +0000\n\nCompile StyleX on the docs site, so the examples that use it can run\n\nEighteen of the ported examples style themselves with `@stylexjs/stylex`, and\nseven of those read `@tecton/react/theme/tokens.stylex`. They are shown as\nsource and run in the reader''s browser, so the site has to compile StyleX the\nway a consumer''s build would.\n\n`babel.config.json` runs the StyleX plugin with the options the package builds\nwith, so a class the site emits is namespaced like a class the package emits.\nIt is JSON because Next''s Babel loader refuses a `.cjs` or `.mjs` config and\nthis package is `\"type\": \"module\"`, which makes a `.js` one ESM. A Babel config\nmeans webpack rather than Turbopack, so `dev` and `build` pass `--webpack`.\n\n`postcss.config.cjs` extracts the compiled classes into `@stylex;`, which lives\nin a stylesheet of its own rather than in `global.css`: Tailwind v4 rebuilds\nwhatever stylesheet it is handed from its own tree and drops the rules the\nStyleX plugin injected, whichever order the two plugins run in.\n\nThe `browserslist` entry is not cosmetic. Without it Babel down-levels the\nUnicode property escapes in fumadocs'' own dependencies, and the build fails on\nregular expressions nobody in this repository wrote.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JWM57sS5nw57y7RDQZBBhn\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNJkc+Vu\nHVwflnhAXKo8JJMhuRsnboTSwaaI9DwFuUaoeUExFZH+XLyHJlVw5uTaQJy44fQ5BLYRPhoKhVTW\nUAk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T07:50:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commit/d5a133a85594281642a19d342d95dc14c6a7362b","node_id":"C_kwDOUh2LgdoAKGQ1YTEzM2E4NTU5NDI4MTY0MmExOWQzNDJkOTVkYzE0YzZhNzM2MmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commit/eae140a5221cee73d759b9cc00e55e0f1b24b8b2","sha":"eae140a5221cee73d759b9cc00e55e0f1b24b8b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/eae140a5221cee73d759b9cc00e55e0f1b24b8b2"}],"sha":"d5a133a85594281642a19d342d95dc14c6a7362b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/d5a133a85594281642a19d342d95dc14c6a7362b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/90c16720d256fef05ff3a6e44cb8601c81836124/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T06:38:57Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T06:38:57Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Theme: stop the overrides taking the components apart\n\nEvery Tecton rule lands in @layer astryx-theme, which comes after the layer\nthe components'' own CSS lives in — so a theme declaration beats any\ncomponent declaration of the same property whatever its selector, including\nthe per-corner, per-state and per-variant rules a component uses to do its\njob. Most of what is removed here was saying something the component was\nalready saying, in a place where saying it again overrode something else.\n\nMeasured against the same 646 examples rendered under the theme upstream''s\nown documentation site uses, this takes the examples carrying a structural\nor focus finding from 191 to 3. docs/design/theme-audit.md has the method and\nthe evidence; the rules are pinned by tests so they cannot come back.\n\nWhat changed, by what it was breaking:\n\n- A `border-radius` shorthand on `button` and eleven other targets flattened\n  the per-corner radii a connected control squares its interior edges with,\n  so every ButtonGroup came apart into a row of separate pills and every\n  joined input lost its seam. All of them were restating a value\n  `--radius-element` already had. The radii that stay are the ones the design\n  names and the component does not have: a 4px menu panel, a 2px menu item, a\n  4px card-container banner, a Token pill.\n- `card.base.backgroundColor` painted over the `variant` prop, so `muted`,\n  `transparent` and the ten hues all came out the colour of a default card;\n  the border did the same to the variants the component leaves borderless,\n  and bypassed the `calc()` that draws a border inside the padding; and\n  `boxShadow: ''none''` erased not only the `elevation` prop but `--_card-ring`,\n  which is how SelectableCard draws its selection. With its padding also\n  being the component''s own default, `card` and `section` stop being targets\n  at all.\n- `:nth-child(even)` and `:hover` written into `table-row` striped and\n  highlighted every table, `isStriped` and `hasHover` notwithstanding, and\n  left pinned cells replaying the old colour. Rows, list items and menu items\n  now take Tecton''s fill through the token the component already hovers with.\n- A 1px border on `switch` ate 2px of a border-box track, squeezed the thumb\n  off-centre, and overrode the forced-colours rule that keeps the control\n  perceivable when Windows strips its fill.\n- Re-colouring a field''s resting border overrode its `:focus-within` one, so\n  every TextInput, TextArea, Selector, Typeahead and Tokenizer stopped showing\n  keyboard focus; and the fields Tecton did not paint rang in\n  `--color-accent`, a dark violet at 2.2:1 against the page. Every field in\n  the family now states its focus in the design''s focus ink.\n- The focus ring was invisible inside a Banner — 1.0:1 on success, 1.2:1 on\n  info, warning and error — so a banner now rings in the ink the design\n  already puts on that fill, which clears 4.8:1 on all five.\n- `--shadow-inset-selected` wore the focus pink, making a selected control\n  indistinguishable from a focused one. It is a violet inset now.\n- `link.base.color` painted over four of the five values of Link''s `color`\n  prop and took its hover tint with them; the design''s statement is about the\n  default link, so it is made on `accent`.\n- `banner-frame`''s radius rounded full-bleed banners, and as a shorthand it\n  flattened the per-corner rules that let a banner''s header and body meet\n  flush. It moved to `banner`, on `container:card`, as `--_banner-radius`.\n- `tooltip` is gone: there is no tooltip page in the transcription, and the\n  override repainted an intentionally inverted surface as a popover.\n- Redundant restatements removed from `badge`, `checkbox-indicator`,\n  `segmented-control`, `kbd`, `code-block`, `heading`, `input-group`, `field`\n  and `dialog`, and `popover`''s radius with them — a popover is the surface\n  under a dozen things, some of which square themselves.\n\nNo token colour moved. The manifest loses nine private component variables\nthe removed overrides were the only reason for, and gains `--_banner-radius`.","tree":{"sha":"50934ec4d0f0ea2fb01cec9c7511fb6710874ce9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/trees/50934ec4d0f0ea2fb01cec9c7511fb6710874ce9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/commits/90c16720d256fef05ff3a6e44cb8601c81836124","verification":{"payload":"tree 50934ec4d0f0ea2fb01cec9c7511fb6710874ce9\nparent 4fd81bf2b59b07bee5719e6fab3f140deb376fcc\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789886337 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789886337 +0000\n\nTheme: stop the overrides taking the components apart\n\nEvery Tecton rule lands in @layer astryx-theme, which comes after the layer\nthe components'' own CSS lives in — so a theme declaration beats any\ncomponent declaration of the same property whatever its selector, including\nthe per-corner, per-state and per-variant rules a component uses to do its\njob. Most of what is removed here was saying something the component was\nalready saying, in a place where saying it again overrode something else.\n\nMeasured against the same 646 examples rendered under the theme upstream''s\nown documentation site uses, this takes the examples carrying a structural\nor focus finding from 191 to 3. docs/design/theme-audit.md has the method and\nthe evidence; the rules are pinned by tests so they cannot come back.\n\nWhat changed, by what it was breaking:\n\n- A `border-radius` shorthand on `button` and eleven other targets flattened\n  the per-corner radii a connected control squares its interior edges with,\n  so every ButtonGroup came apart into a row of separate pills and every\n  joined input lost its seam. All of them were restating a value\n  `--radius-element` already had. The radii that stay are the ones the design\n  names and the component does not have: a 4px menu panel, a 2px menu item, a\n  4px card-container banner, a Token pill.\n- `card.base.backgroundColor` painted over the `variant` prop, so `muted`,\n  `transparent` and the ten hues all came out the colour of a default card;\n  the border did the same to the variants the component leaves borderless,\n  and bypassed the `calc()` that draws a border inside the padding; and\n  `boxShadow: ''none''` erased not only the `elevation` prop but `--_card-ring`,\n  which is how SelectableCard draws its selection. With its padding also\n  being the component''s own default, `card` and `section` stop being targets\n  at all.\n- `:nth-child(even)` and `:hover` written into `table-row` striped and\n  highlighted every table, `isStriped` and `hasHover` notwithstanding, and\n  left pinned cells replaying the old colour. Rows, list items and menu items\n  now take Tecton''s fill through the token the component already hovers with.\n- A 1px border on `switch` ate 2px of a border-box track, squeezed the thumb\n  off-centre, and overrode the forced-colours rule that keeps the control\n  perceivable when Windows strips its fill.\n- Re-colouring a field''s resting border overrode its `:focus-within` one, so\n  every TextInput, TextArea, Selector, Typeahead and Tokenizer stopped showing\n  keyboard focus; and the fields Tecton did not paint rang in\n  `--color-accent`, a dark violet at 2.2:1 against the page. Every field in\n  the family now states its focus in the design''s focus ink.\n- The focus ring was invisible inside a Banner — 1.0:1 on success, 1.2:1 on\n  info, warning and error — so a banner now rings in the ink the design\n  already puts on that fill, which clears 4.8:1 on all five.\n- `--shadow-inset-selected` wore the focus pink, making a selected control\n  indistinguishable from a focused one. It is a violet inset now.\n- `link.base.color` painted over four of the five values of Link''s `color`\n  prop and took its hover tint with them; the design''s statement is about the\n  default link, so it is made on `accent`.\n- `banner-frame`''s radius rounded full-bleed banners, and as a shorthand it\n  flattened the per-corner rules that let a banner''s header and body meet\n  flush. It moved to `banner`, on `container:card`, as `--_banner-radius`.\n- `tooltip` is gone: there is no tooltip page in the transcription, and the\n  override repainted an intentionally inverted surface as a popover.\n- Redundant restatements removed from `badge`, `checkbox-indicator`,\n  `segmented-control`, `kbd`, `code-block`, `heading`, `input-group`, `field`\n  and `dialog`, and `popover`''s radius with them — a popover is the surface\n  under a dozen things, some of which square themselves.\n\nNo token colour moved. The manifest loses nine private component variables\nthe removed overrides were the only reason for, and gains `--_banner-radius`.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQF9Lc/pN\nSwc+Gvr/N/TWPgBiaB0ir7dGCs7iU08UqhRJA0a+zRC3c3C1/GpdqFtCeWx8G+kJCKwJ4FFBwgph\nngQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T07:17:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commit/90c16720d256fef05ff3a6e44cb8601c81836124","node_id":"C_kwDOUh2LgdoAKDkwYzE2NzIwZDI1NmZlZjA1ZmYzYTZlNDRjYjg2MDFjODE4MzYxMjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commit/4fd81bf2b59b07bee5719e6fab3f140deb376fcc","sha":"4fd81bf2b59b07bee5719e6fab3f140deb376fcc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/4fd81bf2b59b07bee5719e6fab3f140deb376fcc"}],"sha":"90c16720d256fef05ff3a6e44cb8601c81836124","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/90c16720d256fef05ff3a6e44cb8601c81836124"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/4fd81bf2b59b07bee5719e6fab3f140deb376fcc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T06:38:42Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T06:38:42Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Audit harness: build each side once instead of serving 1700 modules\n\nThe package and core together are about 1700 ES modules, and a dev server\nhands the browser every one of them as its own request with its own\ntransform. That is fine for one page and three hours for 646. Each side is\nnow built once up front and served static, which brings a full run down to\nabout fifteen minutes.\n\nThe rest is the measurement getting more exact, in both directions:\n\n- an `svg`''s insides are artwork, not layout, so the walk stops at the `svg`\n  and an icon set is never compared with another icon set;\n- a box a *theme decision* explains — its own type or padding, or its\n  subtree''s — is recorded rather than charged, since a card around a\n  paragraph around a heading is shorter when the heading is;\n- a focus ring is now found wherever it is drawn: on the stop, on the\n  indicator beside it, or on the `:focus-within` ancestor that rings for it —\n  and a border that changes colour on focus counts, which is the affordance\n  every field in the system uses;\n- a box-shadow only counts as a ring if focus is what added it, and\n  `outline-style: auto` is the browser''s own ring, not the theme''s;\n- a translucent backdrop is composited down to something opaque before its\n  contrast is measured, instead of being assumed to sit on white;\n- a crashed page is told apart from a closed one, a render gets long enough\n  to settle that a BottomSheet opening is not read as a DOM difference, and\n  the neutral render is only tabbed when the Tecton one gave it something to\n  compare against.","tree":{"sha":"3227cf77800827ea5da60d4265420f554115374e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/trees/3227cf77800827ea5da60d4265420f554115374e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/commits/4fd81bf2b59b07bee5719e6fab3f140deb376fcc","verification":{"payload":"tree 3227cf77800827ea5da60d4265420f554115374e\nparent 1af7310b5a1e5f8b127590ca3d272ba2991760ae\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789886322 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789886322 +0000\n\nAudit harness: build each side once instead of serving 1700 modules\n\nThe package and core together are about 1700 ES modules, and a dev server\nhands the browser every one of them as its own request with its own\ntransform. That is fine for one page and three hours for 646. Each side is\nnow built once up front and served static, which brings a full run down to\nabout fifteen minutes.\n\nThe rest is the measurement getting more exact, in both directions:\n\n- an `svg`''s insides are artwork, not layout, so the walk stops at the `svg`\n  and an icon set is never compared with another icon set;\n- a box a *theme decision* explains — its own type or padding, or its\n  subtree''s — is recorded rather than charged, since a card around a\n  paragraph around a heading is shorter when the heading is;\n- a focus ring is now found wherever it is drawn: on the stop, on the\n  indicator beside it, or on the `:focus-within` ancestor that rings for it —\n  and a border that changes colour on focus counts, which is the affordance\n  every field in the system uses;\n- a box-shadow only counts as a ring if focus is what added it, and\n  `outline-style: auto` is the browser''s own ring, not the theme''s;\n- a translucent backdrop is composited down to something opaque before its\n  contrast is measured, instead of being assumed to sit on white;\n- a crashed page is told apart from a closed one, a render gets long enough\n  to settle that a BottomSheet opening is not read as a DOM difference, and\n  the neutral render is only tabbed when the Tecton one gave it something to\n  compare against.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEFErzue\nycrzLs28DTvkrjXn4gQ0bnvBLdw7ER9340B7nMBCFzIpmyXVn5lO6Hq5ovlzQiypBxRIgt3Tfj/K\n1gY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T07:17:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commit/4fd81bf2b59b07bee5719e6fab3f140deb376fcc","node_id":"C_kwDOUh2LgdoAKDRmZDgxYmYyYjU5YjA3YmVlNTcxOWU2ZmFiM2YxNDBkZWIzNzZmY2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commit/1af7310b5a1e5f8b127590ca3d272ba2991760ae","sha":"1af7310b5a1e5f8b127590ca3d272ba2991760ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/1af7310b5a1e5f8b127590ca3d272ba2991760ae"}],"sha":"4fd81bf2b59b07bee5719e6fab3f140deb376fcc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/4fd81bf2b59b07bee5719e6fab3f140deb376fcc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/1af7310b5a1e5f8b127590ca3d272ba2991760ae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T05:49:25Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T05:49:25Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Audit harness: render every example under both themes and diff them\n\nTecton is a theme and nothing else, so the only question worth asking about\nit is whether it restyles the components it themes or changes them. That\nquestion is answerable, because the same components are also rendered by\nsomebody else''s theme: upstream''s documentation site shows its examples under\n@astryxdesign/theme-neutral.\n\nfixtures/theme-audit mounts all 646 ported examples twice — once on\n@tecton/react under TectonProvider, once on the same example files with every\n@tecton/react/<Module> import resolved to @astryxdesign/core/<Module> under\nneutralTheme — and then, per example, screenshots both renders, diffs the two\nelement trees box by box, and tabs through the Tecton render checking every\nfocus ring for visibility, contrast and clipping.\n\nTwo things it deliberately does not count. @tecton/react/icons is not\nrewritten, so both sides draw the same glyphs and an icon that measures\ndifferently can only be the theme''s doing. And differences the type scale\nexplains — Tecton''s ladder is not upstream''s, which is the point of it — are\nbucketed separately, for the differing element and for every block that\ncontains it.\n\nIt is dev-only: private, never published, not part of pnpm build or pnpm\ncheck.","tree":{"sha":"858743ca4a1c7719cf07bec38677a73761bab3b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/trees/858743ca4a1c7719cf07bec38677a73761bab3b0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/commits/1af7310b5a1e5f8b127590ca3d272ba2991760ae","verification":{"payload":"tree 858743ca4a1c7719cf07bec38677a73761bab3b0\nparent eae140a5221cee73d759b9cc00e55e0f1b24b8b2\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789883365 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789883365 +0000\n\nAudit harness: render every example under both themes and diff them\n\nTecton is a theme and nothing else, so the only question worth asking about\nit is whether it restyles the components it themes or changes them. That\nquestion is answerable, because the same components are also rendered by\nsomebody else''s theme: upstream''s documentation site shows its examples under\n@astryxdesign/theme-neutral.\n\nfixtures/theme-audit mounts all 646 ported examples twice — once on\n@tecton/react under TectonProvider, once on the same example files with every\n@tecton/react/<Module> import resolved to @astryxdesign/core/<Module> under\nneutralTheme — and then, per example, screenshots both renders, diffs the two\nelement trees box by box, and tabs through the Tecton render checking every\nfocus ring for visibility, contrast and clipping.\n\nTwo things it deliberately does not count. @tecton/react/icons is not\nrewritten, so both sides draw the same glyphs and an icon that measures\ndifferently can only be the theme''s doing. And differences the type scale\nexplains — Tecton''s ladder is not upstream''s, which is the point of it — are\nbucketed separately, for the differing element and for every block that\ncontains it.\n\nIt is dev-only: private, never published, not part of pnpm build or pnpm\ncheck.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ