/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/bb955faf8cd911ba92d7626d6f0f86a079ce9307/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T04:43:33Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T04:43:33Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Docs: the surface, the pipeline, the upgrade and what v2 gave up\n\n`component-mapping.md` becomes `surface.md`. There is no mapping any more, so\nwhat the file says instead is what is published, how the 118 subpaths are\ngenerated, the vendoring and the scrub rules, and the five allowlist entries\nwith the reason each one has to stay.\n\n- `build-pipeline.md`: the two new drift checks as steps 0c and 0d, the empty\n  StyleX extract and why it is correct, the declaration scrub in full, the\n  export-target check, the new dist layout and the two surface tests.\n- `upgrading-astryx.md`: step 5 in order — modules and README before the build,\n  the build, the generators, then the documentation port — and the module check\n  the report prints instead of the wrapper check.\n- `docs/design/fidelity-report.md`: a \"what changed in v2\" section at the top.\n  The theme''s verdicts stand, because no token value moved; what is gone is the\n  fidelity that lived in wrapper code, and the one thing lost outright is\n  cross-copy toast merging.\n- `packages/react/CHANGELOG.md` and `README.md`: consumer-facing, written in\n  the component system''s own names, with a before/after that says look the\n  component up in its own documentation rather than in a migration table.\n- Root README: the component-count claims, the guard table and the deviations.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JWM57sS5nw57y7RDQZBBhn","tree":{"sha":"7b57e2a75a5d92ab8239c0837d63a67a708d532a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/trees/7b57e2a75a5d92ab8239c0837d63a67a708d532a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/commits/bb955faf8cd911ba92d7626d6f0f86a079ce9307","verification":{"payload":"tree 7b57e2a75a5d92ab8239c0837d63a67a708d532a\nparent 7d66b458275a124dbeef07314d97b84cee11ce4c\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789879413 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789879413 +0000\n\nDocs: the surface, the pipeline, the upgrade and what v2 gave up\n\n`component-mapping.md` becomes `surface.md`. There is no mapping any more, so\nwhat the file says instead is what is published, how the 118 subpaths are\ngenerated, the vendoring and the scrub rules, and the five allowlist entries\nwith the reason each one has to stay.\n\n- `build-pipeline.md`: the two new drift checks as steps 0c and 0d, the empty\n  StyleX extract and why it is correct, the declaration scrub in full, the\n  export-target check, the new dist layout and the two surface tests.\n- `upgrading-astryx.md`: step 5 in order — modules and README before the build,\n  the build, the generators, then the documentation port — and the module check\n  the report prints instead of the wrapper check.\n- `docs/design/fidelity-report.md`: a \"what changed in v2\" section at the top.\n  The theme''s verdicts stand, because no token value moved; what is gone is the\n  fidelity that lived in wrapper code, and the one thing lost outright is\n  cross-copy toast merging.\n- `packages/react/CHANGELOG.md` and `README.md`: consumer-facing, written in\n  the component system''s own names, with a before/after that says look the\n  component up in its own documentation rather than in a migration table.\n- Root README: the component-count claims, the guard table and the deviations.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JWM57sS5nw57y7RDQZBBhn\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKU2xO/f\nTtd/6YlNpOmUznOWddzfKnR03ZUdBlv41j0TEsQ3CxRreyhcfYOcNm6G8v3AHuKI/nkgSoS3WHgo\n+Q8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T04:49:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commit/bb955faf8cd911ba92d7626d6f0f86a079ce9307","node_id":"C_kwDOUh2LgdoAKGJiOTU1ZmFmOGNkOTExYmE5MmQ3NjI2ZDZmMGY4NmEwNzljZTkzMDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commit/7d66b458275a124dbeef07314d97b84cee11ce4c","sha":"7d66b458275a124dbeef07314d97b84cee11ce4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/7d66b458275a124dbeef07314d97b84cee11ce4c"}],"sha":"bb955faf8cd911ba92d7626d6f0f86a079ce9307","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/bb955faf8cd911ba92d7626d6f0f86a079ce9307"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/fa75a6984ec3ad792f9280ae7e3b44ca5a10b5fe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T04:42:36Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T04:42:36Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Make the ported examples speak Tecton, and keep their icons the right size\n\nThree changes to the port, all of them in the script, so they hold for every\nre-run rather than for this checkout.\n\nAn example is documentation. A comment, a caption or a sample that named the\nlibrary underneath Tecton was a page telling the reader they were reading about\nsomething else — and the docs-site guard fails any page that does it. The port\nnow rewrites prose as well as imports: comments, string and template literals\nand JSX text, in the 34 files that needed it. Identifiers, module specifiers and\nkeys are untouched, and two rewrites are more than a name swap because the plain\nswap would have been untrue: the reset + component stylesheet pair becomes the\none `@tecton/react/styles.css` Tecton ships, and a comment naming the cascade\nlayer says what the layer is, because Tecton''s own stylesheet keeps upstream''s\nlayer name.\n\nOne file is deliberately left naming upstream: the i18n example overrides the\nmessage id `@astryx.selector.placeholder`. That id is the library''s, not prose;\nrewriting it would leave an example that reads right and overrides nothing. It\nis in the log with that reason.\n\nLucide''s `size={n}` is now translated to `width={n} height={n}` rather than\ndropped — a Tecton glyph has no `size`, but it has both of those, so the 25\nicons in the theme showcase draw at the size the example drew them.\n\nThe log gains the two new sections and, in its Notes, the list of subpaths the\nexamples import beyond a component module — the surface `@tecton/react` has to\ncover for them to compile, ready to check a generator against.\n\nStill 646/646 blocks and 53/53 page templates, no drift, and the temporary\ntypecheck harness reports no errors over all 699 ported files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JWM57sS5nw57y7RDQZBBhn","tree":{"sha":"a94ac2283d4f5eb1eb4e15f95f921149df7df0c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/trees/a94ac2283d4f5eb1eb4e15f95f921149df7df0c9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/commits/fa75a6984ec3ad792f9280ae7e3b44ca5a10b5fe","verification":{"payload":"tree a94ac2283d4f5eb1eb4e15f95f921149df7df0c9\nparent cd45135230aa978e599c35cb5d0aa2a3f2592c59\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789879356 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789879356 +0000\n\nMake the ported examples speak Tecton, and keep their icons the right size\n\nThree changes to the port, all of them in the script, so they hold for every\nre-run rather than for this checkout.\n\nAn example is documentation. A comment, a caption or a sample that named the\nlibrary underneath Tecton was a page telling the reader they were reading about\nsomething else — and the docs-site guard fails any page that does it. The port\nnow rewrites prose as well as imports: comments, string and template literals\nand JSX text, in the 34 files that needed it. Identifiers, module specifiers and\nkeys are untouched, and two rewrites are more than a name swap because the plain\nswap would have been untrue: the reset + component stylesheet pair becomes the\none `@tecton/react/styles.css` Tecton ships, and a comment naming the cascade\nlayer says what the layer is, because Tecton''s own stylesheet keeps upstream''s\nlayer name.\n\nOne file is deliberately left naming upstream: the i18n example overrides the\nmessage id `@astryx.selector.placeholder`. That id is the library''s, not prose;\nrewriting it would leave an example that reads right and overrides nothing. It\nis in the log with that reason.\n\nLucide''s `size={n}` is now translated to `width={n} height={n}` rather than\ndropped — a Tecton glyph has no `size`, but it has both of those, so the 25\nicons in the theme showcase draw at the size the example drew them.\n\nThe log gains the two new sections and, in its Notes, the list of subpaths the\nexamples import beyond a component module — the surface `@tecton/react` has to\ncover for them to compile, ready to check a generator against.\n\nStill 646/646 blocks and 53/53 page templates, no drift, and the temporary\ntypecheck harness reports no errors over all 699 ported files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JWM57sS5nw57y7RDQZBBhn\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKR4fUgo\nZtn6QBdeu4HhWVFri/wCegNM0xNV7UUmmIEq2/vdFxSI9qshDpToUe/kE0ZyEbbDNDKCJLIJeIHG\nXQM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T04:49:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commit/fa75a6984ec3ad792f9280ae7e3b44ca5a10b5fe","node_id":"C_kwDOUh2LgdoAKGZhNzVhNjk4NGVjM2FkNzkyZjkyODBhZTdlM2I0NGNhNWExMGI1ZmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commit/cd45135230aa978e599c35cb5d0aa2a3f2592c59","sha":"cd45135230aa978e599c35cb5d0aa2a3f2592c59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/cd45135230aa978e599c35cb5d0aa2a3f2592c59"}],"sha":"fa75a6984ec3ad792f9280ae7e3b44ca5a10b5fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/fa75a6984ec3ad792f9280ae7e3b44ca5a10b5fe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/7d66b458275a124dbeef07314d97b84cee11ce4c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T04:36:02Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T04:36:02Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Port the consumer fixtures and the upgrade path to the new surface\n\nThe four fixtures now use the component system''s own names and props —\nCard/Heading/Text/VStack in place of Panel, TextInput in place of TextField,\nDropdownMenu in place of Menu, glyph components in place of icon-name strings.\n`pnpm check:mfe` passes: 12/12.\n\nTwo harness facts changed with the package, and the spec says so rather than\nbeing made to agree:\n\n- Version B''s derivation moves the card''s padding in the THEME layer, because\n  that is where every Tecton rule lives now. A per-component decision is a\n  cross-version contract in exactly the way a token is, and the split and\n  cascade tests measure that instead of per-version atomic classes.\n- Toasts are the component system''s `useToast`, whose body is a ReactNode and\n  therefore cannot cross from one copy''s React to another''s. One viewport per\n  copy, each showing what it raised; the cross-copy data bus went with the\n  Tecton-owned hook that fed it.\n\nTwo more subpaths are published straight from the vendored files, with no\nmodule in between: `./theme/tokens.stylex`, because StyleX has to see the real\ndefineVars call site, and `./locales/*.json`, because JSON has nothing to wrap\nit in. Both are generated and drift-checked like the rest, and the build now\nverifies that every export target resolves, not just the stylesheets.\n\n`scripts/upgrade-astryx.mjs` regenerates the subpath modules and the README\nbefore the build (which checks them) and re-ports the documentation examples\nafter it, tolerating a missing port script with a message rather than failing.\n`scripts/verify-registry.mjs` derives its version B the same way the harness\ndoes.\n\nThe theme''s custom variants and text types move from an internal `.d.ts` into\na published module, so `variant=\"text-only\"` and `type=\"mediumData\"`\ntype-check for a consumer and not only inside this package.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JWM57sS5nw57y7RDQZBBhn","tree":{"sha":"674499a315f28ff8477478dd3a512b63d2987683","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/trees/674499a315f28ff8477478dd3a512b63d2987683"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/commits/7d66b458275a124dbeef07314d97b84cee11ce4c","verification":{"payload":"tree 674499a315f28ff8477478dd3a512b63d2987683\nparent a04fdd5cf8b986bfc717697c24c732eee9424323\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789878962 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789878962 +0000\n\nPort the consumer fixtures and the upgrade path to the new surface\n\nThe four fixtures now use the component system''s own names and props —\nCard/Heading/Text/VStack in place of Panel, TextInput in place of TextField,\nDropdownMenu in place of Menu, glyph components in place of icon-name strings.\n`pnpm check:mfe` passes: 12/12.\n\nTwo harness facts changed with the package, and the spec says so rather than\nbeing made to agree:\n\n- Version B''s derivation moves the card''s padding in the THEME layer, because\n  that is where every Tecton rule lives now. A per-component decision is a\n  cross-version contract in exactly the way a token is, and the split and\n  cascade tests measure that instead of per-version atomic classes.\n- Toasts are the component system''s `useToast`, whose body is a ReactNode and\n  therefore cannot cross from one copy''s React to another''s. One viewport per\n  copy, each showing what it raised; the cross-copy data bus went with the\n  Tecton-owned hook that fed it.\n\nTwo more subpaths are published straight from the vendored files, with no\nmodule in between: `./theme/tokens.stylex`, because StyleX has to see the real\ndefineVars call site, and `./locales/*.json`, because JSON has nothing to wrap\nit in. Both are generated and drift-checked like the rest, and the build now\nverifies that every export target resolves, not just the stylesheets.\n\n`scripts/upgrade-astryx.mjs` regenerates the subpath modules and the README\nbefore the build (which checks them) and re-ports the documentation examples\nafter it, tolerating a missing port script with a message rather than failing.\n`scripts/verify-registry.mjs` derives its version B the same way the harness\ndoes.\n\nThe theme''s custom variants and text types move from an internal `.d.ts` into\na published module, so `variant=\"text-only\"` and `type=\"mediumData\"`\ntype-check for a consumer and not only inside this package.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JWM57sS5nw57y7RDQZBBhn\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJeG49Hq\nuZHCdNJwkDWGV4bTdhiVURqxI6HLOKgGQkq8RrnB6/2LoaKB295m6nXKEbXdaIqfJtEhND4w470o\nogM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T04:49:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commit/7d66b458275a124dbeef07314d97b84cee11ce4c","node_id":"C_kwDOUh2LgdoAKDdkNjZiNDU4Mjc1YTEyNGRiZWVmMDczMTRkOTdiODRjZWUxMWNlNGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commit/a04fdd5cf8b986bfc717697c24c732eee9424323","sha":"a04fdd5cf8b986bfc717697c24c732eee9424323","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/a04fdd5cf8b986bfc717697c24c732eee9424323"}],"sha":"7d66b458275a124dbeef07314d97b84cee11ce4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/7d66b458275a124dbeef07314d97b84cee11ce4c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/cd45135230aa978e599c35cb5d0aa2a3f2592c59/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T04:30:54Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T04:30:54Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Port the upstream examples into the docs app by rewriting their imports\n\n`@tecton/react` re-exports `@astryxdesign/core` one for one, so an example\nneeds no translation — which is what the previous port got wrong, inventing\ncomponent names and dropping 192 files along the way. This one rewrites import\nlines and nothing else, and carries all 699 files across: 646 blocks and 53\npage templates, into apps/docs/examples.\n\n  ''@astryxdesign/core/X''  ->  ''@tecton/react/X''\n  heroicons / lucide      ->  Tecton glyph components from ''@tecton/react/icons''\n  export default function ->  export function, named for its file\n  the Meta copyright line ->  one THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md at the repository root\n\nDoc objects come over verbatim, with `@astryxdesign/core`, `Astryx` and\n`astryx` rewritten inside their strings and an `id` or `slug` added so a page\ncan find the file the doc describes. `react`, `recharts` and `@stylexjs/stylex`\nare left alone and added to the docs app''s dependencies.\n\nEverything the port changed is in docs/engineering/ported-examples.log with the\nfile it happened to: 582 glyph substitutions, 66 renamed exports, 25 stripped\nprops (lucide''s `size`, which a Tecton glyph does not take) and the one file\nthat needed a hand-written rule — the settings dialog''s nested theme, which\nbecomes a nested `TectonProvider`.\n\n`pnpm examples:port` rewrites the directory; `pnpm examples:check` re-runs the\nport in memory and fails on drift, so a hand edit or an upstream bump cannot\npass unnoticed. apps/docs/scripts/port-examples.tsconfig.json is a temporary\nharness that typechecks all 699 ported files against upstream''s own types —\nwhat the reworked package will publish — and reports no errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JWM57sS5nw57y7RDQZBBhn","tree":{"sha":"6085680a447a65cb72411537032f11ae7a54e8b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/trees/6085680a447a65cb72411537032f11ae7a54e8b6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/commits/cd45135230aa978e599c35cb5d0aa2a3f2592c59","verification":{"payload":"tree 6085680a447a65cb72411537032f11ae7a54e8b6\nparent 365bc4a0c3afe32dd4efcc944ced9575cf45e5fb\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789878654 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789878654 +0000\n\nPort the upstream examples into the docs app by rewriting their imports\n\n`@tecton/react` re-exports `@astryxdesign/core` one for one, so an example\nneeds no translation — which is what the previous port got wrong, inventing\ncomponent names and dropping 192 files along the way. This one rewrites import\nlines and nothing else, and carries all 699 files across: 646 blocks and 53\npage templates, into apps/docs/examples.\n\n  ''@astryxdesign/core/X''  ->  ''@tecton/react/X''\n  heroicons / lucide      ->  Tecton glyph components from ''@tecton/react/icons''\n  export default function ->  export function, named for its file\n  the Meta copyright line ->  one THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md at the repository root\n\nDoc objects come over verbatim, with `@astryxdesign/core`, `Astryx` and\n`astryx` rewritten inside their strings and an `id` or `slug` added so a page\ncan find the file the doc describes. `react`, `recharts` and `@stylexjs/stylex`\nare left alone and added to the docs app''s dependencies.\n\nEverything the port changed is in docs/engineering/ported-examples.log with the\nfile it happened to: 582 glyph substitutions, 66 renamed exports, 25 stripped\nprops (lucide''s `size`, which a Tecton glyph does not take) and the one file\nthat needed a hand-written rule — the settings dialog''s nested theme, which\nbecomes a nested `TectonProvider`.\n\n`pnpm examples:port` rewrites the directory; `pnpm examples:check` re-runs the\nport in memory and fails on drift, so a hand edit or an upstream bump cannot\npass unnoticed. apps/docs/scripts/port-examples.tsconfig.json is a temporary\nharness that typechecks all 699 ported files against upstream''s own types —\nwhat the reworked package will publish — and reports no errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JWM57sS5nw57y7RDQZBBhn\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQA3Xqb/B\nB1Twbph2UXgcnKXv26E4i7zS802CbwYl+TltNFKgqgjhclAsB78x4sL9y+BXogBhGyjfMgc45n5K\n9AA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T04:49:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commit/cd45135230aa978e599c35cb5d0aa2a3f2592c59","node_id":"C_kwDOUh2LgdoAKGNkNDUxMzUyMzBhYTk3OGU1OTljMzVjYjVkMGFhMmEzZjI1OTJjNTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commit/365bc4a0c3afe32dd4efcc944ced9575cf45e5fb","sha":"365bc4a0c3afe32dd4efcc944ced9575cf45e5fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/365bc4a0c3afe32dd4efcc944ced9575cf45e5fb"}],"sha":"cd45135230aa978e599c35cb5d0aa2a3f2592c59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/cd45135230aa978e599c35cb5d0aa2a3f2592c59"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/a04fdd5cf8b986bfc717697c24c732eee9424323/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T04:23:27Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T04:23:27Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Theme: read the overrides against the component API, and test the surface\n\nThe overrides themselves are unchanged — no token value moves — but several\ncomments described a mapping onto components that no longer exist. They now\nname the component they target and say what a custom variant is: another value\nfor a prop the component already has, declared through defineTheme, not a new\ncomponent.\n\nTwo new test files:\n\n- `src/__tests__/surface.test.ts` — every named export of the component system\n  is exported from `@tecton/react` by the SAME reference, every generated\n  subpath re-exports its module by reference, `@tecton/react/theme` carries\n  both halves with no name in common, and the only names Tecton adds are the\n  provider, configureTectonRoot and the theme''s six.\n- `src/__tests__/smoke.test.tsx` — Button (both theme custom variants),\n  TextInput, an open Dialog, Table, TabList and Selector rendered inside\n  TectonProvider, each under the Tecton theme attribute.\n\nTectonProvider loses the toast bus and keeps the root registry: the toast API\nis the component system''s `useToast` now, which resolves its viewport from the\nlayer provider, so the provider mounts one and the data bus that fed Tecton''s\nown hook has no caller left.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JWM57sS5nw57y7RDQZBBhn","tree":{"sha":"e15091e4405c5637eda82d243ec17288271deba9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/trees/e15091e4405c5637eda82d243ec17288271deba9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/commits/a04fdd5cf8b986bfc717697c24c732eee9424323","verification":{"payload":"tree e15091e4405c5637eda82d243ec17288271deba9\nparent 5ed997ceab5647a2c0a2ab63e2cf1d66a13691f1\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789878207 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789878207 +0000\n\nTheme: read the overrides against the component API, and test the surface\n\nThe overrides themselves are unchanged — no token value moves — but several\ncomments described a mapping onto components that no longer exist. They now\nname the component they target and say what a custom variant is: another value\nfor a prop the component already has, declared through defineTheme, not a new\ncomponent.\n\nTwo new test files:\n\n- `src/__tests__/surface.test.ts` — every named export of the component system\n  is exported from `@tecton/react` by the SAME reference, every generated\n  subpath re-exports its module by reference, `@tecton/react/theme` carries\n  both halves with no name in common, and the only names Tecton adds are the\n  provider, configureTectonRoot and the theme''s six.\n- `src/__tests__/smoke.test.tsx` — Button (both theme custom variants),\n  TextInput, an open Dialog, Table, TabList and Selector rendered inside\n  TectonProvider, each under the Tecton theme attribute.\n\nTectonProvider loses the toast bus and keeps the root registry: the toast API\nis the component system''s `useToast` now, which resolves its viewport from the\nlayer provider, so the provider mounts one and the data bus that fed Tecton''s\nown hook has no caller left.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JWM57sS5nw57y7RDQZBBhn\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQA0tM0Ks\nIltQAJMmY0nnypk/gW5FwtQgwsbKEG17x2sMOtcG6Rm6dfnxS24qGo05q15oK/zvyIpRBYFqunGc\nIw8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T04:49:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commit/a04fdd5cf8b986bfc717697c24c732eee9424323","node_id":"C_kwDOUh2LgdoAKGEwNGZkZDVjZjhiOTg2YmZjNzE3Njk3YzI0YzczMmVlZTk0MjQzMjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commit/5ed997ceab5647a2c0a2ab63e2cf1d66a13691f1","sha":"5ed997ceab5647a2c0a2ab63e2cf1d66a13691f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/5ed997ceab5647a2c0a2ab63e2cf1d66a13691f1"}],"sha":"a04fdd5cf8b986bfc717697c24c732eee9424323","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/a04fdd5cf8b986bfc717697c24c732eee9424323"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/5ed997ceab5647a2c0a2ab63e2cf1d66a13691f1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T04:18:37Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T04:18:37Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Publish the component system as it is, under Tecton''s name\n\nThe 48 hand-written Tecton components and the 132 generated pass-through\nwrappers are gone. What replaces them is nothing: `@tecton/react` re-exports\nthe component system whole — same names, same props, same documentation — and\nTecton is the theme applied to it.\n\n- `src/index.ts` is `export * from` the component system, plus TectonProvider,\n  configureTectonRoot and the theme''s public API. No renames, so no conflicts.\n- Every module in the component system''s exports map is published at the same\n  path under `@tecton/react/`, generated by `scripts/generate-modules.mjs`\n  together with `package.json#exports` — 118 subpaths, with `--check` for\n  drift in the build and in `pnpm check`.\n- `@tecton/react/theme` is Tecton''s theme *and* the theme runtime; no name in\n  one collides with the other, so nothing upstream is unreachable.\n- `@tecton/react/icons` is the 131 glyph components, `tectonIconNames` and\n  `tectonIconRegistry`. The invented `<Icon name>` wrapper and `renderIcon`\n  are gone; the theme''s own registry is untouched.\n- The build drops the wrapper check, adds the module check, and scrubs the\n  vendored declarations'' comments and import specifiers — never a\n  string-literal type, an identifier or a `.js` file.\n- The five mentions that survive that scrub are string-literal values the\n  runtime and the stylesheet depend on; they are listed in the surface guard\n  with the reason each one has to stay, and a stale entry fails the check.\n- Tecton now styles no component of its own, so the StyleX extract is empty.\n  The step and the transform stay; the assertions read what is true.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JWM57sS5nw57y7RDQZBBhn","tree":{"sha":"c4d078e310ec1bb6ba3ef689ffdaa36b4012f951","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/trees/c4d078e310ec1bb6ba3ef689ffdaa36b4012f951"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/commits/5ed997ceab5647a2c0a2ab63e2cf1d66a13691f1","verification":{"payload":"tree c4d078e310ec1bb6ba3ef689ffdaa36b4012f951\nparent 365bc4a0c3afe32dd4efcc944ced9575cf45e5fb\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789877917 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789877917 +0000\n\nPublish the component system as it is, under Tecton''s name\n\nThe 48 hand-written Tecton components and the 132 generated pass-through\nwrappers are gone. What replaces them is nothing: `@tecton/react` re-exports\nthe component system whole — same names, same props, same documentation — and\nTecton is the theme applied to it.\n\n- `src/index.ts` is `export * from` the component system, plus TectonProvider,\n  configureTectonRoot and the theme''s public API. No renames, so no conflicts.\n- Every module in the component system''s exports map is published at the same\n  path under `@tecton/react/`, generated by `scripts/generate-modules.mjs`\n  together with `package.json#exports` — 118 subpaths, with `--check` for\n  drift in the build and in `pnpm check`.\n- `@tecton/react/theme` is Tecton''s theme *and* the theme runtime; no name in\n  one collides with the other, so nothing upstream is unreachable.\n- `@tecton/react/icons` is the 131 glyph components, `tectonIconNames` and\n  `tectonIconRegistry`. The invented `<Icon name>` wrapper and `renderIcon`\n  are gone; the theme''s own registry is untouched.\n- The build drops the wrapper check, adds the module check, and scrubs the\n  vendored declarations'' comments and import specifiers — never a\n  string-literal type, an identifier or a `.js` file.\n- The five mentions that survive that scrub are string-literal values the\n  runtime and the stylesheet depend on; they are listed in the surface guard\n  with the reason each one has to stay, and a stale entry fails the check.\n- Tecton now styles no component of its own, so the StyleX extract is empty.\n  The step and the transform stay; the assertions read what is true.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JWM57sS5nw57y7RDQZBBhn\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQITb8kjD\nVKVVWARPdsAwB/KSal0J6auxyPR660lu6tBBxoLultLHwxhZpSYps7fyW+FBaBxEfBojSN/TkM1d\nNgk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T04:49:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.gi