"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Phase 2: the Tecton component surface, icons and documentation guards\n\n47 components and useToast over the upstream library with Tecton names and\nprops, four Tecton-owned StyleX components (Panel, ColorSwatch, circular\nProgress, Icon), 131 generated icons from design/icons, a .doc.mjs and\nexamples per component, a docs-drift check (TypeScript compiler API), and a\nconsumer-surface check that walks every exported subpath''s declarations.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JWM57sS5nw57y7RDQZBBhn","tree":{"sha":"f9442d4335b759bf880840f79e4f5a70fd9b28d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/trees/f9442d4335b759bf880840f79e4f5a70fd9b28d3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/commits/8edd6b195813bd3d86e4bd8194f91c03ac6d93ea","verification":{"payload":"tree f9442d4335b759bf880840f79e4f5a70fd9b28d3\nparent 8fb9be144cf420026eb03131a3375c1c269a52b5\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789867141 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789867141 +0000\n\nPhase 2: the Tecton component surface, icons and documentation guards\n\n47 components and useToast over the upstream library with Tecton names and\nprops, four Tecton-owned StyleX components (Panel, ColorSwatch, circular\nProgress, Icon), 131 generated icons from design/icons, a .doc.mjs and\nexamples per component, a docs-drift check (TypeScript compiler API), and a\nconsumer-surface check that walks every exported subpath''s declarations.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JWM57sS5nw57y7RDQZBBhn\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEsyJlQf\nY7koJnFldbrkNHTRr+cU/QI9d8UaArfmo/3Ht+F+qjaGCkSQz+eUhkLRLpvtR4L+fSYOnDXgaseB\nsQ0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T01:19:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commit/8edd6b195813bd3d86e4bd8194f91c03ac6d93ea","node_id":"C_kwDOUh2LgdoAKDhlZGQ2YjE5NTgxM2JkM2Q4NmU0YmQ4MTk0ZjkxYzAzYWM2ZDkzZWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commit/8fb9be144cf420026eb03131a3375c1c269a52b5","sha":"8fb9be144cf420026eb03131a3375c1c269a52b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/8fb9be144cf420026eb03131a3375c1c269a52b5"}],"sha":"8edd6b195813bd3d86e4bd8194f91c03ac6d93ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/8edd6b195813bd3d86e4bd8194f91c03ac6d93ea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/a46eb1f437b56e6b55e31e91afa1e010196355fd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T00:46:13Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T00:46:13Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Phase 3: document the multi-version model\n\n- docs/engineering/micro-frontends/README.md — the consumer-facing\n  guide: the recommended page shape (the host loads one tokens.css and\n  calls configureTectonRoot(), containers load components.css and mount\n  with scope=\"nested\"), what a host shell must do, what is unsupported\n  (cross-container layer nesting, mixed upstream majors, reaching past\n  Tecton), and the failure-mode table with a status per row. The two\n  upstream state fixes (scroll lock, layer stack) are marked approved\n  and pending a follow-up phase; the third ask (rootSync={false}) is\n  still undecided.\n- docs/engineering/build-pipeline.md — why the token manifest exists\n  (one shared theme name means coverage drift silently hands a token to\n  another version) and what each of the five stylesheet entry points is\n  for, plus the new build steps and post-checks.\n- README.md — the harness fixture and `pnpm check:mfe`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JWM57sS5nw57y7RDQZBBhn","tree":{"sha":"269bd3830b06216cc8ccc31169b4bfd4cd2107eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/trees/269bd3830b06216cc8ccc31169b4bfd4cd2107eb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/commits/a46eb1f437b56e6b55e31e91afa1e010196355fd","verification":{"payload":"tree 269bd3830b06216cc8ccc31169b4bfd4cd2107eb\nparent 0f689cff6cd31e38c56312de2e9a01f36ca5bd4d\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789865173 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789865173 +0000\n\nPhase 3: document the multi-version model\n\n- docs/engineering/micro-frontends/README.md — the consumer-facing\n  guide: the recommended page shape (the host loads one tokens.css and\n  calls configureTectonRoot(), containers load components.css and mount\n  with scope=\"nested\"), what a host shell must do, what is unsupported\n  (cross-container layer nesting, mixed upstream majors, reaching past\n  Tecton), and the failure-mode table with a status per row. The two\n  upstream state fixes (scroll lock, layer stack) are marked approved\n  and pending a follow-up phase; the third ask (rootSync={false}) is\n  still undecided.\n- docs/engineering/build-pipeline.md — why the token manifest exists\n  (one shared theme name means coverage drift silently hands a token to\n  another version) and what each of the five stylesheet entry points is\n  for, plus the new build steps and post-checks.\n- README.md — the harness fixture and `pnpm check:mfe`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JWM57sS5nw57y7RDQZBBhn\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKMqubWh\ngU/KpFhYthtS+3NWbJXx/n/4ZZ8zA7dLulwAUVGg3nlzKaMl6oX5UQRmNjqdc0AbhJ7yVbcvtELW\nZwU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T01:22:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commit/a46eb1f437b56e6b55e31e91afa1e010196355fd","node_id":"C_kwDOUh2LgdoAKGE0NmViMWY0MzdiNTZlNmI1NWUzMWU5MWFmYTFlMDEwMTk2MzU1ZmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commit/0f689cff6cd31e38c56312de2e9a01f36ca5bd4d","sha":"0f689cff6cd31e38c56312de2e9a01f36ca5bd4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/0f689cff6cd31e38c56312de2e9a01f36ca5bd4d"}],"sha":"a46eb1f437b56e6b55e31e91afa1e010196355fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/a46eb1f437b56e6b55e31e91afa1e010196355fd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/0f689cff6cd31e38c56312de2e9a01f36ca5bd4d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T00:46:13Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T00:46:13Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Phase 3: the micro-frontend harness as a workspace fixture\n\nfixtures/consumers/mfe-harness builds @tecton/react, derives a second\n\"released version\" from the built dist (three retuned theme tokens and a\nPanel whose padding moved, so its StyleX class is a different hash),\nbundles both into separate IIFEs with their own React, and drives a\ntwo-container page in Chromium.\n\nDeriving B from dist rather than patching packages/react/src in place —\nwhat the investigation harness did — keeps the worktree untouched and\nstill produces the thing that matters: two versions whose component\nrules carry different atomic class names.\n\nThe spec asserts three mitigations, the host-owns-the-tokens split, and\none recorded behaviour:\n\n  1 the <html> attributes survive a sibling unmount, and the registry\n    reports the re-assertion that did it (holders 2 -> 1, reassertions 1)\n  2 the first owning claim decides the page mode in either mount order,\n    and configureTectonRoot() beats both containers\n  3 styles-no-reset.css leaves the host <h1> byte-identical to a page\n    with no Tecton CSS, while the container stays fully themed\n  4 with tokens.css + components.css both containers resolve the host''s\n    tokens, component styles stay per-version, every sheet declares the\n    same layer order, and a container leaving does not take the root\n  5 with two complete bundles the last-loaded theme wins for every\n    container, in both load orders - recorded, not fixed\n\n`pnpm check:mfe` runs it (16 s). It stays out of `pnpm check` and\n`build:fixtures`: it rebuilds the package a second time and launches a\nbrowser. Chromium is the preinstalled one; nothing downloads a browser.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JWM57sS5nw57y7RDQZBBhn","tree":{"sha":"fde2c9a27104459473bbeec7218782f1d331da0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/trees/fde2c9a27104459473bbeec7218782f1d331da0d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/commits/0f689cff6cd31e38c56312de2e9a01f36ca5bd4d","verification":{"payload":"tree fde2c9a27104459473bbeec7218782f1d331da0d\nparent db724f2e626e5d44438efbdd9e527eb78d30b040\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789865173 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789865173 +0000\n\nPhase 3: the micro-frontend harness as a workspace fixture\n\nfixtures/consumers/mfe-harness builds @tecton/react, derives a second\n\"released version\" from the built dist (three retuned theme tokens and a\nPanel whose padding moved, so its StyleX class is a different hash),\nbundles both into separate IIFEs with their own React, and drives a\ntwo-container page in Chromium.\n\nDeriving B from dist rather than patching packages/react/src in place —\nwhat the investigation harness did — keeps the worktree untouched and\nstill produces the thing that matters: two versions whose component\nrules carry different atomic class names.\n\nThe spec asserts three mitigations, the host-owns-the-tokens split, and\none recorded behaviour:\n\n  1 the <html> attributes survive a sibling unmount, and the registry\n    reports the re-assertion that did it (holders 2 -> 1, reassertions 1)\n  2 the first owning claim decides the page mode in either mount order,\n    and configureTectonRoot() beats both containers\n  3 styles-no-reset.css leaves the host <h1> byte-identical to a page\n    with no Tecton CSS, while the container stays fully themed\n  4 with tokens.css + components.css both containers resolve the host''s\n    tokens, component styles stay per-version, every sheet declares the\n    same layer order, and a container leaving does not take the root\n  5 with two complete bundles the last-loaded theme wins for every\n    container, in both load orders - recorded, not fixed\n\n`pnpm check:mfe` runs it (16 s). It stays out of `pnpm check` and\n`build:fixtures`: it rebuilds the package a second time and launches a\nbrowser. Chromium is the preinstalled one; nothing downloads a browser.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JWM57sS5nw57y7RDQZBBhn\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQK0Kw8Ja\nGPjkX++3CbThH2exLyC/6w2FPLeTl6fmXGGKhquhmRAgHCBj7Vt9IJhIJN4allftRdJWLQdSGwnt\nnwU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T01:22:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commit/0f689cff6cd31e38c56312de2e9a01f36ca5bd4d","node_id":"C_kwDOUh2LgdoAKDBmNjg5Y2ZmNmNkMzFlMzhjNTYzMTJkZTJlOWEwMWYzNmNhNWJkNGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commit/db724f2e626e5d44438efbdd9e527eb78d30b040","sha":"db724f2e626e5d44438efbdd9e527eb78d30b040","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/db724f2e626e5d44438efbdd9e527eb78d30b040"}],"sha":"0f689cff6cd31e38c56312de2e9a01f36ca5bd4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/0f689cff6cd31e38c56312de2e9a01f36ca5bd4d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/db724f2e626e5d44438efbdd9e527eb78d30b040/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T00:33:28Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T00:33:28Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Phase 3: token-coverage manifest and split stylesheet entry points\n\nUnder one shared theme name every version''s theme.css targets the same\n@scope in the same layer, so a token one version overrides and another\ndoes not is answered for BOTH of them by whichever sheet has a rule for\nit (analysis.md F2/F3). theme-token-manifest.json pins the 260 custom\nproperties the built theme must set; the build fails on any omission or\nunexpected extra, and --update-manifest regenerates it on purpose.\n\nThe build now writes five entry points out of the same bytes, each\nopening with the same @layer reset, astryx-base, astryx-theme statement:\n\n  styles.css                 the whole bundle (unchanged)\n  styles-no-reset.css        minus the reset layer, for hosts that own\n                             their own reset\n  tokens.css                 the theme layer only — the host''s half of\n                             the micro-frontend split\n  components.css             reset + foundation + Tecton components,\n                             no theme — the container''s half\n  components-no-reset.css    components.css without the reset\n\nPost-build checks: every entry point declares the layer order, the\nreset-free ones contain no @layer reset block, tokens.css has no\n.astryx/.tecton rule outside the theme @scope, components.css carries no\n[data-astryx-theme= scope, and every CSS export path resolves.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JWM57sS5nw57y7RDQZBBhn","tree":{"sha":"e09b6f6c6d757806e6430a89f764177d7cda0cf7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/trees/e09b6f6c6d757806e6430a89f764177d7cda0cf7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/commits/db724f2e626e5d44438efbdd9e527eb78d30b040","verification":{"payload":"tree e09b6f6c6d757806e6430a89f764177d7cda0cf7\nparent 3c48ed715aed1a9c182b7e14407b5fd2d624eca0\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789864408 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789864408 +0000\n\nPhase 3: token-coverage manifest and split stylesheet entry points\n\nUnder one shared theme name every version''s theme.css targets the same\n@scope in the same layer, so a token one version overrides and another\ndoes not is answered for BOTH of them by whichever sheet has a rule for\nit (analysis.md F2/F3). theme-token-manifest.json pins the 260 custom\nproperties the built theme must set; the build fails on any omission or\nunexpected extra, and --update-manifest regenerates it on purpose.\n\nThe build now writes five entry points out of the same bytes, each\nopening with the same @layer reset, astryx-base, astryx-theme statement:\n\n  styles.css                 the whole bundle (unchanged)\n  styles-no-reset.css        minus the reset layer, for hosts that own\n                             their own reset\n  tokens.css                 the theme layer only — the host''s half of\n                             the micro-frontend split\n  components.css             reset + foundation + Tecton components,\n                             no theme — the container''s half\n  components-no-reset.css    components.css without the reset\n\nPost-build checks: every entry point declares the layer order, the\nreset-free ones contain no @layer reset block, tokens.css has no\n.astryx/.tecton rule outside the theme @scope, components.css carries no\n[data-astryx-theme= scope, and every CSS export path resolves.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JWM57sS5nw57y7RDQZBBhn\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBWrONdv\nW2s6BrbQC2Fd1jOeTZfz82NXmdlIpmpo2pveeYRE16/oQhN5DzPNh5zQGEnmGfGMpcKnjULDhxuO\nSAg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T01:22:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commit/db724f2e626e5d44438efbdd9e527eb78d30b040","node_id":"C_kwDOUh2LgdoAKGRiNzI0ZjJlNjI2ZTVkNDQ0MzhlZmJkZDllNTI3ZWI3OGQzMGIwNDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commit/3c48ed715aed1a9c182b7e14407b5fd2d624eca0","sha":"3c48ed715aed1a9c182b7e14407b5fd2d624eca0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/3c48ed715aed1a9c182b7e14407b5fd2d624eca0"}],"sha":"db724f2e626e5d44438efbdd9e527eb78d30b040","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/db724f2e626e5d44438efbdd9e527eb78d30b040"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/commits/3c48ed715aed1a9c182b7e14407b5fd2d624eca0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T00:33:18Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T00:33:18Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Phase 3: ref-counted root ownership and TectonProvider scope\n\nSeveral copies of @tecton/react on one page fight over <html data-theme>\nand <html data-astryx-theme>: the upstream Theme removes both on any\nunmount, with no ref count, so the first container to leave strips them\nfor everybody (measured, analysis.md F4/F5).\n\n- src/runtime/rootRegistry.ts: a Symbol.for(''tecton.rootOwnership/v1'')\n  record on document, shared by every copy. Ref-counted claims, first\n  owning claim decides, non-owning claims (scope=\"nested\") only keep the\n  attributes alive, a MutationObserver reverts foreign writes, the last\n  release cleans up. Versioned key and version field; an older record is\n  used as it is rather than replaced. SSR-safe.\n- TectonProvider gains scope?: ''root'' | ''nested'' (default ''root'') and\n  takes the matching claim. A single provider behaves exactly as before.\n- configureTectonRoot({mode, themeName}) lets a host shell own the page\n  before any container loads; exported from the barrel.\n\n24 new tests: registry rules (two claims, foreign removal re-asserted,\ndisagreement warned once in dev, last release cleans up, older record\ntolerated, SSR) and the provider wiring on a real document.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JWM57sS5nw57y7RDQZBBhn","tree":{"sha":"ee5a474522c307afc09d514c02f54767c868d4bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/trees/ee5a474522c307afc09d514c02f54767c868d4bd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/tecton-astryx/git/commits/3c48ed715aed1a9c182b7e14407b5fd2d624eca0","verification":{"payload":"tree ee5a474522c307afc09d514c02f54767c868d4bd\nparent 8fb9be144cf420026eb03131a3375c1c269a52b5\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789864398 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789864398 +0000\n\nPhase 3: ref-counted root ownership and TectonProvider scope\n\nSeveral copies of @tecton/react on one page fight over <html data-theme>\nand <html data-astryx-theme>: the upstream Theme removes both on any\nunmount, with no ref count, so the first container to leave strips them\nfor everybody (measured, analysis.md F4/F5).\n\n- src/runtime/rootRegistry.ts: a Symbol.for(''tecton.rootOwnership/v1'')\n  record on document, shared by every copy. Ref-counted claims, first\n  owning claim decides, non-owning claims (scope=\"nested\") only keep the\n  attributes alive, a MutationObserver reverts foreign writes, the last\n  release cleans up. Versioned key and version field; an older record is\n  used as it is rather than replaced. SSR-safe.\n- TectonProvider gains scope?: ''root'' | ''nested'' (default ''root'') and\n  takes the matching claim. A single provider behaves exactly as before.\n- configureTectonRoot({mode, themeName}) lets a host shell own the page\n  before any container loads; exported from the barrel.\n\n24 new tests: registry rules (two claims, foreign removal re-asserted,\ndisag