ived_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Blue-Mink/New-Store/commit/1f6b04c5dbfdbf8907e36015bb7a9d8a9e7bada1","node_id":"C_kwDOUh-77doAKDFmNmIwNGM1ZGJmZGJmODkwN2UzNjAxNWJiN2E5ZDhhOWU3YmFkYTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Blue-Mink/New-Store/commit/9215ae5cd1127ce336e6e563ef4f0cd65f6e31bf","sha":"9215ae5cd1127ce336e6e563ef4f0cd65f6e31bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Blue-Mink/New-Store/commits/9215ae5cd1127ce336e6e563ef4f0cd65f6e31bf"}],"sha":"1f6b04c5dbfdbf8907e36015bb7a9d8a9e7bada1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Blue-Mink/New-Store/commits/1f6b04c5dbfdbf8907e36015bb7a9d8a9e7bada1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22893221?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/conversun","id":22893221,"login":"conversun","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyODkzMjIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Blue-Mink/New-Store/commits/9215ae5cd1127ce336e6e563ef4f0cd65f6e31bf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T15:20:20Z","email":"conversun@gmail.com","name":"conversun"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T15:20:20Z","email":"conversun@gmail.com","name":"conversun"},"message":"fix: validate fpk content, reconcile installed state, respect the safe area\n\nThree user-facing dead-ends, one per fix:\n\n- The downloader rejected astrbot 4.27.4 (an 8483-byte docker fpk) with\n  ''downloaded file too small'': the 10 KiB size floor assumed every fpk\n  carries binaries. Validate the archive instead — gzip stream wrapping a\n  tar with a manifest entry — which also catches full-size HTML error\n  pages no size floor can (fnos-apps#284).\n\n- ScanInstalled aborted on the FIRST unparseable /var/apps manifest, which\n  flipped the whole catalog to not-installed; the store then offered 安装\n  on apps the daemon had registered and dead-ended users on ''已安装，请使\n  用更新功能'' with an empty update tab. Skip bad manifests individually,\n  and fold the daemon''s installed list into the registry as the authority\n  on whether an app exists (fnos-apps#280 daidai-panel, #281 mihomo).\n\n- viewport-fit=cover plus safe-area-inset-bottom padding on the mobile\n  drawer footer keeps 设置 above the Android gesture/nav bar\n  (conversun/fnos-store#7).","tree":{"sha":"0d22f81a403a9e63adfa14c495ce8a107269e452","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Blue-Mink/New-Store/git/trees/0d22f81a403a9e63adfa14c495ce8a107269e452"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Blue-Mink/New-Store/git/commits/9215ae5cd1127ce336e6e563ef4f0cd65f6e31bf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22893221?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/conversun","id":22893221,"login":"conversun","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyODkzMjIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Blue-Mink/New-Store/commit/9215ae5cd1127ce336e6e563ef4f0cd65f6e31bf","node_id":"C_kwDOUh-77doAKDkyMTVhZTVjZDExMjdjZTMzNmU2ZTU2M2VmNGYwY2Q2NWY2ZTMxYmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Blue-Mink/New-Store/commit/b07f41e2e742d80d4f147288368b10ffed754d67","sha":"b07f41e2e742d80d4f147288368b10ffed754d67","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Blue-Mink/New-Store/commits/b07f41e2e742d80d4f147288368b10ffed754d67"}],"sha":"9215ae5cd1127ce336e6e563ef4f0cd65f6e31bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Blue-Mink/New-Store/commits/9215ae5cd1127ce336e6e563ef4f0cd65f6e31bf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22893221?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/conversun","id":22893221,"login":"conversun","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyODkzMjIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Blue-Mink/New-Store/commits/b07f41e2e742d80d4f147288368b10ffed754d67/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T03:21:03Z","email":"conversun@gmail.com","name":"conversun"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T03:21:03Z","email":"conversun@gmail.com","name":"conversun"},"message":"chore: bump version to 1.9.3","tree":{"sha":"4c69839c31848665c0286cafb1d3ff371fb36cf6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Blue-Mink/New-Store/git/trees/4c69839c31848665c0286cafb1d3ff371fb36cf6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Blue-Mink/New-Store/git/commits/b07f41e2e742d80d4f147288368b10ffed754d67","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22893221?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/conversun","id":22893221,"login":"conversun","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyODkzMjIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Blue-Mink/New-Store/commit/b07f41e2e742d80d4f147288368b10ffed754d67","node_id":"C_kwDOUh-77doAKGIwN2Y0MWUyZTc0MmQ4MGQ0ZjE0NzI4ODM2OGIxMGZmZWQ3NTRkNjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Blue-Mink/New-Store/commit/03bdde42c4d712798412d7bf6df4c260f35b8766","sha":"03bdde42c4d712798412d7bf6df4c260f35b8766","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Blue-Mink/New-Store/commits/03bdde42c4d712798412d7bf6df4c260f35b8766"}],"sha":"b07f41e2e742d80d4f147288368b10ffed754d67","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Blue-Mink/New-Store/commits/b07f41e2e742d80d4f147288368b10ffed754d67"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22893221?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/conversun","id":22893221,"login":"conversun","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyODkzMjIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Blue-Mink/New-Store/commits/03bdde42c4d712798412d7bf6df4c260f35b8766/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T18:19:11Z","email":"conversun@gmail.com","name":"conversun"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T18:19:11Z","email":"conversun@gmail.com","name":"conversun"},"message":"fix: never report an unobservable daemon task as a failure\n\nOnce a mutating request may have reached the app-center daemon, losing\nsight of it is not the same as it failing — the daemon keeps working after\nwe stop watching. Conflating the two turns a completed upgrade into a\nuser-visible error and invites a retry that mutates the same app twice.\n\nwaitTask now returns success, definite failure, or ErrTaskOutcomeUnknown:\n\n  - Status polls are observational, so failing to READ one no longer aborts\n    the operation. It rides out a 90s outage instead. StageFpk already did\n    this for its own poll (2a551b3, #247); the task poll covers far more\n    wall-clock time and needs it more. The budget is a duration, not a\n    consecutive-failure count — the poll interval, not the number of\n    failures, decides how much real downtime gets covered.\n  - An unknown taskId is indeterminate. Measured on 1.2.0505,\n    /rpc/v1/common/status answers code 0 with status 5 for a task it does\n    not know, which fell through to the generic branch and surfaced as the\n    bare, actionless \"升级失败: 状态 5\". A reaped task and one lost to a\n    daemon restart are indistinguishable there, and fnOS system updates\n    restart that daemon.\n  - Cancellation and the overall timeout are indeterminate for the same\n    reason. A status the daemon does report but we do not model stays a\n    definite failure: that is the daemon giving a real answer.\n\ndaemonCall now separates the two transport failures via httptrace.\nErrDaemonUnreachable means the socket could not be dialled, so no byte was\nwritten; ErrDaemonAmbiguous means the request was already on its way.\nUninstall only falls back to the CLI on the former. On an ambiguous error\nit refuses, because the CLI path does not pin wizard_delete_data=false the\nway submitUninstall does, so a second uninstall can take the app''s data\nwith it.\n\nAlso stop leaking staged packages. The daemon unpacks every fpk into\n/volN/appcenter-downloads/<app>-<ver>-tpk and never reaps it; a test box\nhad 165 MB of them, including two full copies of an app that had since\nbeen uninstalled, on a volume at 82%. FetchWizard stages too, so merely\npreviewing an install wizard and cancelling left one behind. They are now\nremoved after a DEFINITIVELY finished install/upgrade (never on an unknown\nor failed outcome, where the task may still be reading them) and always\nafter a wizard preview, behind a guard that only touches an absolute\n.../appcenter-downloads/*-tpk since this runs as root.\n\nTwo smaller hazards found alongside:\n\n  - chooseInstallRoute gated the fresh-install fallback on the UPGRADE\n    probe, so a change to the update route could silently reroute installs\n    onto install-local. Split out DaemonInstallAvailable, which probes\n    install/info (10030 on a route that exists; a missing route answers a\n    plain-text 404 that never decodes into a DaemonError).\n  - handleGetWizard reached the daemon without taking the CLI lock, so a\n    wizard preview could stage concurrently with a live install despite the\n    pipeline assuming daemon operations are serialized. The download stays\n    outside the lock; only the staging call takes it.","tree":{"sha":"b895c064e2fbe8ff3c256b390995030f19342fb1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Blue-Mink/New-Store/git/trees/b895c064e2fbe8ff3c256b390995030f19342fb1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Blue-Mink/New-Store/git/commits/03bdde42c4d712798412d7bf6df4c260f35b8766","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22893221?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/conversun","id":22893221,"login":"conversun","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyODkzMjIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Blue-Mink/New-Store/commit/03bdde42c4d712798412d7bf6df4c260f35b8766","node_id":"C_kwDOUh-77doAKDAzYmRkZTQyYzRkNzEyNzk4NDEyZDdiZjZkZjRjMjYwZjM1Yjg3NjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Blue-Mink/New-Store/commit/b3462f9dbf4a459548b4b38cea766b1f304ab0f4","sha":"b3462f9dbf4a459548b4b38cea766b1f304ab0f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Blue-Mink/New-Store/commits/b3462f9dbf4a459548b4b38cea766b1f304ab0f4"}],"sha":"03bdde42c4d712798412d7bf6df4c260f35b8766","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Blue-Mink/New-Store/commits/03bdde42c4d712798412d7bf6df4c260f35b8766"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22893221?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/conversun","id":22893221,"login":"conversun","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyODkzMjIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/conversun","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Blue-Mink/New-Store/commits/b3462f9dbf4a459548b4b38cea766b1f304ab0f4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T18:18:38Z","email":"conversun@gmail.com","name":"conversun"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T18:18:38Z","email":"conversun@gmail.com","name":"conversun"},"message":"fix: update the store through the daemon channel, not install-local\n\nrunSelfUpdate forked a detached `appcenter-cli install-local`. That is the\nuninstall-then-reinstall path this codebase forbids for every app update\nbecause a failed reinstall destroys the app and its @appdata\n(conversun/fnos-apps#189) — pointed at the store itself, where the user is\nthen left with no store to reinstall it from. It did so immediately after\nrequireSafeUpgrade had confirmed the data-preserving channel was available,\nand then never used it.\n\nSubmit the same update/task every other update uses. Measured on fnOS\n1.2.0505: the daemon upgrades the store in place, @appdata survives\nbyte-identical, and it finishes the task after killing this process —\nbeing a separate process is exactly why it can. waitTask simply dies with\nus; the operation does not, and the frontend already polls for the restart.\n\nTwo things go away with it. The extract-to-a-temp-dir step is gone, since\nthe daemon stages the fpk itself. So is setDefaultVolume: that existed only\nto aim install-local, and mutated a GLOBAL fnOS setting to do it, whereas\nthe daemon pins the volume from the app''s own record.","tree":{"sha":"d114450f3d9387d44277e51368678df2d7e945ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Blue-Mink/New-Store/git/trees/d114450f3d9387d44277e51368678df2d7e945ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Blue-Mink/New-Store/git/commits/b3462f9dbf4a459548b4b38cea766b1f304ab0f4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com