,"gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lemcortes","id":182818850,"login":"lemcortes","node_id":"U_kgDOCuWYIg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lemcortes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lemcortes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lemcortes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lemcortes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lemcortes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lemcortes","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commit/662a152dc43a20a9f2d34e7096fbc8058a828b2b","node_id":"C_kwDOUiz2UtoAKDY2MmExNTJkYzQzYTIwYTlmMmQzNGU3MDk2ZmJjODA1OGE4MjhiMmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commit/007b8d6b7e4388085792df4b9e89891a69812b4e","sha":"007b8d6b7e4388085792df4b9e89891a69812b4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/007b8d6b7e4388085792df4b9e89891a69812b4e"}],"sha":"662a152dc43a20a9f2d34e7096fbc8058a828b2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/662a152dc43a20a9f2d34e7096fbc8058a828b2b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/87156669?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devcortes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devcortes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devcortes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devcortes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/devcortes","id":87156669,"login":"devcortes","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTU2NjY5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devcortes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devcortes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devcortes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devcortes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devcortes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/devcortes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/b39852288b73eeccd64567efc772b89cc472bba0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T06:25:52Z","email":"87156669+devcortes@users.noreply.github.com","name":"devcortes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T06:25:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Release/develop to main 20260928 (#20)\n\n* feat(e2e): playwright suite for signing feature (#8)\n\nFase 10e:\n\n* projects/signing/src/app/core/e2e-hooks.ts: install window.__signingE2E\n  when stage=''dev'' AND ?e2e=1. Exposes typed actions that bypass the\n  <video>+getUserMedia (camera) and <canvas> pointer strokes (signature\n  pad) by feeding blobs directly into the same code paths the real UI\n  uses; introspection via getState()/waitForScreen()/waitForStage();\n  debug OTP key install so request_otp echoes the plaintext code back\n  via the HMAC hatch. Zero surface in the pro bundle.\n* sign.component.ts: install hook in ngOnInit and forward the installed\n  debug key to requestOtp so the ceremony can be driven headlessly.\n* playwright.config.ts + e2e/: full suite structure\n  - fixtures/: synthetic id_front/id_back PNGs (Textract-passing) and a\n    signature PNG regenerated from the backend integration_signatures\n    helpers, kept in sync via fixtures/regenerate.sh\n  - helpers/env.ts: single-source env-var loader with a real interface\n  - helpers/backend.ts: thin API clients to register users, seed a\n    process to stage=''signature'', and open raw ceremonies via the M2M\n    service key\n  - helpers/signing-driver.ts: typed wrapper around window.__signingE2E\n  - specs/signing-standalone.spec.ts: opens a raw ceremony and drives\n    the wizard to the async boundary (worker fails on the fake PDF URL,\n    which is expected); no portal dependency\n  - specs/portal-to-payment.spec.ts: registers a user, seeds a process,\n    logs into the portal, clicks ''Firmar ahora'', drives the full\n    ceremony, returns to the portal, and asserts the auto-advance to\n    payment\n* .github/workflows/e2e.yml: manual dispatch workflow; runs against dev\n  using GH env secrets/vars. Not on the deploy critical path (worker\n  takes 30-90s per test).\n* .gitignore: e2e reports/env\n* npm scripts: e2e / e2e:headed / e2e:ui\n\nFace fixture is opt-in via SIGNATURES_TEST_FACE_PATH (privacy). Specs\ntest.skip() gracefully when missing.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs(signing): add block README + reference E2E suite from top-level (#9)\n\nFase 10f (frontend half).\n\n* projects/signing/README.md: brand new. Overview of the signing\n  micro-frontend, the two entry paths (email async / portal same-tab),\n  the server-authoritative state machine (Ceremony.stage -> local\n  screen table), the internal module layout, how to rediscover the\n  signatures API URL when the stack is recreated, security posture\n  (return_url same-origin gate, e2e hook double-gate, debug OTP key),\n  and how to run the SPA locally + tests. Explicitly points at\n  docs/signatures-v2.md $10.4 in the backend repo for the contract.\n* README.md: link the new signing/README from the blocks table.\n  Update the ''no specs yet'' aside to note that the Playwright suite\n  exists at e2e/ (repo root) precisely because it crosses two blocks;\n  points at .github/workflows/e2e.yml and e2e/README.md.\n\nNo code changes.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* chore(config): set production API endpoints\n\n* feat(testability): add stable selectors for UC2 registration validation (#12)\n\nCo-authored-by: David Cortes Bolivar <david.cortes@lemco.co>\n\n* feat(testability): add stable selectors for UC3 initiation validation\n\n* feat(testability): add stable selectors for UC3 process form validation\n\n* feat(testability): add stable selectors for UC3 stage transitions\n\n* feat(testability): add stable selectors for UC3 document validation\n\n* feat(testability): add stable selectors for UC3 signature transition\n\n* feat(testability): add stable selectors for signing ceremony entry\n\n* fix(signing): align debug OTP HMAC key encoding\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Salomon Saenz <122643656+salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: salomon <salomonsaenzg368@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: David Cortes Bolivar <david.cortes@lemco.co>","tree":{"sha":"4602c40e258d28142c4d8a4a292b4549cef2b67d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/git/trees/4602c40e258d28142c4d8a4a292b4549cef2b67d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/git/commits/b39852288b73eeccd64567efc772b89cc472bba0","verification":{"payload":"tree 4602c40e258d28142c4d8a4a292b4549cef2b67d\nparent 5a86b96c6cece4763b44342f49b7a3d0dc5424fb\nauthor devcortes <87156669+devcortes@users.noreply.github.com> 1790576752 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790576752 -0500\n\nRelease/develop to main 20260928 (#20)\n\n* feat(e2e): playwright suite for signing feature (#8)\n\nFase 10e:\n\n* projects/signing/src/app/core/e2e-hooks.ts: install window.__signingE2E\n  when stage=''dev'' AND ?e2e=1. Exposes typed actions that bypass the\n  <video>+getUserMedia (camera) and <canvas> pointer strokes (signature\n  pad) by feeding blobs directly into the same code paths the real UI\n  uses; introspection via getState()/waitForScreen()/waitForStage();\n  debug OTP key install so request_otp echoes the plaintext code back\n  via the HMAC hatch. Zero surface in the pro bundle.\n* sign.component.ts: install hook in ngOnInit and forward the installed\n  debug key to requestOtp so the ceremony can be driven headlessly.\n* playwright.config.ts + e2e/: full suite structure\n  - fixtures/: synthetic id_front/id_back PNGs (Textract-passing) and a\n    signature PNG regenerated from the backend integration_signatures\n    helpers, kept in sync via fixtures/regenerate.sh\n  - helpers/env.ts: single-source env-var loader with a real interface\n  - helpers/backend.ts: thin API clients to register users, seed a\n    process to stage=''signature'', and open raw ceremonies via the M2M\n    service key\n  - helpers/signing-driver.ts: typed wrapper around window.__signingE2E\n  - specs/signing-standalone.spec.ts: opens a raw ceremony and drives\n    the wizard to the async boundary (worker fails on the fake PDF URL,\n    which is expected); no portal dependency\n  - specs/portal-to-payment.spec.ts: registers a user, seeds a process,\n    logs into the portal, clicks ''Firmar ahora'', drives the full\n    ceremony, returns to the portal, and asserts the auto-advance to\n    payment\n* .github/workflows/e2e.yml: manual dispatch workflow; runs against dev\n  using GH env secrets/vars. Not on the deploy critical path (worker\n  takes 30-90s per test).\n* .gitignore: e2e reports/env\n* npm scripts: e2e / e2e:headed / e2e:ui\n\nFace fixture is opt-in via SIGNATURES_TEST_FACE_PATH (privacy). Specs\ntest.skip() gracefully when missing.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs(signing): add block README + reference E2E suite from top-level (#9)\n\nFase 10f (frontend half).\n\n* projects/signing/README.md: brand new. Overview of the signing\n  micro-frontend, the two entry paths (email async / portal same-tab),\n  the server-authoritative state machine (Ceremony.stage -> local\n  screen table), the internal module layout, how to rediscover the\n  signatures API URL when the stack is recreated, security posture\n  (return_url same-origin gate, e2e hook double-gate, debug OTP key),\n  and how to run the SPA locally + tests. Explicitly points at\n  docs/signatures-v2.md $10.4 in the backend repo for the contract.\n* README.md: link the new signing/README from the blocks table.\n  Update the ''no specs yet'' aside to note that the Playwright suite\n  exists at e2e/ (repo root) precisely because it crosses two blocks;\n  points at .github/workflows/e2e.yml and e2e/README.md.\n\nNo code changes.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* chore(config): set production API endpoints\n\n* feat(testability): add stable selectors for UC2 registration validation (#12)\n\nCo-authored-by: David Cortes Bolivar <david.cortes@lemco.co>\n\n* feat(testability): add stable selectors for UC3 initiation validation\n\n* feat(testability): add stable selectors for UC3 process form validation\n\n* feat(testability): add stable selectors for UC3 stage transitions\n\n* feat(testability): add stable selectors for UC3 document validation\n\n* feat(testability): add stable selectors for UC3 signature transition\n\n* feat(testability): add stable selectors for signing ceremony entry\n\n* fix(signing): align debug OTP HMAC key encoding\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Salomon Saenz <122643656+salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: salomon <salomonsaenzg368@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: David Cortes Bolivar <david.cortes@lemco.co>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqughwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjlMQAJjtrIuaF3yH2WP9r+6XPB5X\nlmwoV91YvhoZRM2EwMjy8Q25UtipX6JNTnW46LTSpZYb0zUbRhYxqYMDR4lVLGEy\nPcaFmjW4msCBZ6LPR1iGwGcO33oWu8M6k2WRL3q1R1MSyBoUxlcfDcU4K6WR7UQ6\nSpmi/KXjgkA+xt8Mubvwc59UZ3uUbJU8V7Ksz6Sk2Cop7HSCxBWqUwqRD/70VJ6q\njzNuZY4zmuG9rt9hirv279hqDGDremOzRqEUJDwH0HdDZtXvLHbsuOHjUEw5icL9\nedgGkvKVRmxcJuY+UeZS58+GXHzvobVnvHrlFxRdM4W0MkLlVcfHse/LxZy9P/Ns\nDg4PESy8v6+TS45lbsu3RsK12GBmwYDtewf6D41d79zRuxU4sOsvmnFFr93G06N1\njgGp5mAb1LGFO/DU4zFyT89UCGaPbWSwEfDS/PJ6rtDXREEXqMinAyP1cVqQaCWx\nGMnNQNZ289D4r8rBMIgRMudJfFi/ywIewfOuuxClTkiKI6dEFfkaEeehnyfPQxgZ\nmhejLZi0QzG4PrTUTI703vCeKh2Go9Lhw3iw8r8xwVd79v5WMhlOkhU3hkXXEzan\n89/ThG9/wDaVbyPFgFxHCrEmbVj1Akq/XzaOiKN0Wq+