owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lemcortes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lemcortes","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commit/7cee6ac5049991dc28e8aa2a5ae9574afc2a3597","node_id":"C_kwDOUiz2UtoAKDdjZWU2YWM1MDQ5OTkxZGMyOGU4YWEyYTVhZTk1NzRhZmMyYTM1OTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commit/f73d348271fd9fedc0e03b25a60ea3d790be1111","sha":"f73d348271fd9fedc0e03b25a60ea3d790be1111","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/f73d348271fd9fedc0e03b25a60ea3d790be1111"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commit/5a86b96c6cece4763b44342f49b7a3d0dc5424fb","sha":"5a86b96c6cece4763b44342f49b7a3d0dc5424fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/5a86b96c6cece4763b44342f49b7a3d0dc5424fb"}],"sha":"7cee6ac5049991dc28e8aa2a5ae9574afc2a3597","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/7cee6ac5049991dc28e8aa2a5ae9574afc2a3597"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/87156669?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devcortes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devcortes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devcortes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devcortes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/devcortes","id":87156669,"login":"devcortes","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTU2NjY5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devcortes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devcortes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devcortes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devcortes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devcortes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/devcortes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/5a86b96c6cece4763b44342f49b7a3d0dc5424fb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T00:13:51Z","email":"87156669+devcortes@users.noreply.github.com","name":"devcortes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T00:13:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Develop (#11)\n\n* feat(e2e): playwright suite for signing feature (#8)\n\nFase 10e:\n\n* projects/signing/src/app/core/e2e-hooks.ts: install window.__signingE2E\n  when stage=''dev'' AND ?e2e=1. Exposes typed actions that bypass the\n  <video>+getUserMedia (camera) and <canvas> pointer strokes (signature\n  pad) by feeding blobs directly into the same code paths the real UI\n  uses; introspection via getState()/waitForScreen()/waitForStage();\n  debug OTP key install so request_otp echoes the plaintext code back\n  via the HMAC hatch. Zero surface in the pro bundle.\n* sign.component.ts: install hook in ngOnInit and forward the installed\n  debug key to requestOtp so the ceremony can be driven headlessly.\n* playwright.config.ts + e2e/: full suite structure\n  - fixtures/: synthetic id_front/id_back PNGs (Textract-passing) and a\n    signature PNG regenerated from the backend integration_signatures\n    helpers, kept in sync via fixtures/regenerate.sh\n  - helpers/env.ts: single-source env-var loader with a real interface\n  - helpers/backend.ts: thin API clients to register users, seed a\n    process to stage=''signature'', and open raw ceremonies via the M2M\n    service key\n  - helpers/signing-driver.ts: typed wrapper around window.__signingE2E\n  - specs/signing-standalone.spec.ts: opens a raw ceremony and drives\n    the wizard to the async boundary (worker fails on the fake PDF URL,\n    which is expected); no portal dependency\n  - specs/portal-to-payment.spec.ts: registers a user, seeds a process,\n    logs into the portal, clicks ''Firmar ahora'', drives the full\n    ceremony, returns to the portal, and asserts the auto-advance to\n    payment\n* .github/workflows/e2e.yml: manual dispatch workflow; runs against dev\n  using GH env secrets/vars. Not on the deploy critical path (worker\n  takes 30-90s per test).\n* .gitignore: e2e reports/env\n* npm scripts: e2e / e2e:headed / e2e:ui\n\nFace fixture is opt-in via SIGNATURES_TEST_FACE_PATH (privacy). Specs\ntest.skip() gracefully when missing.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs(signing): add block README + reference E2E suite from top-level (#9)\n\nFase 10f (frontend half).\n\n* projects/signing/README.md: brand new. Overview of the signing\n  micro-frontend, the two entry paths (email async / portal same-tab),\n  the server-authoritative state machine (Ceremony.stage -> local\n  screen table), the internal module layout, how to rediscover the\n  signatures API URL when the stack is recreated, security posture\n  (return_url same-origin gate, e2e hook double-gate, debug OTP key),\n  and how to run the SPA locally + tests. Explicitly points at\n  docs/signatures-v2.md $10.4 in the backend repo for the contract.\n* README.md: link the new signing/README from the blocks table.\n  Update the ''no specs yet'' aside to note that the Playwright suite\n  exists at e2e/ (repo root) precisely because it crosses two blocks;\n  points at .github/workflows/e2e.yml and e2e/README.md.\n\nNo code changes.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* chore(config): set production API endpoints\n\n* feat(testability): establish stable selectors for EUV validation (#10)\n\nCo-authored-by: David Cortes Bolivar <david.cortes@lemco.co>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Salomon Saenz <122643656+salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: salomon <salomonsaenzg368@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: David Cortes Bolivar <david.cortes@lemco.co>","tree":{"sha":"f537380c133aa0faa158b4cd0051035867c170c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/git/trees/f537380c133aa0faa158b4cd0051035867c170c3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/git/commits/5a86b96c6cece4763b44342f49b7a3d0dc5424fb","verification":{"payload":"tree f537380c133aa0faa158b4cd0051035867c170c3\nparent 41c0df0a8560874b26e655e0bbca292ccceef607\nauthor devcortes <87156669+devcortes@users.noreply.github.com> 1790468031 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790468031 -0500\n\nDevelop (#11)\n\n* feat(e2e): playwright suite for signing feature (#8)\n\nFase 10e:\n\n* projects/signing/src/app/core/e2e-hooks.ts: install window.__signingE2E\n  when stage=''dev'' AND ?e2e=1. Exposes typed actions that bypass the\n  <video>+getUserMedia (camera) and <canvas> pointer strokes (signature\n  pad) by feeding blobs directly into the same code paths the real UI\n  uses; introspection via getState()/waitForScreen()/waitForStage();\n  debug OTP key install so request_otp echoes the plaintext code back\n  via the HMAC hatch. Zero surface in the pro bundle.\n* sign.component.ts: install hook in ngOnInit and forward the installed\n  debug key to requestOtp so the ceremony can be driven headlessly.\n* playwright.config.ts + e2e/: full suite structure\n  - fixtures/: synthetic id_front/id_back PNGs (Textract-passing) and a\n    signature PNG regenerated from the backend integration_signatures\n    helpers, kept in sync via fixtures/regenerate.sh\n  - helpers/env.ts: single-source env-var loader with a real interface\n  - helpers/backend.ts: thin API clients to register users, seed a\n    process to stage=''signature'', and open raw ceremonies via the M2M\n    service key\n  - helpers/signing-driver.ts: typed wrapper around window.__signingE2E\n  - specs/signing-standalone.spec.ts: opens a raw ceremony and drives\n    the wizard to the async boundary (worker fails on the fake PDF URL,\n    which is expected); no portal dependency\n  - specs/portal-to-payment.spec.ts: registers a user, seeds a process,\n    logs into the portal, clicks ''Firmar ahora'', drives the full\n    ceremony, returns to the portal, and asserts the auto-advance to\n    payment\n* .github/workflows/e2e.yml: manual dispatch workflow; runs against dev\n  using GH env secrets/vars. Not on the deploy critical path (worker\n  takes 30-90s per test).\n* .gitignore: e2e reports/env\n* npm scripts: e2e / e2e:headed / e2e:ui\n\nFace fixture is opt-in via SIGNATURES_TEST_FACE_PATH (privacy). Specs\ntest.skip() gracefully when missing.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs(signing): add block README + reference E2E suite from top-level (#9)\n\nFase 10f (frontend half).\n\n* projects/signing/README.md: brand new. Overview of the signing\n  micro-frontend, the two entry paths (email async / portal same-tab),\n  the server-authoritative state machine (Ceremony.stage -> local\n  screen table), the internal module layout, how to rediscover the\n  signatures API URL when the stack is recreated, security posture\n  (return_url same-origin gate, e2e hook double-gate, debug OTP key),\n  and how to run the SPA locally + tests. Explicitly points at\n  docs/signatures-v2.md $10.4 in the backend repo for the contract.\n* README.md: link the new signing/README from the blocks table.\n  Update the ''no specs yet'' aside to note that the Playwright suite\n  exists at e2e/ (repo root) precisely because it crosses two blocks;\n  points at .github/workflows/e2e.yml and e2e/README.md.\n\nNo code changes.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* chore(config): set production API endpoints\n\n* feat(testability): establish stable selectors for EUV validation (#10)\n\nCo-authored-by: David Cortes Bolivar <david.cortes@lemco.co>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Salomon Saenz <122643656+salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: salomon <salomonsaenzg368@gmail.com>\nCo-author