hub.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(portal): integrate signatures v2 contract (#7)\n\nFase 10d: switch the portal from the removed browser-facing POST\n/signatures endpoint to the v2 flow where processes/advance opens\nthe ceremony server-side and returns sign_url in the same response.\n\n- Delete shared/core/signatures.service (browser must not talk to\n  the signatures API; the endpoint is now gated by an M2M service\n  key and only /processes/advance calls it from the backend)\n- Remove signaturesApiUrl from shared env (nobody consumes it)\n- Update ProcessSignature type: token -> sign_id, expanded stage\n  enum to match backend v2 public_dict, expose hash/cert fields\n- Change ProcessesService.advance() return type to include the\n  optional sign_url the backend emits on documents -> signature\n- Rewrite process.component.startSignature to use advance()\n  instead of the deleted SignaturesService.create()\n- Append ?return_url=<current> when redirecting to the signing\n  SPA so it can bounce the user back after ceremony ends\n- Auto-advance signature -> payment when the user returns and the\n  embedded ceremony is already signed (avoids a stale UI state\n  where they''d have to click ''Firmar ahora'' again pointlessly)\n- Add UI states for signing / failed / expired ceremonies. The\n  ''Reabrir ceremonia'' button assumes a follow-up backend change\n  that lets advance() reopen a stuck ceremony; until then clicking\n  it will surface a friendly transient error.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"8bf3bad0d5cd59213b7fbc59b902feb4871eee46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/git/trees/8bf3bad0d5cd59213b7fbc59b902feb4871eee46"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/git/commits/41c0df0a8560874b26e655e0bbca292ccceef607","verification":{"payload":"tree 8bf3bad0d5cd59213b7fbc59b902feb4871eee46\nparent 6839cddac1af49d3e276f7570798dfc6194bfbd2\nauthor Salomon Saenz <122643656+salo368@users.noreply.github.com> 1790040979 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790040979 -0500\n\nfeat(portal): integrate signatures v2 contract (#7)\n\nFase 10d: switch the portal from the removed browser-facing POST\n/signatures endpoint to the v2 flow where processes/advance opens\nthe ceremony server-side and returns sign_url in the same response.\n\n- Delete shared/core/signatures.service (browser must not talk to\n  the signatures API; the endpoint is now gated by an M2M service\n  key and only /processes/advance calls it from the backend)\n- Remove signaturesApiUrl from shared env (nobody consumes it)\n- Update ProcessSignature type: token -> sign_id, expanded stage\n  enum to match backend v2 public_dict, expose hash/cert fields\n- Change ProcessesService.advance() return type to include the\n  optional sign_url the backend emits on documents -> signature\n- Rewrite process.component.startSignature to use advance()\n  instead of the deleted SignaturesService.create()\n- Append ?return_url=<current> when redirecting to the signing\n  SPA so it can bounce the user back after ceremony ends\n- Auto-advance signature -> payment when the user returns and the\n  embedded ceremony is already signed (avoids a stale UI state\n  where they''d have to click ''Firmar ahora'' again pointlessly)\n- Add UI states for signing / failed / expired ceremonies. The\n  ''Reabrir ceremonia'' button assumes a follow-up backend change\n  that lets advance() reopen a stuck ceremony; until then clicking\n  it will surface a friendly transient error.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsduTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAu04QACiwR2rXG6vfptAgDeTrqTfg\nvuYk8000Q4CoHxUPitu2YxLB3oxDSwfFk0zNhOCEboPDtZ98ZeY7JztfgpEgkpc6\nHw57kLDjdq/amlG6LWY8h+kW9yFWg2HE+d0X7GiQ45XiUqiKW3WQtk3BaSEArsIr\nildWgRMXWILnOP+igsBqnBqKPz9oXL344kh+HbHZd2VgIb8a5xdlYfEFmF/91cbP\n8fkM/tOKGX6LyBmrBjGXVOvbxgm6Cjox9xExakxYinADbrRTz2f5C