7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/41c0df0a8560874b26e655e0bbca292ccceef607"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/122643656?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/salo368","id":122643656,"login":"salo368","node_id":"U_kgDOB09kyA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/6839cddac1af49d3e276f7570798dfc6194bfbd2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T00:46:48Z","email":"122643656+salo368@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Salomon Saenz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T00:46:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(signing): update signaturesApiUrl to current dev API id (#6)\n\n* feat(signing): rewrite wizard with v2 stage-machine screens\n\nFase 10c. The Fase 10b component was a minimal port that shoved consent\ninto a silent shim before OTP and used the OTP screen as a fake\n''waiting'' spinner while the async sign worker ran. This PR turns the\nwizard into a proper server-authoritative state machine with dedicated\nscreens for every backend CeremonyStage.\n\nNew screens\n-----------\n\n* signature -- own screen for drawing the ink. Reached once the three\n  biometrics are validated AND the signature PNG isn''t uploaded yet.\n* consent -- terms bullet list + explicit checkbox + accept button.\n  Backend contract: POST /consent doesn''t advance the stage, so we\n  chain POST /otp right after so the code is already in flight when\n  the OTP screen mounts.\n* signing -- dedicated ''firmando...'' screen after verifyOtp. Shows a\n  spinner, a mini progress list (OTP verified -> generating signature\n  -> emit cert), and an elapsed-seconds counter. Timeout raised to 180s\n  to cover cold-start pyhanko.\n* failed -- terminal error screen. No retry (the ceremony is dead);\n  routes back to returnUrl or shows ''close this tab''.\n* expired -- terminal TTL screen. Same recovery guidance as failed.\n\nMachinery\n---------\n\n* Server-authoritative screen() computed signal derived from\n  Ceremony.stage + uploads_state. Only local override: reviewAcknowledged\n  keeps the intro screen visible on a fresh stage=''created'' ceremony\n  with no uploads yet; page-refresh mid-flow skips review.\n* Poll cadence is 4s normally, 2s while stage==''signing'' for snappier\n  perceived latency. Terminal stages stop the poll entirely.\n* Every mutation that changes the stage calls refreshFromServerStage()\n  which short-circuits the next tick with an immediate GET so the\n  screen recomputes without a 4s dead time.\n* Timeout guard on the signing screen using WAIT_FOR_SIGNED_TIMEOUT_MS\n  (180s). Surfaces a soft error instead of leaving the user stuck on a\n  spinner forever.\n* Friendlier error copy per stage (consent errors, OTP errors,\n  validation errors) with fallback text.\n\nNaming\n------\n\n* Renamed MissingTokenComponent -> MissingSignIdComponent (aligns with\n  the backend v2 credential name; the URL param is :sign_id since\n  Fase 10b).\n* Removed the last ''token''/''drawing'' terminology from the component\n  and template.\n\nVerified locally\n----------------\n\n* npx ng build signing --configuration dev  (dev bundle: 97 kB gz)\n* npx ng build portal / simulator --configuration dev\n* node --test infra/  (5/5)\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* fix(signing): update signaturesApiUrl to current dev API id\n\nThe hardcoded id (6yif8zgrr4) was from a previous incarnation of the\ncdts-dev-signatures HTTP API. The current stack outputs\nHttpApiUrl=https://514ou9he5b.execute-api.us-east-1.amazonaws.com.\n\nSymptom: every ceremony URL rendered as ''Enlace no valido'' because the\nGET call from the SPA hit an API gateway that no longer routes to the\nsignatures service (returns 403/NotFound and the RxJS error branch\nsets notFound=true).\n\nDiscovered while smoke-testing the Fase 10c wizard against a live\nceremony opened via scripts/e2e-signature.py --stop-at-review.\n\nAlso documents the aws command to re-discover the URL when the API\ngateway is recreated by future destructive migrations, so this drift\nis easier to diagnose next time.\n\nFor pro: the placeholder is unchanged (REPLACE-AT-FIRST-PRO-DEPLOY);\nthe first pro deploy of signatures must land the correct URL.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"7d203e957075ad71571226f116e8cca8fb714b0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/git/trees/7d203e957075ad71571226f116e8cca8fb714b0d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/git/commits/6839cddac1af49d3e276f7570798dfc6194bfbd2","verification":{"payload":"tree 7d203e957075ad71571226f116e8cca8fb714b0d\nparent 43e2855d83d1a0473ecc66105d31fd99ebe67811\nauthor Salomon Saenz <122643656+salo368@users.noreply.github.com> 1790038008 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790038008 -0500\n\nfix(signing): update signaturesApiUrl to current dev API id (#6)\n\n* feat(signing): rewrite wizard with v2 stage-machine screens\n\nFase 10c. The Fase 10b component was a minimal port that shoved consent\ninto a silent shim before OTP and used the OTP screen as a fake\n''waiting'' spinner while the async sign worker ran. This PR turns the\nwizard into a proper server-authoritative state machine with dedicated\nscreens for every backend CeremonyStage.\n\nNew screens\n-----------\n\n* signature -- own screen for drawing the ink. Reached once the three\n  biometrics are validated AND the signature PNG isn''t uploaded yet.\n* consent -- terms bullet list + explicit checkbox + accept button.\n  Backend contract: POST /consent doesn''t advance the stage, so we\n  chain POST /otp right after so the code is already in flight when\n  the OTP screen mounts.\n* signing -- dedicated ''firmando...'' screen after verifyOtp. Shows a\n  spinner, a mini progress list (OTP verified -> generating signature\n  -> emit cert), and an elapsed-seconds counter. Timeout raised to 180s\n  to cover cold-start pyhanko.\n* failed -- terminal error screen. No retry (the ceremony is dead);\n  routes back to returnUrl or shows ''close this tab''.\n* expired -- terminal TTL screen. Same recovery guidance as failed.\n\nMachinery\n---------\n\n* Server-authoritative screen() computed signal derived from\n  Ceremony.stage + uploads_state. Only local override: reviewAcknowledged\n  keeps the intro screen visible on a fresh stage=''created'' ceremony\n  with no uploads yet; page-refresh mid-flow skips review.\n* Poll cadence is 4s normally, 2s while stage==''signing'' for snappier\n  perceived latency. Terminal stages stop the poll entirely.\n* Every mutation that changes the stage calls refreshFromServerStage()\n  which short-circuits the next tick with an immediate GET so the\n  screen recomputes without a 4s dead time.\n* Timeout guard on the signing screen using WAIT_FOR_SIGNED_TIMEOUT_MS\n  (180s). Surfaces a soft error instead of leaving the user stuck on a\n  spinner forever.\n* Friendlier error copy per stage (consent errors, OTP errors,\n  validation errors) with fallback text.\n\nNaming\n------\n\n* Renamed MissingTokenComponent -> MissingSignIdComponent (aligns with\n  the backend v2 credential name; the URL param is :sign_id since\n  Fase 10b).\n* Removed the last ''token''/''drawing'' terminology from the component\n  and template.\n\nVerified locally\n----------------\n\n* npx ng build signing --configuration dev  (dev bundle: 97 kB gz)\n* npx ng build portal / simulator --configuration dev\n* node --test infra/  (5/5)\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* fix(signing): update signaturesApiUrl to current dev API id\n\nThe hardcoded id (6yif8zgrr4) was from a previous incarnation of the\ncdts-dev-signatures HTTP API. The current stack outputs\nHttpApiUrl=https://514ou9he5b.execute-api.us-east-1.amazonaws.com.\n\nSymptom: every ceremony URL rendered as ''Enlace no valido'' because the\nGET call from the SPA hit an API gateway that no longer routes to the\nsignatures service (returns 403/NotFound and the RxJS error branch\nsets notFound=true).\n\nDiscovered while smoke-testing the Fase 10c wizard against a live\nceremony opened via scripts/e2e-signature.py --stop-at-review.\n\nAlso documents the aws command to re-discover the URL when the API\ngateway is recreated by future destructive migrations, so this drift\nis easier to diagnose next time.\n\nFor pro: the placeholder is unchanged (REPLACE-AT-FIRST-PRO-DEPLOY);\nthe first pro deploy of signatures must land the correct URL.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsc/4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoJYQAKFASf48jIoSgM8u81tjPPEL\nayDvUpdq07cpFlTl7S8hiO9tujppsJaAMw7r5B+htPwqup1/aaG6w+0wwCfLx0dH\nxVX8g/NNatZ4AgroyaMXMGcqi9Y/1Wms4h8CN7fdsUuh+Lc+f/eNMoQroL5DdtX8\nXmOqbKH/1u+PNQXGQc24RYVk/H4+CYt2cm4BPe0yrcITU/kbI26TQ11QhcfFG+Uh\nAVOnTu8X80XkRbfzCKYxaPX/VHrN3JLp/Xr9AvbCGBfDrqrXyUyTCVDy7dn4Sh3H\nIpEi9bLdv/Jm5ZF31RqsyZzpfY379BorkRnrcOG5E4rkC5boNB2wc82q2CqmbX3N\nCiLOAzta10+ejoDMufneSe7ATmX0Bt644CteVQu2yL6B8XZ/L