sh mid-flow skips review.\n* Poll cadence is 4s normally, 2s while stage==''signing'' for snappier\n  perceived latency. Terminal stages stop the poll entirely.\n* Every mutation that changes the stage calls refreshFromServerStage()\n  which short-circuits the next tick with an immediate GET so the\n  screen recomputes without a 4s dead time.\n* Timeout guard on the signing screen using WAIT_FOR_SIGNED_TIMEOUT_MS\n  (180s). Surfaces a soft error instead of leaving the user stuck on a\n  spinner forever.\n* Friendlier error copy per stage (consent errors, OTP errors,\n  validation errors) with fallback text.\n\nNaming\n------\n\n* Renamed MissingTokenComponent -> MissingSignIdComponent (aligns with\n  the backend v2 credential name; the URL param is :sign_id since\n  Fase 10b).\n* Removed the last ''token''/''drawing'' terminology from the component\n  and template.\n\nVerified locally\n----------------\n\n* npx ng build signing --configuration dev  (dev bundle: 97 kB gz)\n* npx ng build portal / simulator --configuration dev\n* node --test infra/  (5/5)\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqscTUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQ8wQAInSZuDxHGIGkA1zfWjex5Tf\nZtJYKZwYYfUfqL+DlQyZi1ihrdDQFQ9HoyJjWuXFpWXbVtHbCMZ7yv4xJaAaMVg1\nn01AWo4sFeeO4vg26NYGFoa+r19jqsOXIFLVX+Gu0sk0oPNbhaiepBNzwKQBS2Zo\nEwKVX3XQSwt4kb/25ebIWcrQ8thGp17oAdE0RkLSGvYpVHL2BJQXa2iUoJRqA2gZ\nuTn97LsnbEN2vEKCOxyIc/tvuszuFgrau4WgXWCsNZaRyuk2BqGRrsIi8nF8FLuu\nXY0y+5UYRew66G5f0uqjo4i04mj4Vfc2PCB2TCtuF2ZmkO6XbLtM61RGxJrWtjFo\njv6ScG6yYAsFpr7vp4dSgy1uJbYnMFI8ocN+JQfIdQjkx+E/aGX4hSfEm7vcfo8B\n6u+ybcxdbznJ2yy+Jd/IaMkZoI+ynEKO23HY6RiWnQfzwOvWdAzhOrEecnGZ0dWl\npcLxACihT4Jqo0eQqZsOhqf2MzyGugbr79ORYPpe2ebep7HYrSI1iffCys9yjOvj\nBXrrQeBE2uFrg/efW1yhEzsvFayy2lY6Nl7hoLv2fF09riDVHeQdEzwp+lry/afD\nmOlyYp12mw8VJgzWuwpEPXsKMlU+dWaa4NkFWYyZq5cbf58efMl5p+HjgCDA50AZ\nT272bGEJIeeO7E/Jt085\n=DvPq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T23:59:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commit/43e2855d83d1a0473ecc66105d31fd99ebe67811","node_id":"C_kwDOUiz2UtoAKDQzZTI4NTVkODNkMWEwNDczZWNjNjYxMDVkMzFmZDk5ZWJlNjc4MTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commit/f222339e712301ea1e957ad30d2f2bae510ce204","sha":"f222339e712301ea1e957ad30d2f2bae510ce204","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/f222339e712301ea1e957ad30d2f2bae510ce204"}],"sha":"43e2855d83d1a0473ecc66105d31fd99ebe67811","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/43e2855d83d1a0473ecc66105d31fd99ebe67811"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/122643656?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/salo368","id":122643656,"login":"salo368","node_id":"U_kgDOB09kyA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/f222339e712301ea1e957ad30d2f2bae510ce204/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T23:40:42Z","email":"122643656+salo368@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Salomon Saenz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T23:40:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(ci): inline pipeline per stage so UI renders like backend (#4)\n\nFollow-up to PR #3. The previous shape wrapped the whole pipeline in a\nreusable deploy.yml called from deploy-dev.yml / deploy-pro.yml via\nworkflow_call. That prefixed every job in the run visualization with\n''deploy / ...'' -- so the GitHub UI showed ''deploy / Plan'',\n''deploy / Validate'', ''deploy / signing / Test'', etc. Backend does NOT\nhave that prefix because its deploy-dev.yml and deploy-pro.yml inline\ntheir pipeline directly, calling the per-service reusable\n(service-package.yml) only for the matrix.\n\nThis PR:\n\n* Deletes .github/workflows/deploy.yml (the reusable wrapper).\n* Inlines the full pipeline into deploy-dev.yml with stage=''dev''\n  hardcoded.\n* Inlines the full pipeline into deploy-pro.yml with stage=''pro''\n  hardcoded and a simpler summary (integration is dev-only inside\n  block-package.yml, so on pro it always renders as ''dev-only'').\n* Keeps block-package.yml unchanged -- still the per-block matrix\n  target with validate -> test -> deploy -> integration -> status.\n* README.md: rewrote the Deploy section to describe the shape and\n  added a dedicated block on what the Infrastructure job actually\n  deploys in frontend (CloudFront distribution, three per-block S3\n  buckets, edge routing function, cache behaviors + IAM, SSM\n  parameter). Also clarified that unlike backend, frontend infra has\n  no content to sync -- bundles are uploaded by each block''s own\n  Deploy job.\n\nAfter this PR the run visualization matches backend exactly:\n\n  Plan\n  Validate\n  Infrastructure\n  simulator / Validate    simulator / Test    simulator / Deploy    simulator / Integration    simulator / Status\n  portal    / Validate    portal    / Test    portal    / Deploy    portal    / Integration    portal    / Status\n  signing   / Validate    signing   / Test    signing   / Deploy    signing   / Integration    signing   / Status\n  Deploy summary\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"2da86b7b69bdaf415c085254cc3ac8603d353885","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/git/trees/2da86b7b69bdaf415c085254cc3ac8603d353885"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/git/commits/f222339e712301ea1e957ad30d2f2bae510ce204","verification":{"payload":"tree 2da86b7b69bdaf415c085254cc3ac8603d353885\nparent 513637ec502db6dec31019b81f7a3151cab95739\nauthor Salomon Saenz <122643656+salo368@users.noreply.github.com> 1790034042 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790034042 -0500\n\nchore(ci): inline pipeline per stage so UI renders like backend (#4)\n\nFollow-up to PR #3. The previous shape wrapped the whole pipeline in a\nreusable deploy.yml called from deploy-dev.yml / deploy-pro.yml via\nworkflow_call. That prefixed every job in the run visualization with\n''deploy / ...'' -- so the GitHub UI showed ''deploy / Plan'',\n''deploy / Validate'', ''deploy / signing / Test'', etc. Backend does NOT\nhave that prefix because its deploy-dev.yml and deploy-pro.yml inline\ntheir pipeline directly, calling the per-service reusable\n(service-package.yml) only for the matrix.\n\nThis PR:\n\n* Deletes .github/workflows/deploy.yml (the reusable wrapper).\n* Inlines the full pipeline into deploy-dev.yml with stage=''dev''\n  hardcoded.\n* Inlines the full pipeline into deploy-pro.yml with stage=''pro''\n  hardcoded and a simpler summary (integration is dev-only inside\n  block-package.yml, so on pro it always renders as ''dev-only'').\n* Keeps block-package.yml unchanged -- still the per-block matrix\n  target with validate -> test -> deploy -> integration -> status.\n* README.md: rewrote the Deploy section to describe the shape and\n  added a dedicated block on what the Infrastructure job actually\n  deploys in frontend (CloudFront distribution, three per-block S3\n  buckets, edge routing function, cache behaviors + IAM, SSM\n  parameter). Also clarified that unlike backend, frontend infra has\n  no content to sync -- bundles are uploaded by each block''s own\n  Deploy job.\n\nAfter this PR the run visualization matches backend exactly:\n\n  Plan\n  Validate\n  Infrastructure\n  simulator / Validate    simulator / Test    simulator / Deploy    simulator / Integration    simulator / Status\n  portal    / Validate    portal    / Test    portal    / Deploy    portal    / Integration    portal    / Status\n  signing   / Validate    signing   / Test    signing   / Deploy    signing   / Integration    signing   / Status\n  Deploy summary\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqscB6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/1wQAEesKkTC/bh3bQqjVjycC3ux\n3E/0Hasoa8yHwp21ueKzl/3IfYixMDCF3gQFvM03jTxva8QvePcj7TX8+XcvPye5\nm/mbZvCu4LHaBwpAOSp5wCDLAtSesDM8A68Hfn0wIZLygKI/SkeQEpkiHAN2faZ2\nee4fdJWGxIAo0ZeVkGCMqCn+OXF4EIlm6KlJH61wW0Ag8jCtAlbvJ5Udq5w/2/ID\nIgmptgmGJNU5NHUsLOU6cjZ+Es+Xh6+zMIy6TfD0tC7IkVuhfdubGEBWRaNtBXEm\nYaiwX9cR6WN83e0ejtNHWVvH8jMkm4NeEZyzN8ua9LWIUiD/Q6lXm4vQ6fV