mmits/f222339e712301ea1e957ad30d2f2bae510ce204"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/122643656?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/salo368","id":122643656,"login":"salo368","node_id":"U_kgDOB09kyA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/513637ec502db6dec31019b81f7a3151cab95739/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T23:31:00Z","email":"122643656+salo368@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Salomon Saenz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T23:31:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(ci): align frontend pipeline shape with backend (#3)\n\nMirror the backend pipeline layout so both repos share the same mental\nmodel:\n\n  plan\n   -> validate (cross-cutting: edge router + build every block)\n   -> infrastructure? (conditional serverless deploy of CF+S3 stack)\n   -> blocks [matrix]\n        each block: validate -> test -> deploy -> integration\n   -> summary (per-block, per-stage table)\n\nChanges:\n\n* .github/workflows/block-package.yml (new): reusable per-block workflow\n  with validate -> test -> deploy -> integration -> record_status.\n  Test detects *.spec.ts, skips cleanly if none.\n  Integration detects projects/<block>/e2e or /cypress, dev-only,\n  non-blocking, skips cleanly if none.\n* .github/workflows/deploy.yml: rewritten as an orchestrator. Emits a\n  summary table with per-block outcome, deployed URL, and ''stopped at''\n  column pulled from block-status-* + infrastructure-status artifacts.\n* scripts/ci/plan-deploy.sh: outputs renamed to blocks_to_deploy,\n  blocks_count, run_infrastructure, transversal, total_count (mirrors\n  backend service_to_deploy naming). Diff anchor changed from\n  GITHUB_EVENT_BEFORE to LAST_SUCCESSFUL_DEPLOY_SHA so a failed prior\n  pipeline that landed an infra change doesn''t get skipped forever.\n  is_transversal() covers projects/shared/**, angular.json,\n  package.json, tsconfig*, .nvmrc, scripts/ci/deploy.sh,\n  .github/workflows/**.\n* deploy-dev.yml / deploy-pro.yml: added actions: read permission\n  required by the Plan job''s gh run list call.\n* README.md: rewrote the Deploy section to describe the new shape,\n  document that test/integration lanes exist but are dormant, and\n  point out the exit criteria (add *.spec.ts or projects/<block>/e2e/\n  to activate).\n\nStill no Karma specs and no Playwright/Cypress suites -- both cells\nrender as ''no specs'' / ''no e2e'' in the summary table. When those\nsuites land (Fase 10e for signing E2E), the pipeline picks them up\nwithout any workflow change.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"43b65ae0a09bd42d2a253b4c9e225c55a0678730","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/git/trees/43b65ae0a09bd42d2a253b4c9e225c55a0678730"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/git/commits/513637ec502db6dec31019b81f7a3151cab95739","verification":{"payload":"tree 43b65ae0a09bd42d2a253b4c9e225c55a0678730\nparent 79a08b7b7aba1548757cb970732204bf948702c7\nauthor Salomon Saenz <122643656+salo368@users.noreply.github.com> 1790033460 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790033460 -0500\n\nchore(ci): align frontend pipeline shape with backend (#3)\n\nMirror the backend pipeline layout so both repos share the same mental\nmodel:\n\n  plan\n   -> validate (cross-cutting: edge router + build every block)\n   -> infrastructure? (conditional serverless deploy of CF+S3 stack)\n   -> blocks [matrix]\n        each block: validate -> test -> deploy -> integration\n   -> summary (per-block, per-stage table)\n\nChanges:\n\n* .github/workflows/block-package.yml (new): reusable per-block workflow\n  with validate -> test -> deploy -> integration -> record_status.\n  Test detects *.spec.ts, skips cleanly if none.\n  Integration detects projects/<block>/e2e or /cypress, dev-only,\n  non-blocking, skips cleanly if none.\n* .github/workflows/deploy.yml: rewritten as an orchestrator. Emits a\n  summary table with per-block outcome, deployed URL, and ''stopped at''\n  column pulled from block-status-* + infrastructure-status artifacts.\n* scripts/ci/plan-deploy.sh: outputs renamed to blocks_to_deploy,\n  blocks_count, run_infrastructure, transversal, total_count (mirrors\n  backend service_to_deploy naming). Diff anchor changed from\n  GITHUB_EVENT_BEFORE to LAST_SUCCESSFUL_DEPLOY_SHA so a failed prior\n  pipeline that landed an infra change doesn''t get skipped forever.\n  is_transversal() covers projects/shared/**, angular.json,\n  package.json, tsconfig*, .nvmrc, scripts/ci/deploy.sh,\n  .github/workflows/**.\n* deploy-dev.yml / deploy-pro.yml: added actions: read permission\n  required by the Plan job''s gh run list call.\n* README.md: rewrote the Deploy section to describe the new shape,\n  document that test/integration lanes exist but are dormant, and\n  point out the exit criteria (add *.spec.ts or projects/<block>/e2e/\n  to activate).\n\nStill no Karma specs and no Playwright/Cypress suites -- both cells\nrender as ''no specs'' / ''no e2e'' in the summary table. When those\nsuites land (Fase 10e for signing E2E), the pipeline picks them up\nwithout any workflow change.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsb40CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALKEQAGerDWaPmwLBO8d34N7o+Dyq\n270GTxgg6lujbdlPsoTMk9QxKlL9Eva3W1h9z0Cc6iEZmq+Nm+AV58hwZCcMHAwk\n+sIL84lBLg+hnHE/WAUNyARnYsgWMrX6xJ1Hh6iXg9SgFLNRovXmiPMV3s1MXyYb\nYgA9lH0Ey9daWR/1493f5hJMTvNoJAXaXOyjpk8cde+pY3wkFY+R7/oem0ZSdsWv\nsSYAUdtCrYt2bDkoRCdEUppzgKMYdwphk3ZjTm5HhwDSVUTk+b8/kfSgmtBcDyJ4\npkCJxmHET8/R1xA0kukZz8gtnXIl/dluvQQbihZoJ1WRKQM/jzMKEtYgNi2XoRLs\ndQvcD2Y6/duhwekzQa0+8XTpjUn3Zu1bUnQU68sS5m4xNtqPltSAc+fB8Azty+zI\ns5loykDgeA3PR8NY1GJyfLJ/PQtzV64iF/qiZx2S+KXAf+FkDGaUXh0DcKRovfFO\noiSFdQ+DEYC4D0CeZAZws5k0gWlES4sM90w+Vn+jdzqyZLQK5ichF4mDR1URHbgE\nY8om5VkE7klBHUssBIP/RiJUSKXgGKC1wDIXY5/7s/T89dB/fqktn8Z8Ghz0az9r\n2tjBT7G8alu6Pj5kPAPqYurKvrzc7U79h+ciHZeQ5BeGqW8wcAZUqVmnwMkwg3l+\n/JrdLJ8lPy6m4NNn+kdJ\n=l6Q2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T23:31:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commit/513637ec502db6dec31019b81f7a3151cab95739","node_id":"C_kwDOUiz2UtoAKDUxMzYzN2VjNTAyZGI2ZGVjMzEwMTliODFmN2EzMTUxY2FiOTU3Mzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commit/79a08b7b7aba1548757cb970732204bf948702c7","sha":"79a08b7b7aba1548757cb970732204bf948702c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/79a08b7b7aba1548757cb970732204bf948702c7"}],"sha":"513637ec502db6dec31019b81f7a3151cab95739","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/513637ec502db6dec31019b81f7a3151cab95739"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/122643656?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/salo368","id":122643656,"login":"salo368","node_id":"U_kgDOB09kyA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/79a08b7b7aba1548757cb970732204bf948702c7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T23:13:38Z","email":"122643656+salo368@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Salomon Saenz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T23:13:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(signing): rewrite service + types + route for signatures v2 API (#2)\n\nFase 10b of the frontend migration. This is the infrastructure layer:\nnew HTTP client, new response types, new route param, new host\nintegration point. The UI wiring changes are the minimum needed for\nthe wizard to compile and drive a full ceremony end-to-end against\nthe v2 backend; the proper wizard reshape lands in Fase 10c.\n\n## signatures.service.ts (full rewrite)\n\nClient surface matches backend PR #70 one-to-one:\n\n  * get()               -- returns Ceremony (public_dict() + signer_name\n                           + pdf_url + optional signed_pdf_url).\n  * presignEvidence()   -- POST /upload-url with { evidence_type,\n                           content_type } (was { type }).\n  * uploadEvidence()    -- convenience: presign + PUT S3 in one chain.\n                           Passes Content-Type header on the PUT so\n                           the s3v4 signature matches.\n  * validateIdSide()    -- POST /evidence/id-{front|back} (was\n                           /validate { type }).\n  * validateFace()      -- POST /evidence/face.\n  * registerSignature() -- POST /evidence/signature (NEW: has to be\n                           called after uploading the drawn PNG,\n                           otherwise the ceremony stays at ''identity'').\n  * consent()           -- POST /consent with { terms_version: ''v1.0'' }\n                           (NEW step required before OTP).\n  * requestOtp()        -- POST /otp. Optional debugKeyHex param wraps\n                           the request with X-Debug-OTP-Signature so\n                           E2E tests can pull the plaintext from\n                           _debug_otp without waiting for email.\n  * verifyOtp()         -- POST /otp/verify with { code } (was\n                           /confirm with { otp }). Now returns\n                           stage=''signing'' -- callers must poll get()\n                           for the terminal ''signed''.\n\nTypes mirror the ORM/HTTP shape drift documented in backend #71:\n  * EvidenceTypeApi (''signature_drawing'') for POST /upload-url.\n  * EvidenceOrmKey (''signature'') for reading uploads_state.\n  * EVIDENCE_ORM_TO_API / EVIDENCE_API_TO_ORM bridges.\n\nCeremonyStage covers the full v2 lifecycle including ''consent'',\n''signing'', ''failed'', ''expired''. STAGE_ORDER + TERMINAL_STAGES exported\nfor consumers that want to guard transitions without a switch.\n\ndebugOtpSignature() computes hex(HMAC-SHA256(key, sign_id)) via Web\nCrypto so Playwright / Cypress can hit the debug-OTP hatch. Byte-for-\nbyte identical to backend/services/signatures/src/handlers/request_otp/\nhandler.py::_authorized_for_debug_otp.\n\n## host-app.ts (redesigned)\n\nOld: hardcoded /portal/process/{process_id}. Broken now that v2\nceremonies don''t expose process_id on GET.\n\nNew: resolveReturnUrl(rawQueryParam, currentLocation) validates a\nreturn_url query param. Returns the URL only when it''s an absolute\nhttp(s) URL AND same-origin as the current window. Callers show a\ngeneric \"podes cerrar esta pestana\" landing when null (email-path\nsigners who arrived cold).\n\n## app.routes.ts\n\nRoute param renamed :token -> :sign_id to match the backend\nterminology. External URLs of the shape /sign/{token} need\nregenerating; the portal integration lands in Fase 10d.\n\n## sign.component.ts (minimal viable rewrite)\n\nEnough to compile against the new service AND drive a real ceremony\nto completion:\n\n  * signId variable replaces token throughout.\n  * DOCS array uses API keys (id_front, id_back, face) instead of\n    cedula_*.\n  * apply() translates uploads_state[orm].validated -> docDone[api]\n    with the biometric-vs-drawing distinction (validated===null falls\n    back to uploaded for signature_drawing).\n  * onCaptured() dispatches the three validate endpoints per type.\n  * submitSignature() chains upload -> registerSignature ->\n    acceptConsentAndSendOtp -> requestOtp (silent consent shim; Fase\n    10c introduces the real consent screen).\n  * confirm() -> verifyOtp() + WAIT_FOR_SIGNED_TIMEOUT_MS bound while\n    the async sign worker runs. finishToDone() picks up ''signed'' via\n    the poll loop.\n  * stageToStep() collapses v2 stages onto the current 4-step UI:\n    ''consent'' and ''signing'' merge into ''drawing'' / ''otp'' respectively.\n    Fase 10c will introduce dedicated screens for them.\n  * backToProcess() honors resolveReturnUrl(); no returnUrl means the\n    ''done'' screen hides the button and shows the standalone label.\n  * friendlyValidateError / friendlyOtpError adapted to the v2 error\n    codes returned by the new endpoints.\n\n## sign.component.html\n\nThree field renames (c.page/x/y -> c.signature_location.*,\nc.email_masked -> c.signer_email_masked) plus a conditional\nreturn_url button on the done screen.\n\n## Build\n\nnpm run build -> all three blocks (simulator, portal, signing)\ncompile clean, only the pre-existing bootstrap .form-floating CSS\nwarning. Portal was NOT touched (Fase 10d).\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"e2e80d4674b1f518064a190800cc8a13a8987aa4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/git/trees/e2e80d4674b1f518064a190800cc8a13a8987aa4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/git/commits/79a08b7b7aba1548757cb970732204bf948702c7","verification":{"payload":"tree e2e80d4674b1f518064a190800cc8a13a8987aa4\nparent c0667c4722584efe96a001212d9d62e1b452754d\nauthor Salomon Saenz <122643656+salo368@users.noreply.github.com> 1790032418 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790032418 -0500\n\nfeat(signing): rewrite service + types + route for signatures v2 API (#2)\n\nFase 10b of the frontend migration. This is the infrastructure layer:\nnew HTTP client, new response types, new route param, new host\nintegration point. The UI wiring changes are the minimum needed for\nthe wizard to compile and drive a full ceremony end-to-end against\nthe v2 backend; the proper wizard reshape lands in Fase 10c.\n\n## signatures.service.ts (full rewrite)\n\nClient surface matches backend PR #70 one-to-one:\n\n  * get()               -- returns Ceremony (public_dict() + signer_name\n                           + pdf_url + optional signed_pdf_url).\n  * presignEvidence()   -- POST /upload-url with { evidence_type,\n                           content_type } (was { type }).\n  * uploadEvidence()    -- convenience: presign + PUT S3 in one chain.\n                           Passes Content-Type header on the PUT so\n                           the s3v4 signature matches.\n  * validateIdSide()    -- POST /evidence/id-{front|back} (was\n                           /validate { type }).\n  * validateFace()      -- POST /evidence/face.\n  * registerSignature() -- POST /evidence/signature (NEW: has to be\n                           called after uploading the drawn PNG,\n                           otherwise the ceremony stays at ''identity'').\n  * consent()           -- POST /consent with { terms_version: ''v1.0'' }\n                           (NEW step required before OTP).\n  * requestOtp()        -- POST /otp. Optional debugKeyHex param wraps\n                           the request with X-Debug-OTP-Signature so\n                           E2E tests can pull the plaintext from\n                           _debug_otp without waiting for email.\n  * verifyOtp()         -- POST /otp/verify with { code } (was\n                           /confirm with { otp }). Now returns\n                           stage=''signing'' -- callers must poll get()\n                           for the terminal ''signed''.\n\nTypes mirror the ORM/HTTP shape drift documented in backend #71:\n  * EvidenceTypeApi (''signature_drawing'') for POST /upload-url.\n  * EvidenceOrmKey (''signature'') for reading uploads_state.\n  * EVIDENCE_ORM_TO_API / EVIDENCE_API_TO_ORM bridges.\n\nCeremonyStage covers the full v2 lifecycle including ''consent'',\n''signing'', ''failed'', ''expired''. STAGE_ORDER + TERMINAL_STAGES exported\nfor consumers that want to guard transitions without a switch.\n\ndebugOtpSignature() computes hex(HMAC-SHA256(key, sign_id)) via Web\nCrypto so Playwright / Cypress can hit the debug-OTP hatch. Byte-for-\nbyte identical to backend/services/signatures/src/handlers/request_otp/\nhandler.py::_authorized_for_debug_otp.\n\n## host-app.ts (redesigned)\n\nOld: hardcoded /portal/process/{process_id}. Broken now that v2\nceremonies don''t expose process_id on GET.\n\nNew: resolveReturnUrl(rawQueryParam, currentLocation) validates a\nreturn_url query param. Returns the URL only when it''s an absolute\nhttp(s) URL AND same-origin as the current window. Callers show a\ngeneric \"podes cerrar esta pestana\" landing when null (email-path\nsigners who arrived cold).\n\n## app.routes.ts\n\nRoute param renamed :token -> :sign_id to match the backend\nterminology. External URLs of the shape /sign/{token} need\nregenerating; the portal integration lands in Fase 10d.\n\n## sign.component.ts (minimal viable rewrite)\n\nEnough to compile against the new service AND drive a real ceremony\nto completion:\n\n  * signId variable replaces token throughout.\n  * DOCS array uses API keys (id_front, id_back, face) instead of\n    cedula_*.\n  * apply() translates uploads_state[orm].validated -> docDone[api]\n    with the biometric-vs-drawing distinction (validated===null falls\n    back to uploaded for signature_drawing).\n  * onCaptured() dispatches the three validate endpoints per type.\n  * submitSignature() chains upload -> registerSignature ->\n    acceptConsentAndSendOtp -> requestOtp (silent consent shim; Fase\n    10c introduces the real consent screen).\n  * confirm() -> verifyOtp() + WAIT_FOR_SIGNED_TIMEOUT_MS bound while\n    the async sign worker runs. finishToDone() picks up ''signed'' via\n    the poll loop.\n  * stageToStep() collapses v2 stages onto the current 4-step UI:\n    ''consent'' and ''signing'' merge into ''drawing'' / ''otp'' respectively.\n    Fase 10c will introduce dedicated screens for them.\n  * backToProcess() honors resolveReturnUrl(); no returnUrl means the\n    ''done'' screen hides the button and shows the standalone label.\n  * friendlyValidateError / friendlyOtpError adapted to the v2 error\n    codes returned by the new endpoints.\n\n## sign.component.html\n\nThree field renames (c.page/x/y -> c.signature_location.*,\nc.email_masked -> c.signer_email_masked) plus a conditional\nreturn_url button on the done screen.\n\n## Build\n\nnpm run build -> all three blocks (simulator, portal, signing)\ncompile clean, only the pre-existing bootstrap .form-floating CSS\nwarning. Portal was NOT touched (Fase 10d).\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsboiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEiQQAJWXCAmXOt0tqoG82/dhfKxC\nx5920dFd+045+zLVjcYI8N1/4IIuS/NbjJ+vnIkOSGUebUxb3Q87mzvXTcw2VKmt\nE8vmpcgB5oKm/aO53O38dtPfd/NyhQp1aK7mKa7lxLVP4VD0dqmQqpzo0tksugMo\nYZsU63KAzuKV7uXPnJjn+GcMxzR7nGJG+Rhc4C5FgVKEKfNLJbUSCu2CKgiPTDKv\nwmBHrIdJ1I5Q7eYU6ZeBT5bpvj7w0jn1KmSe55EqlrLYyIF9oQ5OxJHIxBycInpt\nbh/h0dt+b7EE2X70sEaelutmFpQiHhTSudId7FcGpHkwMOnaIMg6Q5S920H/lvgw\nP8dhtyfe4hWzsnTYdrKZOXJ3gsk7wUMWtbkfbX9hzovrT8DkCB8+G95sZ8+ygxp8\nOhh4WIxDBJIUz3aQ/nasliIAJxm3nsPH1PNXyLuj+mEvkywd2aKqmAYxd5JvSw1w\ngw64HzpppaOWwMNBrF/3igzx+dFdXmc0hPScb9CXt+/7JVhiM8KX+/UIpwhzD+Fo\nRYEU2OWUMWrNKLzrh8VTvTyPUPPZsXISXWEsajynHMQzHIajORetIPdibQPwnBnZ\nmfctWOellTZH+oPRD/7KFlRxysLFSJ80wFjLLPWLgIEShNYNijCXds/9C2CizDvr\nff2kFHZEKz1MqdMeQTzC\n=wzjl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T23:13:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,