,"type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/c0667c4722584efe96a001212d9d62e1b452754d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T20:43:22Z","email":"salomonsaenzg368@gmail.com","name":"salomon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T20:43:22Z","email":"salomonsaenzg368@gmail.com","name":"salomon"},"message":"docs(iam): reflejar los buckets por bloque y las CloudFront Functions\n\nAclara que editar el JSON no basta: hay que publicar una version nueva de\nla policy o el deploy falla con AccessDenied, que es justo lo que paso al\nagregar cloudfront:CreateFunction.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"8453e9faa4b9e8eb75e0475de3c9a2ae97d4a3c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/git/trees/8453e9faa4b9e8eb75e0475de3c9a2ae97d4a3c6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/git/commits/c0667c4722584efe96a001212d9d62e1b452754d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/122643656?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/salo368","id":122643656,"login":"salo368","node_id":"U_kgDOB09kyA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commit/c0667c4722584efe96a001212d9d62e1b452754d","node_id":"C_kwDOUiz2UtoAKGMwNjY3YzQ3MjI1ODRlZmU5NmEwMDEyMTJkOWQ2MmUxYjQ1Mjc1NGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commit/ad07f4032275f886e7fcccf622d92929fdce78e8","sha":"ad07f4032275f886e7fcccf622d92929fdce78e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/ad07f4032275f886e7fcccf622d92929fdce78e8"}],"sha":"c0667c4722584efe96a001212d9d62e1b452754d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/c0667c4722584efe96a001212d9d62e1b452754d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/122643656?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/salo368","id":122643656,"login":"salo368","node_id":"U_kgDOB09kyA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/ad07f4032275f886e7fcccf622d92929fdce78e8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T20:37:26Z","email":"122643656+salo368@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Salomon Saenz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T20:37:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: partir el frontend en micro frontends (#1)\n\nTres bloques independientes que se compilan y despliegan por separado, y\nque CloudFront compone bajo el mismo dominio:\n\n  simulator  /          landing, simulador y docs\n  portal     /portal/*  login, cuenta y wizard del proceso\n  signing    /sign/*    ceremonia de firma\n\nEl objetivo es disponibilidad: no hay nada compartido en runtime, asi que\nun despliegue roto de un bloque no puede tumbar a los otros. Se descarto\nModule Federation porque el shell seria un punto unico de fallo y acoplaria\nlas versiones de Angular entre bloques.\n\nCambios estructurales:\n\n- Workspace Angular multi-proyecto. Lo comun vive en projects/shared y se\n  importa como @shared/*; cada bloque tiene su index.html y su baseHref.\n- signing no depende de shared ni conoce el dominio: todo lo que sabe del\n  host esta en un host-app.ts de tres lineas, para poder reusarlo firmando\n  documentos de cualquier tipo.\n- Se quita el hash routing, que impedia enrutar por prefijo en el edge\n  porque el fragmento nunca llega al servidor. Las URLs pasan de\n  /#/firmar/<token> a /sign/<token>.\n- Un bucket por bloque y una CloudFront Function que resuelve el fallback\n  de la SPA por bloque, con tests: el fallback global devolvia siempre el\n  index de la raiz, que con varios bloques sirve el index equivocado.\n- Deploy selectivo por diff, un job por bloque en paralelo, e invalidacion\n  acotada a las rutas del bloque.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"05483758719c14a4cc8b35804859a34a38d2e38a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/git/trees/05483758719c14a4cc8b35804859a34a38d2e38a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/git/commits/ad07f4032275f886e7fcccf622d92929fdce78e8","verification":{"payload":"tree 05483758719c14a4cc8b35804859a34a38d2e38a\nparent 1b1c1b5e1e1c982688ce4130ff5ed75d913eab16\nauthor Salomon Saenz <122643656+salo368@users.noreply.github.com> 1789936646 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789936646 -0500\n\nfeat: partir el frontend en micro frontends (#1)\n\nTres bloques independientes que se compilan y despliegan por separado, y\nque CloudFront compone bajo el mismo dominio:\n\n  simulator  /          landing, simulador y docs\n  portal     /portal/*  login, cuenta y wizard del proceso\n  signing    /sign/*    ceremonia de firma\n\nEl objetivo es disponibilidad: no hay nada compartido en runtime, asi que\nun despliegue roto de un bloque no puede tumbar a los otros. Se descarto\nModule Federation porque el shell seria un punto unico de fallo y acoplaria\nlas versiones de Angular entre bloques.\n\nCambios estructurales:\n\n- Workspace Angular multi-proyecto. Lo comun vive en projects/shared y se\n  importa como @shared/*; cada bloque tiene su index.html y su baseHref.\n- signing no depende de shared ni conoce el dominio: todo lo que sabe del\n  host esta en un host-app.ts de tres lineas, para poder reusarlo firmando\n  documentos de cualquier tipo.\n- Se quita el hash routing, que impedia enrutar por prefijo en el edge\n  porque el fragmento nunca llega al servidor. Las URLs pasan de\n  /#/firmar/<token> a /sign/<token>.\n- Un bucket por bloque y una CloudFront Function que resuelve el fallback\n  de la SPA por bloque, con tests: el fallback global devolvia siempre el\n  index de la raiz, que con varios bloques sirve el index equivocado.\n- Deploy selectivo por diff, un job por bloque en paralelo, e invalidacion\n  acotada a las rutas del bloque.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsEQGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABAkQAI5hw73CdrbatbqUax/4CI9Q\nbJ0cBfRgmP8pDB9GYj7gffOYsHlqSZBwv+UQAUU/F/wujSl32fOyYVdgaXAw7Dip\nriitRk1cm2jgl7F097x+BugVmUuCeUVq09umdILbmzFwzsMGZF7DWFpIsz5eDUM3\nM6mO7tqQFR2vFkdTmpSTfvBI2Q5/sKYs0BfRDyRoQCoVJ1hUrgOfqJ9ed+UL2fPh\nMcgjRlWppsPav7xc8uX