/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/salo368","id":122643656,"login":"salo368","node_id":"U_kgDOB09kyA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/fe6b8b77ba5bf7e0f0254db7ebcaee7a1dc2c413/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T11:02:30Z","email":"salomonsaenzg368@gmail.com","name":"salomon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T11:02:30Z","email":"salomonsaenzg368@gmail.com","name":"salomon"},"message":"fix(files+forms+processes): add bcrypt (auth module needs it) + wire real DEV api urls\n\nLambdas were failing at import time with ''No module named bcrypt'' because\nlibs/utils/auth.py imports bcrypt at top-level for hash_password/verify_password,\nand the 3 new services didn''t declare it in requirements.txt (only auth did).\n\nAlso plug the real HttpApi URLs of files/forms/processes (dev) that came out\nof the first deploy into environment.ts, replacing the placeholders.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"f721dc623feeb1c76288be0e571ae025ddad29f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/git/trees/f721dc623feeb1c76288be0e571ae025ddad29f4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/git/commits/fe6b8b77ba5bf7e0f0254db7ebcaee7a1dc2c413","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/122643656?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/salo368","id":122643656,"login":"salo368","node_id":"U_kgDOB09kyA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commit/fe6b8b77ba5bf7e0f0254db7ebcaee7a1dc2c413","node_id":"C_kwDOUiz2UtoAKGZlNmI4Yjc3YmE1YmY3ZTBmMDI1NGRiN2ViY2FlZTdhMWRjMmM0MTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commit/134a92926a364c6bb5feeb318bae5e5ac4db8521","sha":"134a92926a364c6bb5feeb318bae5e5ac4db8521","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/134a92926a364c6bb5feeb318bae5e5ac4db8521"}],"sha":"fe6b8b77ba5bf7e0f0254db7ebcaee7a1dc2c413","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/fe6b8b77ba5bf7e0f0254db7ebcaee7a1dc2c413"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/122643656?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/salo368","id":122643656,"login":"salo368","node_id":"U_kgDOB09kyA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/134a92926a364c6bb5feeb318bae5e5ac4db8521/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T10:44:58Z","email":"122643656+salo368@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Salomon Saenz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T10:44:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(processes+forms+files): CDT open flow + S3 uploads (#45)\n\nImplementa el flujo real de apertura de CDT guiado por el legacy MVP.\n\n## Backend\n- **Migracion** `20260921000000_processes_forms_files.sql`: crea\n`processes`, `files`, `forms`.\n- **ORM** `libs/orm/{processes,files,forms}.py` con upsert, list,\nregister_from_s3.\n- **Utils S3** `libs/core/s3.py`: `upload_from_bytes`, `presign_upload`,\n`presign_download`.\n- **services/files**: bucket privado `cdts-\\<stage\\>-files` con\nencryption + CORS + BlockPublicAccess. Endpoints `POST\n/files/upload-url` y `GET /files/{id}/download-url`. Worker `on_upload`\ndisparado por S3 ObjectCreated que registra el archivo en DB\n(idempotente por s3_key).\n- **services/forms**: `GET /forms/me` y `PUT /forms/me` (upsert unico\npor usuario, precarga el proximo proceso).\n- **services/processes**: `POST /processes`, `GET /processes`, `GET\n/processes/{id}`, `POST /processes/{id}/advance`. Gates por etapa: form\nrequiere `Forms` (se snapshotea en `form_snapshot`), documents requiere\nal menos un `declaracion_renta`. Firma y pago son mocks que solo avanzan\nal llamar advance.\n- **serverless-compose.yml**: registra `files`, `forms`, `processes`\n(dependen de `migrations`).\n\n## Frontend\n- **Servicios TS**: `processes.service.ts`, `forms.service.ts`,\n`files.service.ts`.\n- **Wizard** `/process/:id` con stepper de 5 etapas (Tus datos -\nDocumentos - Firma - Pago - Listo). Componentes `process-form` y\n`process-documents`. Firma y pago mockeados en UI.\n- **Simulador**: \"Abrir este CDT\" ahora crea el proceso y navega al\nwizard; si no auth guarda intent en localStorage y lo materializa\npost-login/register.\n- **/me**: reemplaza el placeholder por listado de procesos con tarjetas\n(logo, monto, tasa, etapa, interes estimado).\n\n## Notas\n- URLs de los 3 nuevos API Gateways quedan como placeholder en\n`environment.ts`/`.pro.ts` hasta que Actions haga el primer deploy y\nexpongan los outputs.\n- El worker `on_upload` esta cableado via `NotificationConfiguration` +\n`Lambda::Permission` explicitos en el `serverless.yml` para no depender\ndel custom resource de Serverless.\n- Firma y pago quedan como TODO: el gate actual solo requiere llamar\nadvance.\n\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"eb25020e6432acb432bff96a67f6b00a5d246dd4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/git/trees/eb25020e6432acb432bff96a67f6b00a5d246dd4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/git/commits/134a92926a364c6bb5feeb318bae5e5ac4db8521","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commit/134a92926a364c6bb5feeb318bae5e5ac4db8521","node_id":"C_kwDOUiz2UtoAKDEzNGE5MjkyNmEzNjRjNmJiNWZlZWIzMThiYWU1ZTVhYzRkYjg1MjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commit/ce65524adf79d502adb5e0aa88aa82f236e9972c","sha":"ce65524adf79d502adb5e0aa88aa82f236e9972c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/ce65524adf79d502adb5e0aa88aa82f236e9972c"}],"sha":"134a92926a364c6bb5feeb318bae5e5ac4db8521","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/134a92926a364c6bb5feeb318bae5e5ac4db8521"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/122643656?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/salo368","id":122643656,"login":"salo368","node_id":"U_kgDOB09kyA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/ce65524adf79d502adb5e0aa88aa82f236e9972c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T07:58:02Z","email":"122643656+salo368@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Salomon Saenz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T07:58:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(frontend): simulador de CDT (landing publico) + fix EA compuesto (#44)\n\n## Que trae\n\n### Frontend (bloque principal)\n\n- **Nuevo landing publico** en `/`: `SimulatorComponent` que consume\n`GET /banks` + `POST /banks/simulate` y renderiza el flujo del\nlegacy/mvp: hero oscuro con mesh gradient, glass card con rango de tasas\ndel mercado, controles flotantes (monto/plazo segmented/CTA), empty\nstate con icono, y grid de cards por banco con logo, tier badge,\nhighlights, tasa E.A., ganancia animada, total al final e inversion\nminima.\n- **Chrome global** (`AppComponent`): navbar sticky con brand + link\nSimulador + link Mi cuenta (si auth) + login/register o avatar+logout, y\nfooter con mesh gradient.\n- **`AnimatedMoneyComponent`** con conteo animado (easing cubico) para\nlas cifras de resultado.\n- **`BanksService`** para las 2 rutas HTTP.\n- **Rutas reorganizadas**:\n  - `/` \\u2192 simulador (publico, sin guard).\n- `/me` \\u2192 el `HomeComponent` que antes ocupaba `/` (dashboard\nprivado). Login y register redirigen ahora a `/me`.\n  - `/login`, `/register`, `/docs` sin cambios.\n- **Design system** portado del legacy a `styles.css` (paleta violeta\nprofundo + indigo + emerald para dinero; typo Plus Jakarta Sans via\nGoogle Fonts).\n- **Bootstrap 5.3 + Bootstrap Icons** agregados (`npm i bootstrap\nbootstrap-icons`, registrados en `angular.json` como estilos + JS\nbundle).\n- **`environment.{ts,pro.ts}` refactorizados** a `authApiUrl` +\n`banksApiUrl` (cada servicio backend tiene su propio HttpApi en API\nGateway; se colapsan a uno solo cuando pongamos custom domain).\n- dev: `banksApiUrl =\nhttps://elrpxpxr10.execute-api.us-east-1.amazonaws.com`.\n- pro: placeholder (`REPLACE-AT-FIRST-PRO-DEPLOY`) que hay que rellenar\ndespues del primer Deploy PRO del bloque banks; el output `HttpApiUrl`\ndel stack `cdts-pro-banks` da el valor.\n- **`angular.json`**: budgets aflojados (initial: 800kB warn / 1.5MB\nerr; anyComponentStyle: 6kB warn / 10kB err) porque Bootstrap +\nBootstrap Icons pesan y algunos componentes de docs excedian el default.\n\n### Backend\n\n- **`services/banks` simulate**: cambio del calculo de interes simple\nprorrateado (base 360) a **compuesto EA base 365** (`final = amount * (1\n+ rate/100) ^ (days / 365)`). Alineado con el calculo del legacy y\nmatematicamente correcto para EA.\n\n## Impacto en Actions\n\nPlan-deploy detectara cambios en:\n- `backend/services/banks/**` \\u2192 deploy solo del bloque `banks`.\n- `frontend/**` \\u2192 deploy del bloque `frontend` (build angular + s3\nsync + CF invalidation).\n\nSin cambios en migraciones ni en el bloque `assets`.\n\n## Notas de la funcionalidad ''Abrir este CDT''\n\nEl CTA de cada card llama a `openCdt(row)`:\n- Si NO hay sesion \\u2192 redirige a `/register` (fricción intencional\npara captar usuarios).\n- Si SI hay sesion \\u2192 va a `/me` como placeholder. La apertura real\nde CDTs es un feature futuro (requiere el dominio `cdts` en el backend\ncon crear/listar CDTs).\n\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"833456f7267e47016f6eaf9b0db99f6819851e14","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/git/trees/833456f7267e47016f6eaf9b0db99f6819851e14"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/git/commits/ce65524adf79d502adb5e0aa88aa82f236e9972c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commit/ce65524adf79d502adb5e0aa88aa82f236e9972c","node_id":"C_kwDOUiz2UtoAKGNlNjU1MjRhZGY3OWQ1MDJhZGI1ZTBhYTg4YWE4MmYyMzZlOTk3MmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commit/6d44ac10c1661510a0338c4beafc9e4c287aaa43","sha":"6d44ac10c1661510a0338c4beafc9e4c287aaa43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/6d44ac10c1661510a0338c4beafc9e4c287aaa43"}],"sha":"ce65524adf79d502adb5e0aa88aa82f236e9972c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/ce65524adf79d502adb5e0aa88aa82f236e9972c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/122643656?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/salo368","id":122643656,"login":"salo368","node_id":"U_kgDOB09kyA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/6d44ac10c1661510a0338c4beafc9e4c287aaa43/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T06:01:11Z","email":"122643656+salo368@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Salomon Saenz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T06:01:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(frontend): seccion escondida /docs con modelo PAREX (#42)\n\nSeccion escondida en el frontend para documentar el proyecto\n(metodologia PAREX + modelo de servicios de CDT).\n\n## Que trae\n\n- Ruta publica `/#/docs` (no linkeada en el UI, se llega solo por URL\ndirecta).\n- Contenido servido como assets JSON estaticos (`parex.json` 56 KB +\n`contexto.json` 8 KB) cargados bajo demanda: no engordan el bundle\ninicial.\n- 3 vistas navegables:\n- **Contexto**: ficha empresa, canvas, actores, capacidades, portafolio.\n- **Servicios de negocio**: catalogo (S01-S06) + detalle con escenarios\ny encadenamiento de casos de uso.\n- **Casos de uso**: catalogo (C01-C20) + detalle con steps atomicos y\nflujos tipados (FB / FA* / FE* / FX*).\n\n## Bundle impact\n\nChunks lazy nuevos, initial bundle sin cambios:\n\n```\ndocs-shell-component  |   3.00 kB\noverview-component    |   9.32 kB\nservices-component    |  12.87 kB\nuse-cases-component   |  12.41 kB\ndocs-routes           | 823 bytes\n```\n\nLos JSON viven en `frontend/public/assets/docs/` y se sirven directo por\nS3/CloudFront.\n\n## Datos iniciales\n\nExtraidos de `docs/Ingenieria de\nSoftware/servicios_negocio_compacto.md`:\n- 6 servicios (S01-S06)\n- S04 con 5 escenarios completos y sus 15 casos de uso encadenados\n- 20 casos de uso con todos los steps y flujos\n\nLos escenarios de S01/S02/S03/S05/S06 quedan como stub para iterar\ndespues.\n\n## Detalles tecnicos\n\n- Catch-all interno en `DOCS_ROUTES` (`{ path: ''**'', redirectTo: '''' }`)\npara que URLs rotas dentro de `/docs` no caigan en el `**` global (que\nva a `''''`, ruta protegida, y redirige a `/login`).\n- Breadcrumbs con path absoluto `/docs` en lugar de `..` (evita resolver\na rutas intermedias inexistentes).\n- Servicio `DocsService` con `shareReplay` para no re-descargar los JSON\nal navegar entre subrutas.\n- `tsconfig.json`: `rootDir` explicito para silenciar warning TS 5.x.\n\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"b6f00af9a0860d2f10c3356622e0415db22ffaf7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/git/trees/b6f00af9a0860d2f10c3356622e0415db22ffaf7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/git/commits/6d44ac10c1661510a0338c4beafc9e4c287aaa43","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commit/6d44ac10c1661510a0338c4beafc9e4c287aaa43","node_id":"C_kwDOUiz2UtoAKDZkNDRhYzEwYzE2NjE1MTBhMDMzOGM0YmVhZmM5ZTRjMjg3YWFhNDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commit/660be393012f1bf2effe62c67dba5b92685943c2","sha":"660be393012f1bf2effe62c67dba5b92685943c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/660be393012f1bf2effe62c67dba5b92685943c2"}],"sha":"6d44ac10c1661510a0338c4beafc9e4c287aaa43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/6d44ac10c1661510a0338c4beafc9e4c287aaa43"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/122643656?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/salo368","id":122643656,"login":"salo368","node_id":"U_kgDOB09kyA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/660be393012f1bf2effe62c67dba5b92685943c2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T04:36:15Z","email":"122643656+salo368@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Salomon Saenz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T04:36:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(frontend): auth UI (login, register, home protegido) (#39)\n\n* Promote develop -> main (base limpia + stages dev/pro) (#3)\n\n* docs(structure): definir estructura obligatoria del monorepo (#1)\n\n- docs/repo-structure.md: fuente unica de verdad (para humanos y IA).\n- .cursor/rules/repo-structure.mdc: rule con alwaysApply=true para que\n  Cursor aplique la convencion en cada turno.\n- CONTRIBUTING.md: link temprano a la doc de estructura.\n\nConvencion:\n- Un servicio = un dominio en services/<domain>/.\n- Estructura fija: serverless.yml, utils/, data/, src/{handlers,scheduled,workers}/.\n- Cada Lambda = una carpeta con handler.py + function.yml.\n- Todo kebab-case, prefijo AWS cdts-<service>-<stage>-<resource>.\n\nCo-authored-by: salo368 <salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* chore(structure): stages dev/pro, naming cdts-<stage>-<svc>-<fn>, dirs raiz config/utils/data (#2)\n\n- Rename workflow deploy-prod.yml -> deploy-pro.yml (stage=pro, env=pro).\n- Renombra scripts npm deploy:prod/remove:prod/print:prod a *:pro.\n- docs/repo-structure.md: reordena naming a cdts-<stage>-<svc>-<fn>, define\n  stages unicos dev/pro, agrega seccion 7 de dirs raiz (config/utils/data),\n  seccion 10 sobre BD Postgres (schemas dev/pro sin public), y anti-patrones\n  actualizados (rechazar ''prod'' y naming viejo).\n- .cursor/rules/repo-structure.mdc: mismos updates, para que Cursor los aplique\n  en cada turno via alwaysApply=true.\n- README.md: refleja stages dev/pro, deployer ''github-actions-pro-deployer'',\n  workflow deploy-pro.yml.\n- scripts/iam/README.md: usuario pro renombrado.\n- scripts/iam/github-actions-deploy-policy.json: simplifica la lista de roles\n  gestionables al unico prefijo cdts-* (los del MVP ya no existen).\n- Crea config/, utils/, data/ en la raiz cada uno con README explicando su\n  proposito y limites (referencia docs/repo-structure.md).\n\nCo-authored-by: salo368 <salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: salo368 <salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* chore(structure): backend/ split + doc del nuevo flujo (pro) (#6)\n\n* chore(structure): mover todo el backend a backend/ (#4)\n\nDelimita el area del backend en una sola carpeta. La raiz queda para infra de\nproyecto (workflows, .cursor rules, docs, scripts/iam, README, CONTRIBUTING) y\ndeja espacio limpio para un eventual frontend/ hermano.\n\nMovidos a backend/:\n- serverless-compose.yml\n- package.json, package-lock.json\n- requirements-dev.txt, pytest.ini\n- .nvmrc, .python-version\n- config/, utils/, data/  (cross-servicio dentro del backend)\n\nWorkflows actualizados con:\n- defaults.run.working-directory: backend\n- setup-node: cache-dependency-path: backend/package-lock.json\n- setup-python: cache-dependency-path: backend/requirements-dev.txt\n\nDocs y rule actualizados:\n- docs/repo-structure.md: nuevo layout, todos los paths con prefijo backend/,\n  seccion 4 nueva ''Layout del monorepo'', anti-patron nuevo ''archivos backend\n  fuera de backend/''.\n- .cursor/rules/repo-structure.mdc: mismos updates, sigue con alwaysApply=true.\n\nFixes menores:\n- CONTRIBUTING.md: dos referencias ''prod'' -> ''pro'' que quedaron sueltas.\n\nCo-authored-by: salo368 <salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs: nuevo flujo de branching (rama alimenta dev y pro en paralelo)\n\nDocumenta la regla: cada rama feature abre 2 PRs (uno a develop, otro a main\ndesde la misma rama). develop y main nunca se hablan entre si porque el squash\nmerge crea conflictos add/add al hacer develop->main tras un rename.\n\n- CONTRIBUTING.md: seccion ''Flujo de branching'' nueva con diagrama, paso a\n  paso y anti-patrones.\n- README.md: seccion ''Flujo de trabajo'' actualizada.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: salo368 <salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat(ci): deploy selectivo por bloques (#12)\n\nDeja de re-desplegar todo el backend en cada push. Agrupa el codigo en bloques\nindependientes (backend/services/<X>/ y backend/migrations/) y despliega solo\nlos afectados por el diff.\n\nComponentes:\n- scripts/ci/plan-deploy.sh: descubre bloques por arbol, decide plan a partir\n  del diff. Reglas: cambio dentro de un bloque -> solo ese; cambio en archivos\n  globales del backend (compose, config, utils, data, layers, deps) -> deploy\n  total; cambio solo fuera de backend/ -> nada. migrations primero, resto\n  alfabetico, secuencial (max-parallel: 1).\n\n- .github/workflows/deploy-dev.yml y deploy-pro.yml: refactorizados con dos\n  jobs (plan -> deploy matrix). Cada bloque del plan corre en su propio job\n  de la matriz. workflow_dispatch acepta input ''block'' para override manual\n  (''__all__'' para forzar todo).\n\n- .github/workflows/ci.yml: nuevo job ''plan-preview'' que corre el mismo script\n  en modo DRY_RUN=1 para mostrar en la PR que bloques se desplegarian.\n\n- backend/migrations/: carpeta reservada con README que fija la convencion:\n  archivos sql/YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_desc.sql con secciones ''-- +migrate up'' y\n  ''-- +migrate down'', aplicados por Lambda cdts-<stage>-migrations-apply,\n  trackeados en tabla schema_migrations. Sin runtime todavia.\n\n- docs/repo-structure.md: nueva seccion 14 ''Bloques de despliegue'' con\n  reglas, orden, override manual, preview y anti-patrones.\n\n- .cursor/rules/repo-structure.mdc: seccion resumida de bloques.\n\n- README.md: seccion ''Deploy selectivo por bloque''.\n\nTesteado localmente con 4 escenarios (solo un servicio, varios bloques,\ncambio global, cambio fuera de backend/). Comportamiento correcto.\n\nCo-authored-by: salo368 <salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat(migrations): linter que impide calificar schema en .sql (#14)\n\nLas migraciones nunca deben escribir ''dev.users'' o ''pro.users''; el schema\nlo fija la Lambda con SET LOCAL search_path TO <stage> al inicio de cada\ntransaccion, de modo que el MISMO .sql corre en dev y en pro sin cambios.\nSin esta regla, un descuido tipo ''CREATE TABLE dev.users'' en produccion\ncrearia tablas en el schema equivocado silenciosamente.\n\nCambios:\n- scripts/ci/lint-migrations.py: valida los .sql:\n  * Prohibe prefijos ''dev.'', ''pro.'', ''public.''.\n  * Prohibe SET search_path (responsabilidad de la Lambda).\n  * Prohibe CREATE SCHEMA y DROP SCHEMA (los schemas se crean fuera del\n    pipeline).\n  * Exige nombre YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_snake_case.sql.\n  * Exige presencia de ''-- +migrate up''.\n  * Es robusto contra falsos positivos: strippea strings literales y\n    comentarios antes de matchear.\n\n- .github/workflows/ci.yml: nuevo job ''Lint migrations'' que corre el linter\n  en cada PR (3 min timeout).\n\n- backend/migrations/README.md: seccion nueva ''Convencion de schema'' con\n  ejemplos correctos e incorrectos, y explicacion de por que la Lambda es\n  la unica que fija el search_path.\n\n- docs/repo-structure.md §11: bullet nuevo sobre la convencion de schema\n  en migraciones.\n\n- .cursor/rules/repo-structure.mdc: regla dura 9 nueva + anti-patrones\n  nuevos.\n\nTesteado localmente con 6 fixtures (1 valida + 5 con violaciones distintas).\nLos falsos positivos potenciales (schema mencionado en comentario y en\nstring literal) NO se dispararon.\n\nCo-authored-by: salo368 <salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* refactor(structure): split services/ (negocio) vs platform/ (infra) (#16)\n\nIntroduce la separacion explicita entre bloques de dominio de negocio y\nbloques de infraestructura runtime. Motivacion: la Lambda de migrations no\nes un dominio de negocio; forzarla en services/ rompe la regla ''un servicio\n= un dominio''. Un servicio catch-all ''infrastructure/'' seria un cajon de\nsastre que agrupa cosas sin ownership claro.\n\nNueva convencion:\n- backend/services/<X>/  = DOMINIO DE NEGOCIO\n- backend/platform/<X>/  = INFRAESTRUCTURA RUNTIME (una carpeta por\n  responsabilidad, sin catch-all monolitico)\n- Prohibido services -> platform imports y viceversa.\n- Lo cross-cutting reutilizable sigue en backend/layers/shared/.\n\nCambios:\n- git mv backend/migrations -> backend/platform/migrations\n- scripts/ci/plan-deploy.sh: reescrito. Ahora descubre bloques en dos\n  directorios (services/ y platform/). Nueva regla mas robusta: cualquier\n  archivo backend/ fuera de un bloque conocido dispara deploy TOTAL (antes\n  requeria lista explicita de archivos globales; ahora es ''closed by\n  default''). El comportamiento de la lista implicita cubre todo lo anterior\n  (compose, config, utils, data, layers, deps) mas cualquier archivo suelto\n  que agreguemos en el futuro.\n- scripts/ci/lint-migrations.py: SQL_DIR apunta a\n  backend/platform/migrations/sql.\n- backend/platform/migrations/README.md: encabezado explica que es un bloque\n  de platform (§5.2). Links relativos ajustados a la profundidad nueva.\n- docs/repo-structure.md: §5 reescrita (services vs platform), §6\n  generalizada a los dos tipos, §11 y §14 con paths actualizados.\n- .cursor/rules/repo-structure.mdc: reglas duras 4-6 reescritas para incluir\n  ambos tipos, seccion ''Bloques de despliegue'' actualizada, anti-patrones\n  nuevos (''servicio catch-all'', ''import cross-tipo''), plantillas usan\n  {services,platform}.\n- README.md: layout del monorepo con platform/.\n\nTesteado localmente con 6 escenarios cubriendo servicios, platform, mezcla,\nconfig (global), archivo suelto (nuevo caso captado por la regla), y\ncambios solo fuera de backend/. Todos correctos.\n\nCo-authored-by: salo368 <salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat(platform/migrations): implementar Lambda cdts-<stage>-migrations-apply (#20)\n\n* feat(platform/migrations): implementar Lambda cdts-<stage>-migrations-apply\n\nPrimer bloque runtime del proyecto post-cleanup. Publica una Lambda que\naplica los .sql versionados de sql/ contra el schema del stage en la BD.\n\nComponentes:\n- backend/platform/migrations/serverless.yml: servicio Serverless\n  (runtime python3.11, timeout 300s, fuera de VPC, IAM para leer SSM del\n  path /cdts/<stage>/db/*).\n- backend/platform/migrations/requirements.txt: pg8000==1.30.5 (driver\n  puro Python, sin binarios ni layer).\n- backend/platform/migrations/utils/db.py: helper para leer SSM y abrir\n  conexion pg8000 con SSL.\n- backend/platform/migrations/utils/parser.py: parser de archivos .sql\n  con secciones ''-- +migrate up'' / ''-- +migrate down''.\n- backend/platform/migrations/src/handlers/apply/handler.py: handler\n  principal. Crea schema_migrations si no existe (en el schema del\n  stage), enumera sql/*.sql en orden, aplica los pendientes cada uno en\n  su tx con SET LOCAL search_path TO <stage>, registra en la tabla.\n  Falla el batch al primer error.\n- backend/platform/migrations/src/handlers/apply/function.yml:\n  configuracion de la funcion (sin events, se invoca sync desde el\n  pipeline).\n- backend/platform/migrations/sql/20260918170000_bootstrap_pipeline_check.sql:\n  migracion de bootstrap que crea una tabla _pipeline_check con la fecha\n  y el current_schema() para validar end-to-end.\n- backend/tests/test_migrations_parser.py: 7 tests unitarios del parser.\n\nIntegracion con el pipeline:\n- backend/serverless-compose.yml: registra services.migrations ->\n  platform/migrations.\n- backend/package.json: agrega dev dep serverless-python-requirements\n  para empaquetar las deps Python en el bundle.\n- .github/workflows/deploy-dev.yml y deploy-pro.yml: cuando la matriz\n  procesa el bloque ''migrations'', despues del serverless-compose deploy\n  invocan sincronicamente ''aws lambda invoke --function-name\n  cdts-<stage>-migrations-apply'' y fallan el job si la Lambda devuelve\n  errorType.\n\nDecisiones tecnicas:\n- Fuera de VPC: la RDS es publicly accessible con SG 0.0.0.0/0:5432\n  (mala practica; TODO harden en el futuro con VPC endpoint o subnet\n  privada + VPC config en la Lambda).\n- pg8000 en vez de psycopg2-binary: cero binarios, cero problemas de\n  packaging cross-platform.\n- Invocacion sincrona con aws lambda invoke (no CloudFormation Custom\n  Resource): mas simple, mas transparente, mas facil de debuggear.\n- Migracion de bootstrap incluida: valida que la primera invocacion crea\n  tabla y registra version; se puede borrar mas adelante con otra\n  migracion cuando ya haya servicios reales.\n\nTesteado localmente: linter pasa (1 archivo sin violaciones), pytest\npasa (7/7), plan-deploy dry-run genera plan=[''migrations''].\n\n* fix(ci): reemplazar ''serverless-compose print'' por ''package''\n\n* fix(migrations): naming correcto en serverless.yml y function.yml\n\n- Elimina ''provider.naming.functionName'' (no existe en Serverless Framework).\n- Agrega ''provider.stackName'' para forzar CFN stack a cdts-<stage>-migrations.\n- Nombre de la Lambda se define explicito en function.yml con\n  ''name: cdts-${sls:stage}-migrations-apply''.\n- Usa ${sls:stage} y ${aws:region} (sintaxis moderna) en vez de ${self:...}.\n\n* fix(migrations): naming correcto en serverless.yml y function.yml\n\n* fix(migrations)+docs(rules): naming correcto + reglas naming interno vs AWS\n\n- serverless.yml: sacar provider.naming.functionName (no existe), agregar\n  provider.stackName, migrar a sintaxis moderna ${sls:stage}.\n- function.yml: declarar name: cdts-${sls:stage}-migrations-apply explicito\n  y handler: con slashes.\n- docs/repo-structure.md y .cursor/rules/repo-structure.mdc: nueva seccion\n  3.1 (naming interno Python vs AWS), 3.2 (httpApi v2 por default), ejemplo\n  completo actualizado, anti-patrones nuevos.\n\n* fix(ci): sintaxis correcta de serverless-compose para deploy por servicio\n\n''npx serverless-compose deploy --stage dev migrations'' interpreta ''deploy''\ncomo nombre de servicio (error ''Unknown service \"deploy\"'').\n\nSintaxis correcta segun docs de @serverless/compose:\n    npx serverless-compose <service>:<command> [flags]\n\nEjemplo:\n    npx serverless-compose migrations:deploy --stage dev --verbose\n\nAplicado a deploy-dev.yml y deploy-pro.yml.\n\n* fix(migrations): nombrar IAM role con prefix cdts- para matchear policy\n\nServerless por default nombra el role como <service>-<stage>-<region>-lambdaRole\n= ''migrations-dev-us-east-1-lambdaRole''. Ese nombre NO matchea el patron\n''arn:aws:iam::*:role/cdts-*'' de la policy de GitHub Actions, entonces el\ndeploy falla con:\n    User ... is not authorized to perform: iam:GetRole on resource:\n    role migrations-dev-us-east-1-lambdaRole\n\nFix: declarar ''provider.iam.role.name: cdts-${sls:stage}-migrations-lambda''\nen serverless.yml. El role sale con el nombre correcto y la policy lo\nacepta.\n\n* fix(migrations): desactivar slim en pythonRequirements\n\npg8000 depende de scramp, y scramp usa importlib.metadata en runtime\npara leer su propia version. Con ''slim: true'' el plugin borra los\ndirectorios *.dist-info y explota con:\n    No package metadata was found for scramp\n\nTrade-off: bundle un poco mas grande, pero funciona. Alternativa\ncorrecta (mas compleja) seria mantener slim=true y usar slimPatterns\npara preservar los *.dist-info; no vale la pena para migrations.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: salo368 <salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* chore(ci): move validate into deploy workflows; drop ci.yml [skip ci] (#26)\n\nNew pipeline:\n- PRs no longer trigger any workflow (no CI on push to feature branch).\n- Deploy DEV / Deploy PRO now start with a ''validate'' job (pytest,\n  lint-migrations, serverless-compose package). If validate fails, plan\n  and deploy do not run, AWS stays untouched.\n- ci.yml deleted.\n\ndevelop can now accept direct pushes (branch protection change to follow\nin a separate step). main still requires PR.\n\nCo-authored-by: salo368 <salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* chore(code): strip verbose comments, translate remaining to English (#27)\n\nApplies to backend/platform/migrations/**, backend/tests/**, backend/serverless-compose.yml, and scripts/ci/**. No behavior change.\n\nCo-authored-by: salo368 <salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat(frontend): Angular 18 SPA + S3/CloudFront/OAC + frontend block wiring (#28)\n\n* feat(frontend): Angular 18 SPA + S3/CloudFront infra + block wiring\n\n- Add frontend/ (Angular 18 scaffolding, minimal AppComponent showing stage\n  and build time). Configurations renamed development/production -> dev/pro.\n  Env files under src/environments (default = dev, fileReplacement to pro).\n- Add frontend/serverless.yml: S3 private bucket + CloudFront with OAC +\n  bucket policy scoped by aws:SourceArn. SPA fallback for 403/404 -> index.html.\n  Stack cdts-<stage>-frontend, bucket cdts-<stage>-frontend-web-<accountId>.\n- scripts/ci/plan-deploy.sh: support frontend as a single always-together\n  block; support PLATFORM_CONTENT_DIRS (content subdirs of platform blocks\n  that deploy only the block; anything else in a platform block triggers a\n  full backend redeploy). Deploy order: migrations -> alphabetical backend\n  -> frontend.\n- deploy-dev.yml + deploy-pro.yml: conditional steps for matrix.block ==\n  ''frontend'' (sls deploy -> ng build -> s3 sync -> CloudFront invalidation).\n- docs/repo-structure.md + .cursor/rules/repo-structure.mdc: document all\n  the above and the new Actions flow (0 workflows on feat/PRs).\n\n* chore(frontend): drop provider.runtime (no lambdas, cleared sls warning)\n\n* fix(frontend): explicit Content-Type per extension (aws s3 sync serves .js as text/plain on Windows)\n\n- Add scripts/ci/deploy-frontend.sh: upload each extension with aws s3 cp\n  --content-type + long Cache-Control on hashed assets, no-cache on index.html,\n  and a final --size-only sync for stale cleanup. Then CloudFront invalidation.\n- deploy-dev.yml and deploy-pro.yml call the script instead of the raw\n  aws s3 sync that would serve .js as text/plain and break the SPA.\n- docs/repo-structure.md \\u00a75.4 documents the reason and the script.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: salo368 <salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(frontend): npm install (not ci) + pin Node 18 via frontend/.nvmrc (#29)\n\nAngular 18''s lock file contains multiple chokidar/readdirp versions across\nthe tree. npm 10 in CI rejects it with ''lock file''s chokidar@4.0.3 does not\nsatisfy chokidar@3.6.0''. Two changes to make deploys reliable:\n\n- Use npm install --no-audit --no-fund --prefer-offline instead of npm ci\n  for the frontend step only (backend keeps npm ci).\n- Add frontend/.nvmrc pinned to Node 18 (same as local) so the workflow\n  matches the environment that generated the lock file.\n\nCo-authored-by: salo368 <salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(frontend): pin serverless@^3.40 as devDep (#31)\n\nDeploy PRO run 35411505066 failed with ''No version found for 3'': npx\nserverless in frontend/ had no local install so it fetched serverless@4\nfrom the registry, which is incompatible with frameworkVersion: ''3'' in\nfrontend/serverless.yml. Adding serverless@^3.40.0 as a frontend devDep\nkeeps the CLI at v3.\n\nCo-authored-by: salo368 <salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* perf(ci): skip Validate on frontend-only plans; skip sls deploy on src-only changes (#32)\n\n* fix(frontend): pin serverless@^3.40 as devDep\n\nDeploy PRO run 35411505066 failed with ''No version found for 3'': npx\nserverless in frontend/ had no local install so it fetched serverless@4\nfrom the registry, which is incompatible with frameworkVersion: ''3'' in\nfrontend/serverless.yml. Adding serverless@^3.40.0 as a frontend devDep\nkeeps the CLI at v3.\n\n* perf(ci): skip Validate on frontend-only plans; skip sls deploy on src-only changes\n\nTwo optimizations reducing typical frontend iteration time from ~1m30s to ~50s:\n\n1. Reorder jobs: plan runs first (no deps). Validate now needs plan and\n   runs only when needs.plan.outputs.backend_count != ''0''. Deploy needs\n   [plan, validate] and runs when validate is success or skipped. Saves\n   ~30s on pure-frontend plans (no pytest, no serverless-compose package).\n\n2. plan-deploy.sh exposes frontend_infra_changed=1 iff any file under\n   frontend/ (excluding src/) changed. The ''Deploy frontend infra'' step\n   in both workflows is gated on this flag, so content-only changes to\n   frontend/src/** skip the ~15s no-op sls deploy and go straight to\n   ng build + s3 sync + invalidation.\n\nAlso added PLAN_DEPLOY_TEST_CHANGED_FILES hook for unit-style testing of\nplan-deploy.sh classifier + outputs (used to validate this change locally\nacross 11 scenarios).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: salo368 <salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat(backend): auto-registro de Lambdas + function.yml minimal (#34)\n\nElimina el boilerplate repetitivo en cada function.yml. Antes cada Lambda\nrequeria declarar ''name: cdts-${sls:stage}-<service>-<function>'' y\n''handler: src/<tipo>/<folder>/handler.handler'' aunque son mecanicos y\nderivables de la convencion. Ahora se autogeneran.\n\nComponentes:\n\n- backend/utils/build-functions.js: helper compartido que escanea\n  src/{handlers,scheduled,workers}/*/function.yml, valida snake_case en\n  las carpetas y autoderiva name = cdts-<stage>-<service>-<folder-kebab>\n  y handler = src/<tipo>/<folder>/handler.handler. Hace merge con lo\n  declarado en cada function.yml; si estos declaran name: o handler:\n  explicitos, ganan (escape hatch para casos raros).\n\n- backend/<block>/functions.js: shim de 3 lineas por bloque que delega\n  al helper compartido pasando __dirname. Por ejemplo:\n      module.exports.build = require(''../../utils/build-functions'')(__dirname);\n\n- <block>/serverless.yml: cambia de enumerar cada Lambda a la unica\n  linea:\n      functions: ${file(./functions.js):build}\n\n- function.yml del dev: baja de 5 lineas (con name, handler, description,\n  memorySize, timeout) a solo lo especifico (events, memory/timeout\n  overrides, environment, layers, description opcional).\n\nPiloto aplicado a backend/platform/migrations. La Lambda AWS queda con\nexactamente el mismo nombre (cdts-<stage>-migrations-apply) y misma\nconfig; solo cambio COMO se declara. Validado con:\n\n  * node --test tests/build-functions.test.js       (12/12 pass)\n  * npx serverless-compose package --stage dev      (compila)\n  * npx serverless-compose package --stage pro      (stage dinamico)\n  * npx serverless-compose migrations:deploy --stage dev\n    -> cdts-dev-migrations-apply invocada OK, 768ms\n\nCI:\n- deploy-dev.yml + deploy-pro.yml: nuevo step ''Test JS helpers'' en el\n  job validate que corre node --test sobre tests/*.test.js.\n\nDocs:\n- docs/repo-structure.md: nueva seccion 8.1 documentando el helper, §3.1\n  reescrita (name/handler ya no se escriben), §10 con ejemplo actualizado,\n  §12 anti-patrones nuevos (''declarar name/handler sin razon'',\n  ''enumerar Lambdas manual'').\n- .cursor/rules/repo-structure.mdc: espejo, con regla dura nueva 8\n  sobre auto-registro y plantilla actualizada.\n\nCo-authored-by: salo368 <salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat(auth): promover servicio auth a pro (validado en dev, 11/11 smoke tests) (#38)\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* feat(frontend): auth UI (login, register, home protegido)\n\n- environments/environment{,pro}.ts: apiBaseUrl por stage.\n- core/auth.service.ts: signals user/token/isAuthenticated, persistencia\n  en localStorage, llamadas a /auth/{register,login,me,logout}.\n- core/auth.interceptor.ts: Authorization: Bearer, redirect a /login en 401.\n- core/auth.guard.ts: requireAuth y requireGuest.\n- pages/{login,register,home}.component.*: forms reactivos, CSS simple,\n  errores del backend visibles al usuario.\n- app.config.ts: provideRouter (hash location) + provideHttpClient con\n  interceptor.\n- app.routes.ts: 3 rutas lazy loaded, catch-all a home.\n\nBuild: 274 KB initial, 76 KB gzip. Sin dependencies nuevas.\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: salo368 <salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"a6f67b07740e704d389b93d9714a770861bb4fc9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/git/trees/a6f67b07740e704d389b93d9714a770861bb4fc9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/git/commits/660be393012f1bf2effe62c67dba5b92685943c2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commit/660be393012f1bf2effe62c67dba5b92685943c2","node_id":"C_kwDOUiz2UtoAKDY2MGJlMzkzMDEyZjFiZjJlZmZlNjJjNjdkYmE1YjkyNjg1OTQzYzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commit/e32c8119c3594faf68c2b10be3e87041a5512f98","sha":"e32c8119c3594faf68c2b10be3e87041a5512f98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/e32c8119c3594faf68c2b10be3e87041a5512f98"}],"sha":"660be393012f1bf2effe62c67dba5b92685943c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/660be393012f1bf2effe62c67dba5b92685943c2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/122643656?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/salo368","id":122643656,"login":"salo368","node_id":"U_kgDOB09kyA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/salo368","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/salo368/Software-Inge-frontend/commits/e32c8119c3594faf68c2b10be3e87041a5512f98/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T01:36:28Z","email":"122643656+salo368@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Salomon Saenz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T01:36:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: sync develop with main (frontend block + CI perf) (#33)\n\n* Promote develop -> main (base limpia + stages dev/pro) (#3)\n\n* docs(structure): definir estructura obligatoria del monorepo (#1)\n\n- docs/repo-structure.md: fuente unica de verdad (para humanos y IA).\n- .cursor/rules/repo-structure.mdc: rule con alwaysApply=true para que\n  Cursor aplique la convencion en cada turno.\n- CONTRIBUTING.md: link temprano a la doc de estructura.\n\nConvencion:\n- Un servicio = un dominio en services/<domain>/.\n- Estructura fija: serverless.yml, utils/, data/, src/{handlers,scheduled,workers}/.\n- Cada Lambda = una carpeta con handler.py + function.yml.\n- Todo kebab-case, prefijo AWS cdts-<service>-<stage>-<resource>.\n\nCo-authored-by: salo368 <salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* chore(structure): stages dev/pro, naming cdts-<stage>-<svc>-<fn>, dirs raiz config/utils/data (#2)\n\n- Rename workflow deploy-prod.yml -> deploy-pro.yml (stage=pro, env=pro).\n- Renombra scripts npm deploy:prod/remove:prod/print:prod a *:pro.\n- docs/repo-structure.md: reordena naming a cdts-<stage>-<svc>-<fn>, define\n  stages unicos dev/pro, agrega seccion 7 de dirs raiz (config/utils/data),\n  seccion 10 sobre BD Postgres (schemas dev/pro sin public), y anti-patrones\n  actualizados (rechazar ''prod'' y naming viejo).\n- .cursor/rules/repo-structure.mdc: mismos updates, para que Cursor los aplique\n  en cada turno via alwaysApply=true.\n- README.md: refleja stages dev/pro, deployer ''github-actions-pro-deployer'',\n  workflow deploy-pro.yml.\n- scripts/iam/README.md: usuario pro renombrado.\n- scripts/iam/github-actions-deploy-policy.json: simplifica la lista de roles\n  gestionables al unico prefijo cdts-* (los del MVP ya no existen).\n- Crea config/, utils/, data/ en la raiz cada uno con README explicando su\n  proposito y limites (referencia docs/repo-structure.md).\n\nCo-authored-by: salo368 <salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: salo368 <salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* chore(structure): backend/ split + doc del nuevo flujo (pro) (#6)\n\n* chore(structure): mover todo el backend a backend/ (#4)\n\nDelimita el area del backend en una sola carpeta. La raiz queda para infra de\nproyecto (workflows, .cursor rules, docs, scripts/iam, README, CONTRIBUTING) y\ndeja espacio limpio para un eventual frontend/ hermano.\n\nMovidos a backend/:\n- serverless-compose.yml\n- package.json, package-lock.json\n- requirements-dev.txt, pytest.ini\n- .nvmrc, .python-version\n- config/, utils/, data/  (cross-servicio dentro del backend)\n\nWorkflows actualizados con:\n- defaults.run.working-directory: backend\n- setup-node: cache-dependency-path: backend/package-lock.json\n- setup-python: cache-dependency-path: backend/requirements-dev.txt\n\nDocs y rule actualizados:\n- docs/repo-structure.md: nuevo layout, todos los paths con prefijo backend/,\n  seccion 4 nueva ''Layout del monorepo'', anti-patron nuevo ''archivos backend\n  fuera de backend/''.\n- .cursor/rules/repo-structure.mdc: mismos updates, sigue con alwaysApply=true.\n\nFixes menores:\n- CONTRIBUTING.md: dos referencias ''prod'' -> ''pro'' que quedaron sueltas.\n\nCo-authored-by: salo368 <salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs: nuevo flujo de branching (rama alimenta dev y pro en paralelo)\n\nDocumenta la regla: cada rama feature abre 2 PRs (uno a develop, otro a main\ndesde la misma rama). develop y main nunca se hablan entre si porque el squash\nmerge crea conflictos add/add al hacer develop->main tras un rename.\n\n- CONTRIBUTING.md: seccion ''Flujo de branching'' nueva con diagrama, paso a\n  paso y anti-patrones.\n- README.md: seccion ''Flujo de trabajo'' actualizada.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: salo368 <salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat(ci): deploy selectivo por bloques (#12)\n\nDeja de re-desplegar todo el backend en cada push. Agrupa el codigo en bloques\nindependientes (backend/services/<X>/ y backend/migrations/) y despliega solo\nlos afectados por el diff.\n\nComponentes:\n- scripts/ci/plan-deploy.sh: descubre bloques por arbol, decide plan a partir\n  del diff. Reglas: cambio dentro de un bloque -> solo ese; cambio en archivos\n  globales del backend (compose, config, utils, data, layers, deps) -> deploy\n  total; cambio solo fuera de backend/ -> nada. migrations primero, resto\n  alfabetico, secuencial (max-parallel: 1).\n\n- .github/workflows/deploy-dev.yml y deploy-pro.yml: refactorizados con dos\n  jobs (plan -> deploy matrix). Cada bloque del plan corre en su propio job\n  de la matriz. workflow_dispatch acepta input ''block'' para override manual\n  (''__all__'' para forzar todo).\n\n- .github/workflows/ci.yml: nuevo job ''plan-preview'' que corre el mismo script\n  en modo DRY_RUN=1 para mostrar en la PR que bloques se desplegarian.\n\n- backend/migrations/: carpeta reservada con README que fija la convencion:\n  archivos sql/YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_desc.sql con secciones ''-- +migrate up'' y\n  ''-- +migrate down'', aplicados por Lambda cdts-<stage>-migrations-apply,\n  trackeados en tabla schema_migrations. Sin runtime todavia.\n\n- docs/repo-structure.md: nueva seccion 14 ''Bloques de despliegue'' con\n  reglas, orden, override manual, preview y anti-patrones.\n\n- .cursor/rules/repo-structure.mdc: seccion resumida de bloques.\n\n- README.md: seccion ''Deploy selectivo por bloque''.\n\nTesteado localmente con 4 escenarios (solo un servicio, varios bloques,\ncambio global, cambio fuera de backend/). Comportamiento correcto.\n\nCo-authored-by: salo368 <salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat(migrations): linter que impide calificar schema en .sql (#14)\n\nLas migraciones nunca deben escribir ''dev.users'' o ''pro.users''; el schema\nlo fija la Lambda con SET LOCAL search_path TO <stage> al inicio de cada\ntransaccion, de modo que el MISMO .sql corre en dev y en pro sin cambios.\nSin esta regla, un descuido tipo ''CREATE TABLE dev.users'' en produccion\ncrearia tablas en el schema equivocado silenciosamente.\n\nCambios:\n- scripts/ci/lint-migrations.py: valida los .sql:\n  * Prohibe prefijos ''dev.'', ''pro.'', ''public.''.\n  * Prohibe SET search_path (responsabilidad de la Lambda).\n  * Prohibe CREATE SCHEMA y DROP SCHEMA (los schemas se crean fuera del\n    pipeline).\n  * Exige nombre YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_snake_case.sql.\n  * Exige presencia de ''-- +migrate up''.\n  * Es robusto contra falsos positivos: strippea strings literales y\n    comentarios antes de matchear.\n\n- .github/workflows/ci.yml: nuevo job ''Lint migrations'' que corre el linter\n  en cada PR (3 min timeout).\n\n- backend/migrations/README.md: seccion nueva ''Convencion de schema'' con\n  ejemplos correctos e incorrectos, y explicacion de por que la Lambda es\n  la unica que fija el search_path.\n\n- docs/repo-structure.md §11: bullet nuevo sobre la convencion de schema\n  en migraciones.\n\n- .cursor/rules/repo-structure.mdc: regla dura 9 nueva + anti-patrones\n  nuevos.\n\nTesteado localmente con 6 fixtures (1 valida + 5 con violaciones distintas).\nLos falsos positivos potenciales (schema mencionado en comentario y en\nstring literal) NO se dispararon.\n\nCo-authored-by: salo368 <salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* refactor(structure): split services/ (negocio) vs platform/ (infra) (#16)\n\nIntroduce la separacion explicita entre bloques de dominio de negocio y\nbloques de infraestructura runtime. Motivacion: la Lambda de migrations no\nes un dominio de negocio; forzarla en services/ rompe la regla ''un servicio\n= un dominio''. Un servicio catch-all ''infrastructure/'' seria un cajon de\nsastre que agrupa cosas sin ownership claro.\n\nNueva convencion:\n- backend/services/<X>/  = DOMINIO DE NEGOCIO\n- backend/platform/<X>/  = INFRAESTRUCTURA RUNTIME (una carpeta por\n  responsabilidad, sin catch-all monolitico)\n- Prohibido services -> platform imports y viceversa.\n- Lo cross-cutting reutilizable sigue en backend/layers/shared/.\n\nCambios:\n- git mv backend/migrations -> backend/platform/migrations\n- scripts/ci/plan-deploy.sh: reescrito. Ahora descubre bloques en dos\n  directorios (services/ y platform/). Nueva regla mas robusta: cualquier\n  archivo backend/ fuera de un bloque conocido dispara deploy TOTAL (antes\n  requeria lista explicita de archivos globales; ahora es ''closed by\n  default''). El comportamiento de la lista implicita cubre todo lo anterior\n  (compose, config, utils, data, layers, deps) mas cualquier archivo suelto\n  que agreguemos en el futuro.\n- scripts/ci/lint-migrations.py: SQL_DIR apunta a\n  backend/platform/migrations/sql.\n- backend/platform/migrations/README.md: encabezado explica que es un bloque\n  de platform (§5.2). Links relativos ajustados a la profundidad nueva.\n- docs/repo-structure.md: §5 reescrita (services vs platform), §6\n  generalizada a los dos tipos, §11 y §14 con paths actualizados.\n- .cursor/rules/repo-structure.mdc: reglas duras 4-6 reescritas para incluir\n  ambos tipos, seccion ''Bloques de despliegue'' actualizada, anti-patrones\n  nuevos (''servicio catch-all'', ''import cross-tipo''), plantillas usan\n  {services,platform}.\n- README.md: layout del monorepo con platform/.\n\nTesteado localmente con 6 escenarios cubriendo servicios, platform, mezcla,\nconfig (global), archivo suelto (nuevo caso captado por la regla), y\ncambios solo fuera de backend/. Todos correctos.\n\nCo-authored-by: salo368 <salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat(platform/migrations): implementar Lambda cdts-<stage>-migrations-apply (#20)\n\n* feat(platform/migrations): implementar Lambda cdts-<stage>-migrations-apply\n\nPrimer bloque runtime del proyecto post-cleanup. Publica una Lambda que\naplica los .sql versionados de sql/ contra el schema del stage en la BD.\n\nComponentes:\n- backend/platform/migrations/serverless.yml: servicio Serverless\n  (runtime python3.11, timeout 300s, fuera de VPC, IAM para leer SSM del\n  path /cdts/<stage>/db/*).\n- backend/platform/migrations/requirements.txt: pg8000==1.30.5 (driver\n  puro Python, sin binarios ni layer).\n- backend/platform/migrations/utils/db.py: helper para leer SSM y abrir\n  conexion pg8000 con SSL.\n- backend/platform/migrations/utils/parser.py: parser de archivos .sql\n  con secciones ''-- +migrate up'' / ''-- +migrate down''.\n- backend/platform/migrations/src/handlers/apply/handler.py: handler\n  principal. Crea schema_migrations si no existe (en el schema del\n  stage), enumera sql/*.sql en orden, aplica los pendientes cada uno en\n  su tx con SET LOCAL search_path TO <stage>, registra en la tabla.\n  Falla el batch al primer error.\n- backend/platform/migrations/src/handlers/apply/function.yml:\n  configuracion de la funcion (sin events, se invoca sync desde el\n  pipeline).\n- backend/platform/migrations/sql/20260918170000_bootstrap_pipeline_check.sql:\n  migracion de bootstrap que crea una tabla _pipeline_check con la fecha\n  y el current_schema() para validar end-to-end.\n- backend/tests/test_migrations_parser.py: 7 tests unitarios del parser.\n\nIntegracion con el pipeline:\n- backend/serverless-compose.yml: registra services.migrations ->\n  platform/migrations.\n- backend/package.json: agrega dev dep serverless-python-requirements\n  para empaquetar las deps Python en el bundle.\n- .github/workflows/deploy-dev.yml y deploy-pro.yml: cuando la matriz\n  procesa el bloque ''migrations'', despues del serverless-compose deploy\n  invocan sincronicamente ''aws lambda invoke --function-name\n  cdts-<stage>-migrations-apply'' y fallan el job si la Lambda devuelve\n  errorType.\n\nDecisiones tecnicas:\n- Fuera de VPC: la RDS es publicly accessible con SG 0.0.0.0/0:5432\n  (mala practica; TODO harden en el futuro con VPC endpoint o subnet\n  privada + VPC config en la Lambda).\n- pg8000 en vez de psycopg2-binary: cero binarios, cero problemas de\n  packaging cross-platform.\n- Invocacion sincrona con aws lambda invoke (no CloudFormation Custom\n  Resource): mas simple, mas transparente, mas facil de debuggear.\n- Migracion de bootstrap incluida: valida que la primera invocacion crea\n  tabla y registra version; se puede borrar mas adelante con otra\n  migracion cuando ya haya servicios reales.\n\nTesteado localmente: linter pasa (1 archivo sin violaciones), pytest\npasa (7/7), plan-deploy dry-run genera plan=[''migrations''].\n\n* fix(ci): reemplazar ''serverless-compose print'' por ''package''\n\n* fix(migrations): naming correcto en serverless.yml y function.yml\n\n- Elimina ''provider.naming.functionName'' (no existe en Serverless Framework).\n- Agrega ''provider.stackName'' para forzar CFN stack a cdts-<stage>-migrations.\n- Nombre de la Lambda se define explicito en function.yml con\n  ''name: cdts-${sls:stage}-migrations-apply''.\n- Usa ${sls:stage} y ${aws:region} (sintaxis moderna) en vez de ${self:...}.\n\n* fix(migrations): naming correcto en serverless.yml y function.yml\n\n* fix(migrations)+docs(rules): naming correcto + reglas naming interno vs AWS\n\n- serverless.yml: sacar provider.naming.functionName (no existe), agregar\n  provider.stackName, migrar a sintaxis moderna ${sls:stage}.\n- function.yml: declarar name: cdts-${sls:stage}-migrations-apply explicito\n  y handler: con slashes.\n- docs/repo-structure.md y .cursor/rules/repo-structure.mdc: nueva seccion\n  3.1 (naming interno Python vs AWS), 3.2 (httpApi v2 por default), ejemplo\n  completo actualizado, anti-patrones nuevos.\n\n* fix(ci): sintaxis correcta de serverless-compose para deploy por servicio\n\n''npx serverless-compose deploy --stage dev migrations'' interpreta ''deploy''\ncomo nombre de servicio (error ''Unknown service \"deploy\"'').\n\nSintaxis correcta segun docs de @serverless/compose:\n    npx serverless-compose <service>:<command> [flags]\n\nEjemplo:\n    npx serverless-compose migrations:deploy --stage dev --verbose\n\nAplicado a deploy-dev.yml y deploy-pro.yml.\n\n* fix(migrations): nombrar IAM role con prefix cdts- para matchear policy\n\nServerless por default nombra el role como <service>-<stage>-<region>-lambdaRole\n= ''migrations-dev-us-east-1-lambdaRole''. Ese nombre NO matchea el patron\n''arn:aws:iam::*:role/cdts-*'' de la policy de GitHub Actions, entonces el\ndeploy falla con:\n    User ... is not authorized to perform: iam:GetRole on resource:\n    role migrations-dev-us-east-1-lambdaRole\n\nFix: declarar ''provider.iam.role.name: cdts-${sls:stage}-migrations-lambda''\nen serverless.yml. El role sale con el nombre correcto y la policy lo\nacepta.\n\n* fix(migrations): desactivar slim en pythonRequirements\n\npg8000 depende de scramp, y scramp usa importlib.metadata en runtime\npara leer su propia version. Con ''slim: true'' el plugin borra los\ndirectorios *.dist-info y explota con:\n    No package metadata was found for scramp\n\nTrade-off: bundle un poco mas grande, pero funciona. Alternativa\ncorrecta (mas compleja) seria mantener slim=true y usar slimPatterns\npara preservar los *.dist-info; no vale la pena para migrations.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: salo368 <salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* chore(ci): move validate into deploy workflows; drop ci.yml [skip ci] (#26)\n\nNew pipeline:\n- PRs no longer trigger any workflow (no CI on push to feature branch).\n- Deploy DEV / Deploy PRO now start with a ''validate'' job (pytest,\n  lint-migrations, serverless-compose package). If validate fails, plan\n  and deploy do not run, AWS stays untouched.\n- ci.yml deleted.\n\ndevelop can now accept direct pushes (branch protection change to follow\nin a separate step). main still requires PR.\n\nCo-authored-by: salo368 <salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* chore(code): strip verbose comments, translate remaining to English (#27)\n\nApplies to backend/platform/migrations/**, backend/tests/**, backend/serverless-compose.yml, and scripts/ci/**. No behavior change.\n\nCo-authored-by: salo368 <salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat(frontend): Angular 18 SPA + S3/CloudFront/OAC + frontend block wiring (#28)\n\n* feat(frontend): Angular 18 SPA + S3/CloudFront infra + block wiring\n\n- Add frontend/ (Angular 18 scaffolding, minimal AppComponent showing stage\n  and build time). Configurations renamed development/production -> dev/pro.\n  Env files under src/environments (default = dev, fileReplacement to pro).\n- Add frontend/serverless.yml: S3 private bucket + CloudFront with OAC +\n  bucket policy scoped by aws:SourceArn. SPA fallback for 403/404 -> index.html.\n  Stack cdts-<stage>-frontend, bucket cdts-<stage>-frontend-web-<accountId>.\n- scripts/ci/plan-deploy.sh: support frontend as a single always-together\n  block; support PLATFORM_CONTENT_DIRS (content subdirs of platform blocks\n  that deploy only the block; anything else in a platform block triggers a\n  full backend redeploy). Deploy order: migrations -> alphabetical backend\n  -> frontend.\n- deploy-dev.yml + deploy-pro.yml: conditional steps for matrix.block ==\n  ''frontend'' (sls deploy -> ng build -> s3 sync -> CloudFront invalidation).\n- docs/repo-structure.md + .cursor/rules/repo-structure.mdc: document all\n  the above and the new Actions flow (0 workflows on feat/PRs).\n\n* chore(frontend): drop provider.runtime (no lambdas, cleared sls warning)\n\n* fix(frontend): explicit Content-Type per extension (aws s3 sync serves .js as text/plain on Windows)\n\n- Add scripts/ci/deploy-frontend.sh: upload each extension with aws s3 cp\n  --content-type + long Cache-Control on hashed assets, no-cache on index.html,\n  and a final --size-only sync for stale cleanup. Then CloudFront invalidation.\n- deploy-dev.yml and deploy-pro.yml call the script instead of the raw\n  aws s3 sync that would serve .js as text/plain and break the SPA.\n- docs/repo-structure.md \\u00a75.4 documents the reason and the script.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: salo368 <salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(frontend): npm install (not ci) + pin Node 18 via frontend/.nvmrc (#29)\n\nAngular 18''s lock file contains multiple chokidar/readdirp versions across\nthe tree. npm 10 in CI rejects it with ''lock file''s chokidar@4.0.3 does not\nsatisfy chokidar@3.6.0''. Two changes to make deploys reliable:\n\n- Use npm install --no-audit --no-fund --prefer-offline instead of npm ci\n  for the frontend step only (backend keeps npm ci).\n- Add frontend/.nvmrc pinned to Node 18 (same as local) so the workflow\n  matches the environment that generated the lock file.\n\nCo-authored-by: salo368 <salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(frontend): pin serverless@^3.40 as devDep (#31)\n\nDeploy PRO run 35411505066 failed with ''No version found for 3'': npx\nserverless in frontend/ had no local install so it fetched serverless@4\nfrom the registry, which is incompatible with frameworkVersion: ''3'' in\nfrontend/serverless.yml. Adding serverless@^3.40.0 as a frontend devDep\nkeeps the CLI at v3.\n\nCo-authored-by: salo368 <salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* perf(ci): skip Validate on frontend-only plans; skip sls deploy on src-only changes (#32)\n\n* fix(frontend): pin serverless@^3.40 as devDep\n\nDeploy PRO run 35411505066 failed with ''No version found for 3'': npx\nserverless in frontend/ had no local install so it fetched serverless@4\nfrom the registry, which is incompatible with frameworkVersion: ''3'' in\nfrontend/serverless.yml. Adding serverless@^3.40.0 as a frontend devDep\nkeeps the CLI at v3.\n\n* perf(ci): skip Validate on frontend-only plans; skip sls deploy on src-only changes\n\nTwo optimizations reducing typical frontend iteration time from ~1m30s to ~50s:\n\n1. Reorder jobs: plan runs first (no deps). Validate now needs plan and\n   runs only when needs.plan.outputs.backend_count != ''0''. Deploy needs\n   [plan, validate] and runs when validate is success or skipped. Saves\n   ~30s on pure-frontend plans (no pytest, no serverless-compose package).\n\n2. plan-deploy.sh exposes frontend_infra_changed=1 iff any file under\n   frontend/ (excluding src/) changed. The ''Deploy frontend infra'' step\n   in both workflows is gated on this flag, so content-only changes to\n   frontend/src/** skip the ~15s no-op sls deploy and go straight to\n   ng build + s3 sync + invalidation.\n\nAlso added PLAN_DEPLOY_TEST_CHANGED_FILES hook for unit-style testing of\nplan-deploy.sh classifier + outputs (used to validate this change locally\nacross 11 scenarios).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: salo368 <salo368@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: salo368 <salo368@users.