DQ6VXNlcjI5NzA5NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/commits/e2e4662c79d7595f82bc8d4c81845fabc24d491d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T19:46:17Z","email":"bryan.cash@programitcash.com","name":"Bryan Cash"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T19:46:17Z","email":"bryan.cash@programitcash.com","name":"Bryan Cash"},"message":"Break the three long functions into their parts: the graph''s nodes, the map read, the Scoreboard\n\nbuild_graph held six node closures in one 79-line function; the nodes are\nnow methods on a small Nodes class holding the dependencies, and\nbuild_graph is the wiring alone. week_map, at 48 lines, splits into the\npoints, the most-retrieved list and the assembly. Scoreboard, at 96\nlines, becomes a usePlays hook (the replay counter) and four\nsingle-purpose pieces — the yardage, the line, the field, the legend —\ncomposed by a twelve-line Scoreboard. Behaviour and tests unchanged.","tree":{"sha":"c37e2eb6521b2ef6a6c801390430d492658ddada","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/git/trees/c37e2eb6521b2ef6a6c801390430d492658ddada"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/git/commits/e2e4662c79d7595f82bc8d4c81845fabc24d491d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29709447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcas