tps://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/commits/d1d712e694da6df4d50a4bdd3950966d69a40613/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T10:17:27Z","email":"bryan.cash@programitcash.com","name":"Bryan Cash"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T10:17:27Z","email":"bryan.cash@programitcash.com","name":"Bryan Cash"},"message":"Draw the numbers as stencil digits; open the moods as a stack of color chips\n\ndigits.ts is a numeral set of its own: ten glyphs on a 100 × 140 grid built\nfrom circles and straight strokes of one weight, with a cut wherever two\nstrokes would meet — the Ø with its slash, the broken 2 and 4, dashed\ncircles for the 0, 6, 8 and 9 so a cut lands on a curve — plus a comma.\nStencilNumber sets a formatted count in them, one SVG per glyph, tabular by\nconstruction, with the gold offset painted as a second layer beneath.\nNumeral and the Scoreboard''s yardage now use it; Anton keeps the words.\n\nMoodChips is the mood legend as a modal: the seven moods dealt in one by\none as a stack of color chips over a 62% ink scrim, each chip a card in its\nmood''s gradient with the product name top-left and the gradient''s two hex\nstops as its code above the mood word bottom-left, text in ink or mist by\nthe chip''s luminance (contrast.ts). The chosen chip lifts and wears an ink\nring; Esc, the backdrop and the cross close it. MoodSwatch takes an onClick\nand becomes a text control; the Scoreboard''s swatches open the chips on\ntheir mood, as does the MoodSwatch plate. The scrim carries no blur: a\nbackdrop blur over the fixed grain layer mirrors the page in Chrome.\n\nThree words join the vocab (the product name, Moods, Close) as accessible\nnames. The Numeral plate shows all ten digits. Three new tests cover the\nchips, their highlight and close, and the luminance rule; DESIGN.md records\nthe chips, the stencil digits and the no-blur rule.","tree":{"sha":"ec4ba212f3a8c0a91e76d79cd8e84e3fa1f0e188","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/git/trees/ec4ba212f3a8c0a91e76d79cd8e84e3fa1f0e188"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/git/commits/d1d712e694da6df4d50a4bdd3950966d69a40613","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29709447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bcashofficial","id":29709447,"login":"bcashofficial","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NzA5NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/commit/d1d712e694da6df4d50a4bdd3950966d69a40613","node_id":"C_kwDOUi30JNoAKGQxZDcxMmU2OTRkYTZkZjRkNTBhNGJkZDM5NTA5NjZkNjlhNDA2MTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/commit/f5af2a91da90afeb6610e637ff71abb05d1daf8c","sha":"f5af2a91da90afeb6610e637ff71abb05d1daf8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/commits/f5af2a91da90afeb6610e637ff71abb05d1daf8c"}],"sha":"d1d712e694da6df4d50a4bdd3950966d69a40613","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/commits/d1d712e694da6df4d50a4bdd3950966d69a40613"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29709447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bcashofficial","id":29709447,"login":"bcashofficial","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NzA5NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/commits/f5af2a91da90afeb6610e637ff71abb05d1daf8c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T10:06:53Z","email":"bryan.cash@programitcash.com","name":"Bryan Cash"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T10:06:53Z","email":"bryan.cash@programitcash.com","name":"Bryan Cash"},"message":"Finish part 02 of the design system: Numeral, MoodSwatch, MoodMix, Scoreboard; PulseBar replays on hover\n\nPulseBar now plays again whenever the pointer enters it — the ticks rise\nin sequence and the chip rolls from zero — and a parent can replay it by\nchanging replayKey; useRollingNumber takes the same key and restarts from\nzero when it changes. A head prop renders the field alone for a parent that\ncarries its own word and yardage, with the meter then labelled directly. A\ncustom label (a handle, a subject) keeps its own case; only the mood word\nis set in tracked caps.\n\nNumeral: a count in Anton with the gold offset in three sizes, thousands\nseparated (format.ts), tabular, an optional caption in micro caps, and a\nroll to its value when asked. MoodSwatch: a gradient pill and the word;\non sets full ink and the gold underline. MoodMix: a set of voices'' hundred\nyards as one segmented pill, a segment per mood sized by its share in the\nmood''s gradient on the pulse track, described in words for assistive tech\n(describeMix in pulseMath). Scoreboard: controlled by the thread — resting\nand current readings; every change replays the large field in the new mood,\nrolls the digits, swaps the word and handle, and lights the matching swatch,\nwith the yard lines marked beneath in Anton.\n\nEach is a plate in the manual, the Scoreboard plate wired to four readings\nyou can hover; the manual''s figure labels are trimmed to bare words and the\nplanned specs lose their backticks. Seven new tests: thousands and captions,\nthe mix''s segments and its description, the swatch''s on state, and the\nscoreboard at rest and while playing a reading.","tree":{"sha":"47947100a05ab2d5957375b98bc7333caafc0f0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/git/trees/47947100a05ab2d5957375b98bc7333caafc0f0a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/git/commits/f5af2a91da90afeb6610e637ff71abb05d1daf8c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29709447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bcashofficial","id":29709447,"login":"bcashofficial","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NzA5NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/commit/f5af2a91da90afeb6610e637ff71abb05d1daf8c","node_id":"C_kwDOUi30JNoAKGY1YWYyYTkxZGE5MGFmZWI2NjEwZTYzN2ZmNzFhYmIwNWQxZGFmOGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/commit/bbc9ca92f0cda643d5f0760426796d8920a7f3bb","sha":"bbc9ca92f0cda643d5f0760426796d8920a7f3bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/commits/bbc9ca92f0cda643d5f0760426796d8920a7f3bb"}],"sha":"f5af2a91da90afeb6610e637ff71abb05d1daf8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/commits/f5af2a91da90afeb6610e637ff71abb05d1daf8c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29709447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bcashofficial","id":29709447,"login":"bcashofficial","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NzA5NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/commits/bbc9ca92f0cda643d5f0760426796d8920a7f3bb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T09:56:41Z","email":"bryan.cash@programitcash.com","name":"Bryan Cash"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T09:56:41Z","email":"bryan.cash@programitcash.com","name":"Bryan Cash"},"message":"Strip the manual''s copy and set the body face to Helvetica Neue\n\nThe manual now shows and does not explain: the plate glosses, the palette\nand grounds paragraphs, the typography rules, the motion and words notes,\nand the PulseBar and LaughSticker captions are gone, as is the catalog''s\ngloss field. A plate is its heading and its figures. Specimen lines in the\ntypography plate name only their scale step.\n\nThe body face is Helvetica Neue from the system; Archivo and its licence\nare removed from the bundle and fonts.ts mounts only Anton. tokens,\ncssVariables, DESIGN.md and the README follow.","tree":{"sha":"347f71d44bd856e8626d7a887131a08199625f8a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/git/trees/347f71d44bd856e8626d7a887131a08199625f8a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/git/commits/bbc9ca92f0cda643d5f0760426796d8920a7f3bb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29709447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bcashofficial","id":29709447,"login":"bcashofficial","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NzA5NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/commit/bbc9ca92f0cda643d5f0760426796d8920a7f3bb","node_id":"C_kwDOUi30JNoAKGJiYzljYTkyZjBjZGE2NDNkNWYwNzYwNDI2Nzk2ZDg5MjBhN2YzYmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/commit/1ded5e01565bc42c0a7c2793624b473b83693e5f","sha":"1ded5e01565bc42c0a7c2793624b473b83693e5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/commits/1ded5e01565bc42c0a7c2793624b473b83693e5f"}],"sha":"bbc9ca92f0cda643d5f0760426796d8920a7f3bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/commits/bbc9ca92f0cda643d5f0760426796d8920a7f3bb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29709447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bcashofficial","id":29709447,"login":"bcashofficial","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NzA5NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/commits/1ded5e01565bc42c0a7c2793624b473b83693e5f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T09:49:36Z","email":"bryan.cash@programitcash.com","name":"Bryan Cash"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T09:49:36Z","email":"bryan.cash@programitcash.com","name":"Bryan Cash"},"message":"Add the manual: the design system read as a book, on its own URL\n\nThe remote''s own URL now renders a manual instead of a smoke preview: a\nfixed index rail on the left listing every part and every plate, numbered\n(01.1 …), text only, the current plate in full ink with the gold underline;\nthe plate on the right as a lifted sheet with a running head (part ·\nnumber · Planned when it is), the name in Anton with the offset, and its\ngloss. The landing plate is the contents with a built-of-total count. The\nplate key rides the URL hash so a link lands on a plate.\n\nFive parts: Foundations (palette, typography, grounds, motion, words — all\nbuilt, rendered from the tokens and vocab themselves), The pulse (PulseBar\nand LaughSticker built; MoodMix, MoodSwatch, Scoreboard, Numeral planned),\nThe board (TextLink, Avatar, VoiceMessage, Pane, GroupTabs, SubjectRow),\nThe rail (PostCard, Masonry, StatusDot) and Chrome and the flyer (Masthead,\nFootball, SectionMenu, ThemeSwitch, Flyer, DoubleRule). A planned plate\nrenders the spec it will be built to — what it is, drawn from the approved\nboard sheet, and the props expected — so the whole system is visible before\nit exists and each primitive replaces its own spec when it lands.\n\nDecision recorded in README, CLAUDE.md and DESIGN.md: with one consumer the\nmanual on this URL is the playground; voices-fe links here rather than\nkeeping a second copy that would drift. Four tests cover the catalog''s\nkeys and numbering and the manual''s navigation and planned plates.","tree":{"sha":"8e16ee094aaab0597bb4036d45d085eac4256dc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/git/trees/8e16ee094aaab0597bb4036d45d085eac4256dc3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/git/commits/1ded5e01565bc42c0a7c2793624b473b83693e5f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29709447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bcashofficial","id":29709447,"login":"bcashofficial","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NzA5NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/commit/1ded5e01565bc42c0a7c2793624b473b83693e5f","node_id":"C_kwDOUi30JNoAKDFkZWQ1ZTAxNTY1YmM0MmMwYTdjMjc5MzYyNGI0NzNiODM2OTNlNWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/commit/2a304c9be59891791e112d2fba746188e27af687","sha":"2a304c9be59891791e112d2fba746188e27af687","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/commits/2a304c9be59891791e112d2fba746188e27af687"}],"sha":"1ded5e01565bc42c0a7c2793624b473b83693e5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/commits/1ded5e01565bc42c0a7c2793624b473b83693e5f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29709447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bcashofficial","id":29709447,"login":"bcashofficial","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NzA5NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/commits/2a304c9be59891791e112d2fba746188e27af687/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T09:44:05Z","email":"bryan.cash@programitcash.com","name":"Bryan Cash"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T09:44:05Z","email":"bryan.cash@programitcash.com","name":"Bryan Cash"},"message":"Add PulseBar: the reading as a 100-yard field of ticks, with the sticker\n\nThe first primitive, built to the segmented-tick reference in the platform''s\ncolors. Fifty thin ticks spread across the consumer''s width, two yards each,\nevery fifth taller for a ten-yard line; the filled run takes the mood''s\ngradient one tick at a time through color-mix, the rest sit in the line\ncolor. Above it a dot in the mood''s color, the mood word in micro caps, and\nthe yardage in a gold chip that rolls to its value through the new\nuseRollingNumber hook (420ms ease-out cubic, an instant jump under reduced\nmotion). It is a meter to assistive tech, named by its mood word.\n\nIt plays: on mount the ticks rise in sequence fourteen milliseconds apart;\nthe head tick breathes on the yard line; moving the cursor across the field\nraises a gaussian wave of ticks around it, written straight to the tick\nelements so no render is paid per pixel. All of it is off under reduced\nmotion. LaughSticker — the die-cut laughing face that marks a voice read as\nsarcasm — is its own primitive and sits at the end of the row.\n\nThe mood gradient stops moved from vocab.ts into tokens.moodStops, per\ntheme, because pale gold on a white ground vanished: Hyped now runs gold to\na deeper gold in light and gold to pale in dark, Level''s far stop deepens a\nstep in light, and Heated starts on whichever ink the theme has. vocab''s\nMOODS reference the --sv-mood-* variables, so every primitive paints\ncorrectly on either ground with no per-theme code.\n\nstyles.ts holds mountStyle (one <style> per primitive, mounted on first\nrender) and prefersReducedMotion; pulseMath.ts holds the pure tick\narithmetic so the component file exports only components. Six PulseBar\ntests cover the fill and head, the meter semantics, the sticker, the\nten-yard lines, clamping, and the gradient walk. The Preview renders one\nlarge bar and all seven moods; DESIGN.md section 5 now describes the tick\nanatomy and the per-theme stops.","tree":{"sha":"bb339763191e4488a576422e14a6f450592f4983","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/git/trees/bb339763191e4488a576422e14a6f450592f4983"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/git/commits/2a304c9be59891791e112d2fba746188e27af687","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29709447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bcashofficial","id":29709447,"login":"bcashofficial","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NzA5NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/commit/2a304c9be59891791e112d2fba746188e27af687","node_id":"C_kwDOUi30JNoAKDJhMzA0YzliZTU5ODkxNzkxZTExMmQyZmJhNzQ2MTg4ZTI3YWY2ODc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/commit/adf3247a57a9097d3c66f7a2d4a4ba6ee45581d6","sha":"adf3247a57a9097d3c66f7a2d4a4ba6ee45581d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/commits/adf3247a57a9097d3c66f7a2d4a4ba6ee45581d6"}],"sha":"2a304c9be59891791e112d2fba746188e27af687","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/commits/2a304c9be59891791e112d2fba746188e27af687"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29709447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bcashofficial","id":29709447,"login":"bcashofficial","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NzA5NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcashofficial","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/commits/adf3247a57a9097d3c66f7a2d4a4ba6ee45581d6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T09:33:47Z","email":"bryan.cash@programitcash.com","name":"Bryan Cash"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T09:33:47Z","email":"bryan.cash@programitcash.com","name":"Bryan Cash"},"message":"Serve the design system from compose so make dev shows it on :5301\n\nvoices-design-system gets a Dockerfile (node:22-slim, npm ci, the\ndevelopment-flavour build so a host on vite dev shares the same jsx runtime,\nvite preview on 5301) and a compose service; make dev prints the two URLs\nit brings up. The remote''s own URL renders the Preview — the masthead in\nAnton with the gold offset, the theme switch, the seven mood gradients on\nthe leather and grain grounds — and /assets/remoteEntry.js is what voices-fe\nwill load.","tree":{"sha":"a5359ef6c1c761e42ccfa4c9351d8c8b29353e8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/git/trees/a5359ef6c1c761e42ccfa4c9351d8c8b29353e8b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bcashofficial/steeler-voices/git/commits/adf3247a5